    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nACC means the Australian Crime Commission.\nACC Act means the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002.\naccess, in relation to a stored communication, has the meaning\ngiven by section 6AA. This definition does not apply to\nSchedule 1.\naccessible, in relation to a communication, has the meaning given\nby section 5H.\naccess request has the meaning given by subsection 107P(1).\nACMA means the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority.\nactivities prejudicial to security has the same meaning as it has in\nthe Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979.\naffidavit includes affirmation.\nAFP employee has the same meaning as in the Australian Federal\nPolice Act 1979.\nAFP Minister has the meaning given by section 100.1 of the\nCriminal Code.\nagency means:\n\n(a) except in Chapter 2—an interception agency or another\nenforcement agency; or\n\n(b) in Chapter 2—an interception agency.\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nACC means the Australian Crime Commission.\nACC Act means the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002.\naccess, in relation to a stored communication, has the meaning\ngiven by section 6AA. This definition does not apply to\nSchedule 1.\naccessible, in relation to a communication, has the meaning given\nby section 5H.\naccess request has the meaning given by subsection 107P(1).\nACMA means the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority.\nactivities prejudicial to security has the same meaning as it has in\nthe Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979.\naffidavit includes affirmation.\nAFP employee has the same meaning as in the Australian Federal\nPolice Act 1979.\nAFP Minister has the meaning given by section 100.1 of the\nCriminal Code.\nagency means:\n\n(a) except in Chapter 2—an interception agency or another\nenforcement agency; or\n\n(b) in Chapter 2—an interception agency.\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d980e40cc283b5bd025ef98d4f603e502b91457deb6f4b81285653e5f5f6289c",
      "skos:note": "Definitions and explanations of terms used in the Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nACC means the Australian Crime Commission.\nACC Act means the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002.\naccess, in relation to a stored communication, has the meaning\ngiven by section 6AA. This definition does not apply to\nSchedule 1.\naccessible, in relation to a communication, has the meaning given\nby section 5H.\naccess request has the meaning given by subsection 107P(1).\nACMA means the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority.\nactivities prejudicial to security has the same meaning as it has in\nthe Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979.\naffidavit includes affirmation.\nAFP employee has the same meaning as in the Australian Federal\nPolice Act 1979.\nAFP Minister has the meaning given by section 100.1 of the\nCriminal Code.\nagency means:\n\n(a) except in Chapter 2—an interception agency or another\nenforcement agency; or\n\n(b) in Chapter 2—an interception agency.\n\nChapter 1  Introduction"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5-norm",
