    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5AB Authorised officers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "Authorised officers of an enforcement agency\n\n(1) The head (however described) of an enforcement agency may, by\nwriting, authorise a management office or management position in\nthe enforcement agency for the purposes of subparagraph (b)(iii) of\nthe definition of authorised officer in subsection 5(1).\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 5AC\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nAuthorised officers of the Australian Federal Police\n\n(1A) The Commissioner of Police may authorise, in writing, a senior\nexecutive AFP employee who is a member of the Australian\nFederal Police to be an authorised officer.\n\n(2) A copy of an authorisation must be given to the Communications\nAccess Coordinator:\n\n(a) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1)—\nby the head of the enforcement agency; and\n\n(b) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1A)—\nby the Commissioner of Police.\nAuthorisations are not legislative instruments\n\n(3) An authorisation made under this section is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "Authorised officers of an enforcement agency\n\n(1) The head (however described) of an enforcement agency may, by\nwriting, authorise a management office or management position in\nthe enforcement agency for the purposes of subparagraph (b)(iii) of\nthe definition of authorised officer in subsection 5(1).\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 5AC\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nAuthorised officers of the Australian Federal Police\n\n(1A) The Commissioner of Police may authorise, in writing, a senior\nexecutive AFP employee who is a member of the Australian\nFederal Police to be an authorised officer.\n\n(2) A copy of an authorisation must be given to the Communications\nAccess Coordinator:\n\n(a) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1)—\nby the head of the enforcement agency; and\n\n(b) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1A)—\nby the Commissioner of Police.\nAuthorisations are not legislative instruments\n\n(3) An authorisation made under this section is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5ab-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fcc88bbafad3a5fb5ceb649b22e6206a70ca4a0a6ec1a01c5fb350f99b58effd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5ab",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5AB Authorised officers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "Authorised officers of an enforcement agency\n\n(1) The head (however described) of an enforcement agency may, by\nwriting, authorise a management office or management position in\nthe enforcement agency for the purposes of subparagraph (b)(iii) of\nthe definition of authorised officer in subsection 5(1).\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 5AC\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nAuthorised officers of the Australian Federal Police\n\n(1A) The Commissioner of Police may authorise, in writing, a senior\nexecutive AFP employee who is a member of the Australian\nFederal Police to be an authorised officer.\n\n(2) A copy of an authorisation must be given to the Communications\nAccess Coordinator:\n\n(a) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1)—\nby the head of the enforcement agency; and\n\n(b) in the case of an authorisation made under subsection (1A)—\nby the Commissioner of Police.\nAuthorisations are not legislative instruments\n\n(3) An authorisation made under this section is not a legislative\ninstrument."
    },
