    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5B Exempt proceedings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Act to an exempt proceeding is a reference to:\n\n(a) a proceeding by way of a prosecution for a prescribed\noffence; or\n\n(aa) a proceeding by way of review of a decision of the\nOrganisation to make an adverse security assessment (within\nthe meaning of Part IV of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979) or a qualified security assessment\n(within the meaning of that Part); or\n\n(ab) a proceeding by way of review of a decision of the ACC to\nmake an adverse criminal intelligence assessment (within the\nmeaning of Part III of the Australian Crime Commission Act\n2002); or\n\n(b) a proceeding for the confiscation or forfeiture of property, or\nfor the imposition of a pecuniary penalty, in connection with\nthe commission of a prescribed offence; or\n\n(ba) a proceeding under the Spam Act 2003; or\n\n(bb) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, Division 104 (control orders) or Division 105A\n(post-sentence orders) of the Criminal Code; or\n\n(bba) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, Division 395 of the Criminal Code\n(community safety orders); or\n\n(bc) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, a preventative detention order law, so far as the\nproceeding relates to a preventative detention order (within\nthe meaning of that law); or\n\n(bd) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, a post-sentence detention law or a\npost-sentence supervision law; or\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 5B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(be) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the main unexplained wealth provisions; or\n\n(bf) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the unexplained wealth legislation of a\nparticipating State, the Australian Capital Territory or the\nNorthern Territory; or\n\n(c) a proceeding for the taking of evidence pursuant to section 43\nof the Extradition Act 1988, in so far as the proceeding\nrelates to a prescribed offence; or\n\n(ca) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, an organised crime control law; or\n\n(d) a proceeding for the extradition of a person from a State or\nTerritory to another State or Territory, in so far as the\nproceeding relates to a prescribed offence; or\n\n(da) a proceeding by way of a coroner’s inquest if, in the opinion\nof the coroner, the event that is the subject of the inquest may\nhave resulted from the commission of a prescribed offence;\nor\n\n(e) a police disciplinary proceeding; or\n\n(ea) a proceeding in so far as it relates to:\n\n(i) a decision by the Commissioner of Police to terminate\nthe employment of an AFP employee or the\nappointment of a special member of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n\n(ii) a decision by the Commissioner of a Police Force of a\nState to terminate the appointment of an officer or\nmember of staff of that Police Force; or\n\n(eb) a proceeding in so far as it is, or relates to, disciplinary or\nlegal action (within the meaning of section 6S) that is in\nrelation to an eligible staff member (within the meaning of\nthat section) of the Australian Federal Police or the ACC; or\n\n(f) any other proceeding (not being a proceeding by way of a\nprosecution for an offence) in so far as it relates to alleged\nmisbehaviour, or alleged improper conduct, of an officer of\nthe Commonwealth or of a State; or\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A reference in this Act to an exempt proceeding is a reference to:\n\n(a) a proceeding by way of a prosecution for a prescribed\noffence; or\n\n(aa) a proceeding by way of review of a decision of the\nOrganisation to make an adverse security assessment (within\nthe meaning of Part IV of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979) or a qualified security assessment\n(within the meaning of that Part); or\n\n(ab) a proceeding by way of review of a decision of the ACC to\nmake an adverse criminal intelligence assessment (within the\nmeaning of Part III of the Australian Crime Commission Act\n2002); or\n\n(b) a proceeding for the confiscation or forfeiture of property, or\nfor the imposition of a pecuniary penalty, in connection with\nthe commission of a prescribed offence; or\n\n(ba) a proceeding under the Spam Act 2003; or\n\n(bb) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, Division 104 (control orders) or Division 105A\n(post-sentence orders) of the Criminal Code; or\n\n(bba) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, Division 395 of the Criminal Code\n(community safety orders); or\n\n(bc) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, a preventative detention order law, so far as the\nproceeding relates to a preventative detention order (within\nthe meaning of that law); or\n\n(bd) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, a post-sentence detention law or a\npost-sentence supervision law; or\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 5B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(be) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the main unexplained wealth provisions; or\n\n(bf) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the unexplained wealth legislation of a\nparticipating State, the Australian Capital Territory or the\nNorthern Territory; or\n\n(c) a proceedin",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "206351fd458b76ad6e53cd3d46fbfb6db8e97f484341970fc4b0f62b846f69e6",
      "skos:note": "Exempt proceedings defined"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5B Exempt proceedings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A reference in this Act to an exempt proceeding is a reference to:\n\n(a) a proceeding by way of a prosecution for a prescribed\noffence; or\n\n(aa) a proceeding by way of review of a decision of the\nOrganisation to make an adverse security assessment (within\nthe meaning of Part IV of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979) or a qualified security assessment\n(within the meaning of that Part); or\n\n(ab) a proceeding by way of review of a decision of the ACC to\nmake an adverse criminal intelligence assessment (within the\nmeaning of Part III of the Australian Crime Commission Act\n2002); or\n\n(b) a proceeding for the confiscation or forfeiture of property, or\nfor the imposition of a pecuniary penalty, in connection with\nthe commission of a prescribed offence; or\n\n(ba) a proceeding under the Spam Act 2003; or\n\n(bb) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, Division 104 (control orders) or Division 105A\n(post-sentence orders) of the Criminal Code; or\n\n(bba) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, Division 395 of the Criminal Code\n(community safety orders); or\n\n(bc) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, a preventative detention order law, so far as the\nproceeding relates to a preventative detention order (within\nthe meaning of that law); or\n\n(bd) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, a post-sentence detention law or a\npost-sentence supervision law; or\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 5B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(be) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the main unexplained wealth provisions; or\n\n(bf) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, the unexplained wealth legislation of a\nparticipating State, the Australian Capital Territory or the\nNorthern Territory; or\n\n(c) a proceeding for the taking of evidence pursuant to section 43\nof the Extradition Act 1988, in so far as the proceeding\nrelates to a prescribed offence; or\n\n(ca) a proceeding under, or a proceeding relating to a matter\narising under, an organised crime control law; or\n\n(d) a proceeding for the extradition of a person from a State or\nTerritory to another State or Territory, in so far as the\nproceeding relates to a prescribed offence; or\n\n(da) a proceeding by way of a coroner’s inquest if, in the opinion\nof the coroner, the event that is the subject of the inquest may\nhave resulted from the commission of a prescribed offence;\nor\n\n(e) a police disciplinary proceeding; or\n\n(ea) a proceeding in so far as it relates to:\n\n(i) a decision by the Commissioner of Police to terminate\nthe employment of an AFP employee or the\nappointment of a special member of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n\n(ii) a decision by the Commissioner of a Police Force of a\nState to terminate the appointment of an officer or\nmember of staff of that Police Force; or\n\n(eb) a proceeding in so far as it is, or relates to, disciplinary or\nlegal action (within the meaning of section 6S) that is in\nrelation to an eligible staff member (within the meaning of\nthat section) of the Australian Federal Police or the ACC; or\n\n(f) any other proceeding (not being a proceeding by way of a\nprosecution for an offence) in so far as it relates to alleged\nmisbehaviour, or alleged improper conduct, of an officer of\nthe Commonwealth or of a State; or\n\nChapter 1  Introduction"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5b-norm",
