    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5C Information or question relevant to inspection by Ombudsman",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, information or a question is relevant\nto an inspection under Part 2-7 or Chapter 4A of an agency’s\nrecords if the information or question is about:\n\n(a) in any case:\n\n(i) the location;\n\n(ii) the making, compilation or keeping; or\n\n(iii) the accuracy or completeness;\n\nof any of those records;\n\n(b) in any case—any matter to which any of those records\nrelates; or\n\n(c) if the Ombudsman suspects on reasonable grounds that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened this Act—any matter\nrelating to the suspected contravention.\n\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) limits the generality of a reference in this\nAct to information, or to a question, that is relevant to an\ninspection of an agency’s records.\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 5D\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, information or a question is relevant\nto an inspection under Part 2-7 or Chapter 4A of an agency’s\nrecords if the information or question is about:\n\n(a) in any case:\n\n(i) the location;\n\n(ii) the making, compilation or keeping; or\n\n(iii) the accuracy or completeness;\n\nof any of those records;\n\n(b) in any case—any matter to which any of those records\nrelates; or\n\n(c) if the Ombudsman suspects on reasonable grounds that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened this Act—any matter\nrelating to the suspected contravention.\n\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) limits the generality of a reference in this\nAct to information, or to a question, that is relevant to an\ninspection of an agency’s records.\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 5D\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
