    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5e-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5E(1) Serious contraventions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 88,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a serious contravention is a\ncontravention of a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\nthat:\n\n(a) is a serious offence; or\n\n(b) is an offence punishable:\n\n(i) by imprisonment for a period, or a maximum period, of\nat least 3 years; or\n\n(ii) if the offence is committed by an individual—by a fine,\nor a maximum fine, of at least 180 penalty units; or\n\n(iii) if the offence cannot be committed by an individual—\nby a fine, or a maximum fine, of at least 900 penalty\nunits; or\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 5F\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) could, if established, render the person committing the\ncontravention liable:\n\n(i) if the contravention were committed by an individual—\nto pay a pecuniary penalty of 180 penalty units or more,\nor to pay an amount that is the monetary equivalent of\n180 penalty units or more; or\n\n(ii) if the contravention cannot be committed by an\nindividual—to pay a pecuniary penalty of 900 penalty\nunits or more, or to pay an amount that is the monetary\nequivalent of 900 penalty units or more."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
