    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5E(3) Serious contraventions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5e-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "(3) To avoid doubt, a reference in this section to a number of penalty\nunits in relation to a contravention of a law of a State or a Territory\nincludes a reference to an amount of a fine or pecuniary penalty\nthat is equivalent, under section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914, to\nthat number of penalty units.\n5F  When a communication is passing over a telecommunications\nsystem\n\nFor the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1), a\ncommunication:\n\n(a) is taken to start passing over a telecommunications system\nwhen it is sent or transmitted by the person sending the\ncommunication; and\n\n(b) is taken to continue to pass over the system until it becomes\naccessible to the intended recipient of the communication.\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "skos:definition": "(3) To avoid doubt, a reference in this section to a number of penalty\nunits in relation to a contravention of a law of a State or a Territory\nincludes a reference to an amount of a fine or pecuniary penalty\nthat is equivalent, under section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914, to\nthat number of penalty units.\n5F  When a communication is passing over a telecommunications\nsystem\n\nFor the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1), a\ncommunication:\n\n(a) is taken to start passing over a telecommunications system\nwhen it is sent or transmitted by the person sending the\ncommunication; and\n\n(b) is taken to continue to pass over the system until it becomes\naccessible to the intended recipient of the communication.\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5e-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "268a36e6b37b08990b150f14171de005a245e7e68d70c66bf508834460033d9e",
      "skos:note": "Reference to penalty units includes reference to equivalent fine or pecuniary penalty amount."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5e-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5E(3) Serious contraventions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 88,
      "values:originalText": "(3) To avoid doubt, a reference in this section to a number of penalty\nunits in relation to a contravention of a law of a State or a Territory\nincludes a reference to an amount of a fine or pecuniary penalty\nthat is equivalent, under section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914, to\nthat number of penalty units.\n5F  When a communication is passing over a telecommunications\nsystem\n\nFor the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1), a\ncommunication:\n\n(a) is taken to start passing over a telecommunications system\nwhen it is sent or transmitted by the person sending the\ncommunication; and\n\n(b) is taken to continue to pass over the system until it becomes\naccessible to the intended recipient of the communication.\n\nChapter 1  Introduction"
    },
