    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5G The intended recipient of a communication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.90",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1), the intended\nrecipient of a communication is:\n\n(a) if the communication is addressed to an individual (either in\nthe individual’s own capacity or in the capacity of an\nemployee or agent of another person)—the individual; or\n\n(b) if the communication is addressed to a person who is not an\nindividual—the person; or\n\n(c) if the communication is not addressed to a person—the\nperson who has, or whose employee or agent has, control\nover the telecommunications service to which the\ncommunication is sent.\n5H  When a communication is accessible to the intended recipient\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, a communication is accessible to its\nintended recipient if it:\n\n(a) has been received by the telecommunications service\nprovided to the intended recipient; or\n\n(b) is under the control of the intended recipient; or\n\n(c) has been delivered to the telecommunications service\nprovided to the intended recipient.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not limit the circumstances in which a\ncommunication may be taken to be accessible to its intended\nrecipient for the purposes of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1), the intended\nrecipient of a communication is:\n\n(a) if the communication is addressed to an individual (either in\nthe individual’s own capacity or in the capacity of an\nemployee or agent of another person)—the individual; or\n\n(b) if the communication is addressed to a person who is not an\nindividual—the person; or\n\n(c) if the communication is not addressed to a person—the\nperson who has, or whose employee or agent has, control\nover the telecommunications service to which the\ncommunication is sent.\n5H  When a communication is accessible to the intended recipient\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, a communication is accessible to its\nintended recipient if it:\n\n(a) has been received by the telecommunications service\nprovided to the intended recipient; or\n\n(b) is under the control of the intended recipient; or\n\n(c) has been delivered to the telecommunications service\nprovided to the intended recipient.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not limit the circumstances in which a\ncommunication may be taken to be accessible to its intended\nrecipient for the purposes of this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-5g-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0846b31dc8fbb44133178f7f3e5e594ee3c2c721da65529684898d28fa9fda41"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-5g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5G The intended recipient of a communication",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 90,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1), the intended\nrecipient of a communication is:\n\n(a) if the communication is addressed to an individual (either in\nthe individual’s own capacity or in the capacity of an\nemployee or agent of another person)—the individual; or\n\n(b) if the communication is addressed to a person who is not an\nindividual—the person; or\n\n(c) if the communication is not addressed to a person—the\nperson who has, or whose employee or agent has, control\nover the telecommunications service to which the\ncommunication is sent.\n5H  When a communication is accessible to the intended recipient\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, a communication is accessible to its\nintended recipient if it:\n\n(a) has been received by the telecommunications service\nprovided to the intended recipient; or\n\n(b) is under the control of the intended recipient; or\n\n(c) has been delivered to the telecommunications service\nprovided to the intended recipient.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not limit the circumstances in which a\ncommunication may be taken to be accessible to its intended\nrecipient for the purposes of this Act."
    },
