        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\neligible Judge (except when used in Schedule 1) means a Judge:\n\n(a) in relation to whom a consent under subsection (2) and a\ndeclaration under subsection (3) are in force; and\n\n(b) in relation to a warrant applied for by the National\nAnti-Corruption Commission—who is a superior Court\nJudge.\nJudge means a person who is a Judge of a court created by the\nParliament.\n\n(2) A Judge may by writing consent to be nominated by the\nAttorney-General under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The Attorney-General may by writing declare Judges in relation to\nwhom consents are in force under subsection (2) to be eligible\nJudges for the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1).\n\n(4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of\na function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this Act\n(other than Schedule 1), the same protection and immunity as a\nJustice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High\nCourt.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\neligible Judge (except when used in Schedule 1) means a Judge:\n\n(a) in relation to whom a consent under subsection (2) and a\ndeclaration under subsection (3) are in force; and\n\n(b) in relation to a warrant applied for by the National\nAnti-Corruption Commission—who is a superior Court\nJudge.\nJudge means a person who is a Judge of a court created by the\nParliament.\n\n(2) A Judge may by writing consent to be nominated by the\nAttorney-General under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The Attorney-General may by writing declare Judges in relation to\nwhom consents are in force under subsection (2) to be eligible\nJudges for the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1).\n\n(4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of\na function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this Act\n(other than Schedule 1), the same protection and immunity as a\nJustice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High\nCourt.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6d-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6d-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "27915d2515c571d25af2d2a58f8525693a44cbae4a8bc59150de652a1e3f647c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6D Judges",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\neligible Judge (except when used in Schedule 1) means a Judge:\n\n(a) in relation to whom a consent under subsection (2) and a\ndeclaration under subsection (3) are in force; and\n\n(b) in relation to a warrant applied for by the National\nAnti-Corruption Commission—who is a superior Court\nJudge.\nJudge means a person who is a Judge of a court created by the\nParliament.\n\n(2) A Judge may by writing consent to be nominated by the\nAttorney-General under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The Attorney-General may by writing declare Judges in relation to\nwhom consents are in force under subsection (2) to be eligible\nJudges for the purposes of this Act (other than Schedule 1).\n\n(4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of\na function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this Act\n(other than Schedule 1), the same protection and immunity as a\nJustice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High\nCourt."
    },
