    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6db",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6DB Issuing authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6db"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.97",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, appoint as an issuing\nauthority:\n\n(a) a person who is:\n\n(i) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(iii) a magistrate;\n\nand in relation to whom a consent under subsection (2) is in\nforce; or\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) holds an appointment to the Administrative Review\nTribunal as Deputy President, senior member or general\nmember; and\n\n(ii) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of a federal court or of\nthe Supreme Court of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(iii) has been enrolled for at least 5 years.\n\n(2) A person who is:\n\n(a) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(c) a magistrate;\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, appoint as an issuing\nauthority:\n\n(a) a person who is:\n\n(i) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(iii) a magistrate;\n\nand in relation to whom a consent under subsection (2) is in\nforce; or\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) holds an appointment to the Administrative Review\nTribunal as Deputy President, senior member or general\nmember; and\n\n(ii) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of a federal court or of\nthe Supreme Court of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(iii) has been enrolled for at least 5 years.\n\n(2) A person who is:\n\n(a) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(c) a magistrate;\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6db-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6db-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "13fa03c0c7888297abaa9c2cbf5f0f201ad051309acbcfd57c86e563f6cb8425"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6db",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6DB Issuing authorities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 97,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by writing, appoint as an issuing\nauthority:\n\n(a) a person who is:\n\n(i) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(iii) a magistrate;\n\nand in relation to whom a consent under subsection (2) is in\nforce; or\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) holds an appointment to the Administrative Review\nTribunal as Deputy President, senior member or general\nmember; and\n\n(ii) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of a federal court or of\nthe Supreme Court of a State or a Territory; and\n\n(iii) has been enrolled for at least 5 years.\n\n(2) A person who is:\n\n(a) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or\n\n(c) a magistrate;\n\nChapter 1  Introduction"
    },
