    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6E Lawfully intercepted information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.99",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsections (2), (2A) and (3), a reference in this Act to\nlawfully intercepted information is a reference to information\nobtained (whether before or after the commencement of this\nsection) by intercepting, otherwise than in contravention of\nsubsection 7(1), a communication passing over a\ntelecommunications system.\n\n(2) A reference in this Act to lawfully intercepted information that was\noriginally obtained by an agency, or by an eligible authority of a\nState, is a reference to:\n\n(a) information obtained, whether before or after the\ncommencement of this section, by intercepting a\ncommunication under a warrant issued to the agency or\nauthority; or\n\n(b) information communicated to the agency or authority in\naccordance with section 65A or 63E.\n\n(2A) A reference in this Act to lawfully intercepted information includes\na reference to information obtained by accessing a stored\ncommunication under a section 31A authorisation.\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsections (2), (2A) and (3), a reference in this Act to\nlawfully intercepted information is a reference to information\nobtained (whether before or after the commencement of this\nsection) by intercepting, otherwise than in contravention of\nsubsection 7(1), a communication passing over a\ntelecommunications system.\n\n(2) A reference in this Act to lawfully intercepted information that was\noriginally obtained by an agency, or by an eligible authority of a\nState, is a reference to:\n\n(a) information obtained, whether before or after the\ncommencement of this section, by intercepting a\ncommunication under a warrant issued to the agency or\nauthority; or\n\n(b) information communicated to the agency or authority in\naccordance with section 65A or 63E.\n\n(2A) A reference in this Act to lawfully intercepted information includes\na reference to information obtained by accessing a stored\ncommunication under a section 31A authorisation.\n\nChapter 1  Introduction",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6e-ss-2a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0b39a54d649ab4c449c91f154e18af79d7c94fd9052a544120cf5725f6fade0b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6E Lawfully intercepted information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 99,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsections (2), (2A) and (3), a reference in this Act to\nlawfully intercepted information is a reference to information\nobtained (whether before or after the commencement of this\nsection) by intercepting, otherwise than in contravention of\nsubsection 7(1), a communication passing over a\ntelecommunications system.\n\n(2) A reference in this Act to lawfully intercepted information that was\noriginally obtained by an agency, or by an eligible authority of a\nState, is a reference to:\n\n(a) information obtained, whether before or after the\ncommencement of this section, by intercepting a\ncommunication under a warrant issued to the agency or\nauthority; or\n\n(b) information communicated to the agency or authority in\naccordance with section 65A or 63E.\n\n(2A) A reference in this Act to lawfully intercepted information includes\na reference to information obtained by accessing a stored\ncommunication under a section 31A authorisation.\n\nChapter 1  Introduction"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6e-ss-1",
