      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.99",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsections (2), (2A) and (3), a reference in this Act to\nlawfully intercepted information is a reference to information\nobtained (whether before or after the commencement of this\nsection) by intercepting, otherwise than in contravention of\nsubsection 7(1), a communication passing over a\ntelecommunications system.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsections (2), (2A) and (3), a reference in this Act to\nlawfully intercepted information is a reference to information\nobtained (whether before or after the commencement of this\nsection) by intercepting, otherwise than in contravention of\nsubsection 7(1), a communication passing over a\ntelecommunications system.",
      "values:partOf": {
