    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6ea",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6EA Interception warrant information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6ea"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "A reference in this Act to interception warrant information is a\nreference to:\n\n(a) information about any of the following:\n\n(i) an application for an interception warrant;\n\n(ii) the issue of an interception warrant;\n\n(iii) the existence or non-existence of an interception\nwarrant;\n\n(iv) the expiry of an interception warrant; or\n\n(b) any other information that is likely to enable the\nidentification of:\n\n(i) the telecommunications service to which an interception\nwarrant relates; or\n\n(ii) a person specified in an interception warrant as a person\nusing or likely to use the telecommunications service to\nwhich the warrant relates.\n6EAA  Preservation notice information\n\nA reference in this Act to preservation notice information is a\nreference to:\n\n(a) information about any of the following:\n\n(i) the giving of a preservation notice;\n\n(ii) for a foreign preservation notice—the making of a\nrequest under section 107P to preserve stored\ncommunications covered by the notice;\n\n(iii) the existence or non-existence of a preservation notice;\n\n(iv) the expiry of a preservation notice; or\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 6EB\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) any other information that is likely to enable the\nidentification of:\n\n(i) the person or telecommunications service specified in a\npreservation notice; or\n\n(ii) the person or telecommunications service to which a\npreservation notice relates.",
      "skos:definition": "A reference in this Act to interception warrant information is a\nreference to:\n\n(a) information about any of the following:\n\n(i) an application for an interception warrant;\n\n(ii) the issue of an interception warrant;\n\n(iii) the existence or non-existence of an interception\nwarrant;\n\n(iv) the expiry of an interception warrant; or\n\n(b) any other information that is likely to enable the\nidentification of:\n\n(i) the telecommunications service to which an interception\nwarrant relates; or\n\n(ii) a person specified in an interception warrant as a person\nusing or likely to use the telecommunications service to\nwhich the warrant relates.\n6EAA  Preservation notice information\n\nA reference in this Act to preservation notice information is a\nreference to:\n\n(a) information about any of the following:\n\n(i) the giving of a preservation notice;\n\n(ii) for a foreign preservation notice—the making of a\nrequest under section 107P to preserve stored\ncommunications covered by the notice;\n\n(iii) the existence or non-existence of a preservation notice;\n\n(iv) the expiry of a preservation notice; or\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 6EB\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) any other information that is likely to enable the\nidentification of:\n\n(i) the person or telecommunications service specified in a\npreservation notice; or\n\n(ii) the person or telecommunications service to which a\npreservation notice relates.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6ea-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6ea-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "72420e5ab47346999758f8d11ce56037ec5a68c6e6fb696b79667d89dc9ad547",
      "skos:note": "Reference to interception warrant information includes details about applications, warrants, and their existence/non-existence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6ea",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6EA Interception warrant information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "A reference in this Act to interception warrant information is a\nreference to:\n\n(a) information about any of the following:\n\n(i) an application for an interception warrant;\n\n(ii) the issue of an interception warrant;\n\n(iii) the existence or non-existence of an interception\nwarrant;\n\n(iv) the expiry of an interception warrant; or\n\n(b) any other information that is likely to enable the\nidentification of:\n\n(i) the telecommunications service to which an interception\nwarrant relates; or\n\n(ii) a person specified in an interception warrant as a person\nusing or likely to use the telecommunications service to\nwhich the warrant relates.\n6EAA  Preservation notice information\n\nA reference in this Act to preservation notice information is a\nreference to:\n\n(a) information about any of the following:\n\n(i) the giving of a preservation notice;\n\n(ii) for a foreign preservation notice—the making of a\nrequest under section 107P to preserve stored\ncommunications covered by the notice;\n\n(iii) the existence or non-existence of a preservation notice;\n\n(iv) the expiry of a preservation notice; or\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 6EB\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) any other information that is likely to enable the\nidentification of:\n\n(i) the person or telecommunications service specified in a\npreservation notice; or\n\n(ii) the person or telecommunications service to which a\npreservation notice relates."
    },
