      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.102",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A reference in this Act to an officer of a Territory includes a\nreference to:\n\n(a) a person holding, or acting in, an office (including a judicial\noffice) or appointment, or employed, under a law of the\nTerritory; and\n\n(b) a person who is, or is a member of, an authority or body\nestablished for a public purpose by or under a law of the\nTerritory, or is an officer or employee of such an authority or\nbody.\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 6H\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A reference in this Act to an officer of a Territory includes a\nreference to:\n\n(a) a person holding, or acting in, an office (including a judicial\noffice) or appointment, or employed, under a law of the\nTerritory; and\n\n(b) a person who is, or is a member of, an authority or body\nestablished for a public purpose by or under a law of the\nTerritory, or is an officer or employee of such an authority or\nbody.\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 6H\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
