    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6r",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6R Communications Access Coordinator",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6r"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Act:\nCommunications Access Coordinator means:\n\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 6S\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) if a person or body is covered by an instrument made under\nsubsection (2)—that person or body.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify one or more\npersons or bodies, or one or more classes of persons or bodies, for\nthe purposes of paragraph (b) of the definition of Communications\nAccess Coordinator in subsection (1).\n\n(2A) The Minister must only specify a person or class of persons in an\ninstrument made under subsection (2) if the person is an APS\nemployee, or the class of persons consists wholly of APS\nemployees, in the Department.\nInstrument must specify certain functions or powers\n\n(2B) An instrument made under subsection (2) must specify the\nfunctions or powers of a Communications Access Coordinator\nunder this Act or any other Act that a person or body, or a class of\npersons or bodies, specified in the instrument may perform or\nexercise.\n\n(2C) A person or body, or a class of persons or bodies, specified in an\ninstrument made under subsection (2) may only perform the\nfunctions or exercise the powers specified in that instrument in\nrelation to that person or body, or class of persons or bodies.\n\n(3) Unless the context otherwise requires, an act done by or in relation\nto a Communications Access Coordinator is taken to be an act\ndone by or in relation to the Coordinator on behalf of all the\ninterception agencies and all the enforcement agencies.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Act:\nCommunications Access Coordinator means:\n\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n\nIntroduction  Chapter 1\nInterpretation  Part 1-2\n\nSection 6S\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) if a person or body is covered by an instrument made under\nsubsection (2)—that person or body.\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, specify one or more\npersons or bodies, or one or more classes of persons or bodies, for\nthe purposes of paragraph (b) of the definition of Communications\nAccess Coordinator in subsection (1).\n\n(2A) The Minister must only specify a person or class of persons in an\ninstrument made under subsection (2) if the person is an APS\nemployee, or the class of persons consists wholly of APS\nemployees, in the Department.\nInstrument must specify certain functions or powers\n\n(2B) An instrument made under subsection (2) must specify the\nfunctions or powers of a Communications Access Coordinator\nunder this Act or any other Act that a person or body, or a class of\npersons or bodies, specified in the instrument may perform or\nexercise.\n\n(2C) A person or body, or a class of persons or bodies, specified in an\ninstrument made under subsection (2) may only perform the\nfunctions or exercise the powers specified in that instrument in\nrelation to that person or body, or class of persons or bodies.\n\n(3) Unless the context otherwise requires, an act done by or in relation\nto a Communications Access Coordinator is taken to be an act\ndone by or in relation to the Coordinator on behalf of all the\ninterception agencies and all the enforcement agencies.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6r-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6r-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6r-ss-2a"
        },
        {
