    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6u",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6U Succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6u"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If 2 or more successive control orders are made in relation to the\nsame person, each later control order is a succeeding Part 5.3\nsupervisory order in relation to each earlier control order.\nNote:\nIf an interim control order is confirmed, the confirmed control order is\na succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to the interim\ncontrol order (see the definition of control order in section 5).\n\n(2) If an interim supervision order is made in relation to a person, any\nlater extended supervision order in relation to the person is a\nsucceeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to an earlier\ninterim supervision order.\n\n(3) If 2 or more successive extended supervision orders or interim\nsupervision orders are made in relation to the same person, each\nlater extended supervision order or interim supervision order is a\nsucceeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to each earlier\nextended supervision order or interim supervision order.\n6UA  When a community safety supervision order is taken to be in\nforce\n\nFor the purposes of this Act, a community safety supervision order\nis taken to be in force in relation to a person if the order has been\nmade but the period specified in the order under\nparagraph 395.13(5)(d) of the Criminal Code has not yet begun.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If 2 or more successive control orders are made in relation to the\nsame person, each later control order is a succeeding Part 5.3\nsupervisory order in relation to each earlier control order.\nNote:\nIf an interim control order is confirmed, the confirmed control order is\na succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to the interim\ncontrol order (see the definition of control order in section 5).\n\n(2) If an interim supervision order is made in relation to a person, any\nlater extended supervision order in relation to the person is a\nsucceeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to an earlier\ninterim supervision order.\n\n(3) If 2 or more successive extended supervision orders or interim\nsupervision orders are made in relation to the same person, each\nlater extended supervision order or interim supervision order is a\nsucceeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to each earlier\nextended supervision order or interim supervision order.\n6UA  When a community safety supervision order is taken to be in\nforce\n\nFor the purposes of this Act, a community safety supervision order\nis taken to be in force in relation to a person if the order has been\nmade but the period specified in the order under\nparagraph 395.13(5)(d) of the Criminal Code has not yet begun.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6u-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6u-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6u-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aaa4bdd96f4042efb527e3c7ba0d684dff6a49a1518fa61babf934800254ec3a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6u",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6U Succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If 2 or more successive control orders are made in relation to the\nsame person, each later control order is a succeeding Part 5.3\nsupervisory order in relation to each earlier control order.\nNote:\nIf an interim control order is confirmed, the confirmed control order is\na succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to the interim\ncontrol order (see the definition of control order in section 5).\n\n(2) If an interim supervision order is made in relation to a person, any\nlater extended supervision order in relation to the person is a\nsucceeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to an earlier\ninterim supervision order.\n\n(3) If 2 or more successive extended supervision orders or interim\nsupervision orders are made in relation to the same person, each\nlater extended supervision order or interim supervision order is a\nsucceeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in relation to each earlier\nextended supervision order or interim supervision order.\n6UA  When a community safety supervision order is taken to be in\nforce\n\nFor the purposes of this Act, a community safety supervision order\nis taken to be in force in relation to a person if the order has been\nmade but the period specified in the order under\nparagraph 395.13(5)(d) of the Criminal Code has not yet begun."
    },
