    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6v",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6V Substitution of references to the Attorney-General",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6v"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.113",
      "values:originalText": "Unless the Prime Minister is satisfied that exceptional\ncircumstances exist, the Governor-General must not make a\nsubstituted reference order under subsection 19B(2) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901 that relates to a provision of this Act that\nrefers to the Attorney-General.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "Unless the Prime Minister is satisfied that exceptional\ncircumstances exist, the Governor-General must not make a\nsubstituted reference order under subsection 19B(2) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901 that relates to a provision of this Act that\nrefers to the Attorney-General.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6v-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6v-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6v-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b3bb675534c5e3d8a5853d2a125c3063378d7118f9953d627fa151a71f8f00d",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on making substituted reference orders under certain circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-6v",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6V Substitution of references to the Attorney-General",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 113,
      "values:originalText": "Unless the Prime Minister is satisfied that exceptional\ncircumstances exist, the Governor-General must not make a\nsubstituted reference order under subsection 19B(2) of the Acts\nInterpretation Act 1901 that relates to a provision of this Act that\nrefers to the Attorney-General.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6v-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6v"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6v-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "forbid",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits the Governor-General from making substituted reference orders.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Prime Minister is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Governor-General must not make a substituted reference order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-6v-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Relates to exceptional circumstances.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Exceptional circumstances exist.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "During exceptional circumstances, the Governor-General must not make a substituted reference order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Telecommunications not to be intercepted",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.114",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person shall not:\n\n(a) intercept;\n\n(b) authorize, suffer or permit another person to intercept; or\n\n(c) do any act or thing that will enable him or her or another\nperson to intercept;\na communication passing over a telecommunications system.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to or in relation to:\n\n(a) an act or thing done by an employee of a carrier in the course\nof his or her duties for or in connection with:\n\n(i) the installation of any line, or the installation of any\nequipment, used or intended for use in connection with\na telecommunications service; or\n\n(ii) the operation or maintenance of a telecommunications\nsystem; or\n\n(iii) the identifying or tracing of any person who has\ncontravened, or is suspected of having contravened or\nbeing likely to contravene, a provision of Part 10.6 of\nthe Criminal Code;\n\nwhere it is reasonably necessary for the employee to do that\nact or thing in order to perform those duties effectively; or\n\n(aa) the interception of a communication by another person\nlawfully engaged in duties relating to the installation,\nconnection or maintenance of equipment or a line, where it is\nreasonably necessary for the person to intercept the\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nProhibition on interception of telecommunications  Part 2-1\n\nSection 7\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncommunication in order to perform those duties effectively;\nor\n\n(aaa) the interception of a communication by a person if:\n\n(i) the person is authorised, in writing, by a responsible\nperson for a computer network to engage in network\nprotection duties in relation to the network; and\n\n(ii) it is reasonably necessary for the person to intercept the\ncommunication in order to perform those duties\neffectively; or\n\n(ab) the interception of a communication by a person lawfully\nengaged in duties relating to the installation, connection or\nmaintenance of equipment used, or to be used, for the\ninterception of communications under warrants; or\n\n(ac) the interception of a communication where the interception\nresults from, or is incidental to, action taken by an ASIO\nemployee, in the lawful performance of his or her duties, for\nthe purpose of:\n\n(i) discovering whether a listening device is being used at,\nor in relation to, a particular place; or\n\n(ii) determining the location of a listening device; or\n\n(ad) the interception of a communication where the interception\nresults from, or is incidental to, action taken by an ASIO\naffiliate, in accordance with the contract, agreement or other\narrangement under which the ASIO affiliate is performing\nfunctions or services for the Organisation, for the purpose of:\n\n(i) discovering whether a listening device is being used at,\nor in relation to, a particular place; or\n\n(ii) determining the location of a listening device; or\n\n(b) the interception of a communication under a warrant; or\n\n(ba) the interception of a communication under subsection 25A(4)\nor (8), 27A(1) or (3C), 27E(2) or 27E(6) of the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation Act 1979; or\n\n(bb) the interception of a communication under\nsubsection 27E(7), 27KE(9) or 27KP(8) of the Surveillance\nDevices Act 2004; or\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person shall not:\n\n(a) intercept;\n\n(b) authorize, suffer or permit another person to intercept; or\n\n(c) do any act or thing that will enable him or her or another\nperson to intercept;\na communication passing over a telecommunications system.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to or in relation to:\n\n(a) an act or thing done by an employee of a carrier in the course\nof his or her duties for or in connection with:\n\n(i) the installation of any line, or the installation of any\nequipment, used or intended for use in connection with\na telecommunications service; or\n\n(ii) the operation or maintenance of a telecommunications\nsystem; or\n\n(iii) the identifying or tracing of any person who has\ncontravened, or is suspected of having contravened or\nbeing likely to contravene, a provision of Part 10.6 of\nthe Criminal Code;\n\nwhere it is reasonably necessary for the employee to do that\nact or thing in order to perform those duties effectively; or\n\n(aa) the interception of a communication by another person\nlawfully engaged in duties relating to the installation,\nconnection or maintenance of equipment or a line, where it is\nreasonably necessary for the person to intercept the\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nProhibition on interception of telecommunications  Part 2-1\n\nSection 7\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ncommunication in order to perform those duties effectively;\nor\n\n(aaa) the interception of a communication by a person if:\n\n(i) the person is authorised, in writing, by a responsible\nperson for a computer network to engage in network\nprotection duties in relation to the network; and\n\n(ii) it is reasonably necessary for the person to intercept the\ncommunication in order to perform those duties\neffectively; or\n\n(ab) the interception of a communication by a person lawfully\nengaged in duties relating to the installation, connection or\nmaintenance of equipment used, or to be used, for the\ninterception of communic",
