    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Issue of telecommunications service warrants by Attorney-General",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.119",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, upon receipt by the Attorney-General of a request by the\nDirector-General of Security for the issue of a warrant under this\nsection in respect of a telecommunications service, the\nAttorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the telecommunications service is being or is likely to be:\n\n(i) used by a person engaged in, or reasonably suspected by\nthe Director-General of Security of being engaged in, or\nof being likely to engage in, activities prejudicial to\nsecurity; or\n\n(ia) the means by which a person receives or sends a\ncommunication from or to another person who is\nengaged in, or reasonably suspected by the\nDirector-General of Security of being engaged in, or of\nbeing likely to engage in, such activities; or\n\n(ii) used for purposes prejudicial to security; and\n\n(b) the interception by the Organisation of communications\nmade to or from the telecommunications service will, or is\nlikely to, assist the Organisation in carrying out its function\nof obtaining intelligence relating to security;\nthe Attorney-General may, by warrant under his or her hand,\nauthorize persons approved under section 12 in respect of the\nwarrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or restrictions that\nare specified in the warrant, communications that are being made\nto or from that service and such a warrant may authorize entry on\nany premises specified in the warrant for the purpose of installing,\nmaintaining, using or recovering any equipment used to intercept\nsuch communications.\nNote:\nSubparagraph (a)(ia)—subsection (3) restricts the issuing of warrants\nif subparagraph (a)(ia) applies.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where, upon receipt by the Attorney-General of a request by the\nDirector-General of Security for the issue of a warrant under this\nsection in respect of a telecommunications service, the\nAttorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the telecommunications service is being or is likely to be:\n\n(i) used by a person engaged in, or reasonably suspected by\nthe Director-General of Security of being engaged in, or\nof being likely to engage in, activities prejudicial to\nsecurity; or\n\n(ia) the means by which a person receives or sends a\ncommunication from or to another person who is\nengaged in, or reasonably suspected by the\nDirector-General of Security of being engaged in, or of\nbeing likely to engage in, such activities; or\n\n(ii) used for purposes prejudicial to security; and\n\n(b) the interception by the Organisation of communications\nmade to or from the telecommunications service will, or is\nlikely to, assist the Organisation in carrying out its function\nof obtaining intelligence relating to security;\nthe Attorney-General may, by warrant under his or her hand,\nauthorize persons approved under section 12 in respect of the\nwarrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or restrictions that\nare specified in the warrant, communications that are being made\nto or from that service and such a warrant may authorize entry on\nany premises specified in the warrant for the purpose of installing,\nmaintaining, using or recovering any equipment used to intercept\nsuch communications.\nNote:\nSubparagraph (a)(ia)—subsection (3) restricts the issuing of warrants\nif subparagraph (a)(ia) applies.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-9-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-9-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a35d0a1e23c5684e79f5c9682420867050a7cfcb0f2d07af39d1740cf313521c",
      "skos:note": "Attorney-General may issue warrant for interception of communications under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Issue of telecommunications service warrants by Attorney-General",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 119,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, upon receipt by the Attorney-General of a request by the\nDirector-General of Security for the issue of a warrant under this\nsection in respect of a telecommunications service, the\nAttorney-General is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the telecommunications service is being or is likely to be:\n\n(i) used by a person engaged in, or reasonably suspected by\nthe Director-General of Security of being engaged in, or\nof being likely to engage in, activities prejudicial to\nsecurity; or\n\n(ia) the means by which a person receives or sends a\ncommunication from or to another person who is\nengaged in, or reasonably suspected by the\nDirector-General of Security of being engaged in, or of\nbeing likely to engage in, such activities; or\n\n(ii) used for purposes prejudicial to security; and\n\n(b) the interception by the Organisation of communications\nmade to or from the telecommunications service will, or is\nlikely to, assist the Organisation in carrying out its function\nof obtaining intelligence relating to security;\nthe Attorney-General may, by warrant under his or her hand,\nauthorize persons approved under section 12 in respect of the\nwarrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or restrictions that\nare specified in the warrant, communications that are being made\nto or from that service and such a warrant may authorize entry on\nany premises specified in the warrant for the purpose of installing,\nmaintaining, using or recovering any equipment used to intercept\nsuch communications.\nNote:\nSubparagraph (a)(ia)—subsection (3) restricts the issuing of warrants\nif subparagraph (a)(ia) applies.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
