    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-9a-ss-1c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9A(1C) Issue of named person warrants by Attorney-General",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-9a-ss-1c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.120",
      "values:originalText": "(1C) The reference in paragraph (1)(b) to the interception of\ncommunications made to or from a telecommunications service\nincludes a reference to the accessing of the communications as\nstored communications after they have ceased to pass over a\ntelecommunications system.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1C) The reference in paragraph (1)(b) to the interception of\ncommunications made to or from a telecommunications service\nincludes a reference to the accessing of the communications as\nstored communications after they have ceased to pass over a\ntelecommunications system.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-9a"
      },
