    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11A Telecommunications service warrant for collection of foreign",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-11a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "intelligence\n\n(1) Where:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to\nthe Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to\nissue a warrant under this section authorising persons\napproved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts\nor things referred to in subsection 9(1) in relation to a\nparticular telecommunications service for the purpose of\nobtaining foreign intelligence relating to a matter specified in\nthe notice; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "intelligence\n\n(1) Where:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to\nthe Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to\nissue a warrant under this section authorising persons\napproved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts\nor things referred to in subsection 9(1) in relation to a\nparticular telecommunications service for the purpose of\nobtaining foreign intelligence relating to a matter specified in\nthe notice; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1fd00f3b97b8501bc770be9afef199ce7a252a888bc96ecddab04bdec98a041",
      "skos:note": "The Attorney-General must issue a warrant for the collection of foreign intelligence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-11a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11A Telecommunications service warrant for collection of foreign",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "intelligence\n\n(1) Where:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to\nthe Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to\nissue a warrant under this section authorising persons\napproved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts\nor things referred to in subsection 9(1) in relation to a\nparticular telecommunications service for the purpose of\nobtaining foreign intelligence relating to a matter specified in\nthe notice; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The Attorney-General must issue a warrant.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11B Named person warrant for collection of foreign intelligence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-11b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.127",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, under his or her hand, issue a warrant\nin respect of a person if:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to\nthe Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to\nissue a warrant under this section authorising persons\napproved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts\nor things referred to in subsection 9A(1A) in relation to:\n\n(i) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that a person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(ii) communications that are being made by means of a\nparticular telecommunications device or particular\ntelecommunications devices that a person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use;\n\nfor the purpose of obtaining foreign intelligence relating to a\nmatter specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied, on the basis of advice\nreceived from the Minister for Defence or the Minister for\nForeign Affairs, that:\n\n(i) the obtaining of foreign intelligence relating to that\nmatter is in the interests of Australia’s national security,\nAustralia’s foreign relations or Australia’s national\neconomic well-being; and\n\n(ii) it is necessary to intercept the communications of the\nperson or foreign organisation in order to obtain the\nintelligence referred to in paragraph (a); and\n\n(iii) relying on a telecommunications service warrant to\nobtain the intelligence would be ineffective.\n\n(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in\nrespect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or\nrestrictions that are specified in the warrant:\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may, under his or her hand, issue a warrant\nin respect of a person if:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to\nthe Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to\nissue a warrant under this section authorising persons\napproved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts\nor things referred to in subsection 9A(1A) in relation to:\n\n(i) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that a person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(ii) communications that are being made by means of a\nparticular telecommunications device or particular\ntelecommunications devices that a person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use;\n\nfor the purpose of obtaining foreign intelligence relating to a\nmatter specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied, on the basis of advice\nreceived from the Minister for Defence or the Minister for\nForeign Affairs, that:\n\n(i) the obtaining of foreign intelligence relating to that\nmatter is in the interests of Australia’s national security,\nAustralia’s foreign relations or Australia’s national\neconomic well-being; and\n\n(ii) it is necessary to intercept the communications of the\nperson or foreign organisation in order to obtain the\nintelligence referred to in paragraph (a); and\n\n(iii) relying on a telecommunications service warrant to\nobtain the intelligence would be ineffective.\n\n(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in\nrespect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or\nrestrictions that are specified in the warrant:\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11b-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd5ec6c52d97b8314f78c9c75767b7b6f98c68201cb17dfa043ce211e8485016"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-11b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11B Named person warrant for collection of foreign intelligence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 127,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, under his or her hand, issue a warrant\nin respect of a person if:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to\nthe Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to\nissue a warrant under this section authorising persons\napproved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts\nor things referred to in subsection 9A(1A) in relation to:\n\n(i) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that a person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(ii) communications that are being made by means of a\nparticular telecommunications device or particular\ntelecommunications devices that a person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use;\n\nfor the purpose of obtaining foreign intelligence relating to a\nmatter specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied, on the basis of advice\nreceived from the Minister for Defence or the Minister for\nForeign Affairs, that:\n\n(i) the obtaining of foreign intelligence relating to that\nmatter is in the interests of Australia’s national security,\nAustralia’s foreign relations or Australia’s national\neconomic well-being; and\n\n(ii) it is necessary to intercept the communications of the\nperson or foreign organisation in order to obtain the\nintelligence referred to in paragraph (a); and\n\n(iii) relying on a telecommunications service warrant to\nobtain the intelligence would be ineffective.\n\n(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in\nrespect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or\nrestrictions that are specified in the warrant:\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-11b-ss-1",
