    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Persons authorised to intercept communications for Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.135",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General of Security, or an ASIO employee or ASIO\naffiliate appointed by the Director-General of Security, in writing,\nto be an authorizing officer for the purposes of this subsection,\nmay, by writing under his or her hand, approve any persons, or\nclass of persons, as persons authorized to exercise, on behalf of the\nOrganisation, the authority conferred by Part 2-2 warrants.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, and without limiting subsection (1), if approval is\ngiven to a person or class of persons holding, occupying or\nperforming the duties of an office or position, then the approval\nextends to such an office or position that comes into existence after\nthe approval is given.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, affect the interpretation of\nany other provision of this Act.\n\n(4) The Director-General of Security must, as soon as practicable after\nthe authority conferred by a Part 2-2 warrant is exercised on behalf\nof the Organisation, cause one or more written records to be made\nthat identify each person who exercised that authority.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General of Security, or an ASIO employee or ASIO\naffiliate appointed by the Director-General of Security, in writing,\nto be an authorizing officer for the purposes of this subsection,\nmay, by writing under his or her hand, approve any persons, or\nclass of persons, as persons authorized to exercise, on behalf of the\nOrganisation, the authority conferred by Part 2-2 warrants.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, and without limiting subsection (1), if approval is\ngiven to a person or class of persons holding, occupying or\nperforming the duties of an office or position, then the approval\nextends to such an office or position that comes into existence after\nthe approval is given.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, affect the interpretation of\nany other provision of this Act.\n\n(4) The Director-General of Security must, as soon as practicable after\nthe authority conferred by a Part 2-2 warrant is exercised on behalf\nof the Organisation, cause one or more written records to be made\nthat identify each person who exercised that authority.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-12-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-12-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-12-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-12-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a072c0899e7084784017395517d778c88163c650b50f5153939a329bf30dc45"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Persons authorised to intercept communications for Organisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 135,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General of Security, or an ASIO employee or ASIO\naffiliate appointed by the Director-General of Security, in writing,\nto be an authorizing officer for the purposes of this subsection,\nmay, by writing under his or her hand, approve any persons, or\nclass of persons, as persons authorized to exercise, on behalf of the\nOrganisation, the authority conferred by Part 2-2 warrants.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, and without limiting subsection (1), if approval is\ngiven to a person or class of persons holding, occupying or\nperforming the duties of an office or position, then the approval\nextends to such an office or position that comes into existence after\nthe approval is given.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, affect the interpretation of\nany other provision of this Act.\n\n(4) The Director-General of Security must, as soon as practicable after\nthe authority conferred by a Part 2-2 warrant is exercised on behalf\nof the Organisation, cause one or more written records to be made\nthat identify each person who exercised that authority."
    },
