    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13 Discontinuance of interception before expiration of warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.135",
      "values:originalText": "Where, before a Part 2-2 warrant ceases to be in force, the\nDirector-General of Security is satisfied that the grounds on which\nthe warrant was issued have ceased to exist, he or she shall\nforthwith inform the Attorney-General accordingly and take such\nsteps that are necessary to ensure that the interception of\ncommunications under the warrant is discontinued.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "Where, before a Part 2-2 warrant ceases to be in force, the\nDirector-General of Security is satisfied that the grounds on which\nthe warrant was issued have ceased to exist, he or she shall\nforthwith inform the Attorney-General accordingly and take such\nsteps that are necessary to ensure that the interception of\ncommunications under the warrant is discontinued.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-13-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-13-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b658e8782a73b3a867b1f4673f9b181f563ef34aba49df12759fb6cbe9a5e77e",
      "skos:note": "Ensure discontinuation of interception upon warrant expiration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13 Discontinuance of interception before expiration of warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 135,
      "values:originalText": "Where, before a Part 2-2 warrant ceases to be in force, the\nDirector-General of Security is satisfied that the grounds on which\nthe warrant was issued have ceased to exist, he or she shall\nforthwith inform the Attorney-General accordingly and take such\nsteps that are necessary to ensure that the interception of\ncommunications under the warrant is discontinued.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-13-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-13"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-13-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "shall",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imperative obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-14",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "14 Certain records retained by Organisation to be destroyed",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-14"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "Where:\n\n(a) a record or copy has been made of a communication\nintercepted by virtue of a Part 2-2 warrant;\n\n(b) the record or copy is in the possession or custody, or under\nthe control, of the Organisation; and\n\n(c) the Director-General of Security is satisfied that the record or\ncopy is not required, and is not likely to be required, in or in\nconnection with the performance by the Organisation of its\nfunctions or the exercise of its powers (including the powers\nconferred by sections 64 and 65);\nthe Director-General of Security shall cause the record or copy to\nbe destroyed.\nNote:\nSee subsection 11C(5) and paragraph 11C(6)(b) for additional rules\nabout the destruction of material obtained under a warrant issued\nunder section 11C.",
      "skos:definition": "Where:\n\n(a) a record or copy has been made of a communication\nintercepted by virtue of a Part 2-2 warrant;\n\n(b) the record or copy is in the possession or custody, or under\nthe control, of the Organisation; and\n\n(c) the Director-General of Security is satisfied that the record or\ncopy is not required, and is not likely to be required, in or in\nconnection with the performance by the Organisation of its\nfunctions or the exercise of its powers (including the powers\nconferred by sections 64 and 65);\nthe Director-General of Security shall cause the record or copy to\nbe destroyed.\nNote:\nSee subsection 11C(5) and paragraph 11C(6)(b) for additional rules\nabout the destruction of material obtained under a warrant issued\nunder section 11C.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-14-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-14-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b629337983c16398718927fc2c267a33766611ff6f6f06ec269b2beb01a9d058",
      "skos:note": "Destroy records no longer required for Organisation's functions or powers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Certain records retained by Organisation to be destroyed",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "Where:\n\n(a) a record or copy has been made of a communication\nintercepted by virtue of a Part 2-2 warrant;\n\n(b) the record or copy is in the possession or custody, or under\nthe control, of the Organisation; and\n\n(c) the Director-General of Security is satisfied that the record or\ncopy is not required, and is not likely to be required, in or in\nconnection with the performance by the Organisation of its\nfunctions or the exercise of its powers (including the powers\nconferred by sections 64 and 65);\nthe Director-General of Security shall cause the record or copy to\nbe destroyed.\nNote:\nSee subsection 11C(5) and paragraph 11C(6)(b) for additional rules\nabout the destruction of material obtained under a warrant issued\nunder section 11C."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-14-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-14"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-14-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits destruction of records",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 How warrants etc. to be dealt with",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where the Attorney-General issues or revokes a Part 2-2 warrant,\nhe or she shall cause:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security to be informed forthwith of\nthe issue of the warrant or of the revocation, as the case may\nbe; and\n\n(b) the warrant or the instrument of revocation, as the case may\nbe, to be forwarded, as soon as practicable, to the Director\nGeneral of Security.\n\n(1A) Where:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security is informed under\nparagraph (1)(a) of the issue of a warrant (other than a\nwarrant under section 11C); and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept\ncommunications made to or from a telecommunications\nservice while they are passing over a telecommunications\nsystem operated by a carrier; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising the Organisation to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-2\n\nSection 15\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ba) the execution of the warrant will involve the taking of action\nby the carrier or its employees;\nthe Director-General of Security shall cause:\n\n(c) an authorised representative of that carrier to be informed\nforthwith of the issue of the warrant; and\n\n(d) where, under paragraph (1)(b), the Director-General of\nSecurity receives the warrant—a copy of the warrant,\ncertified in writing by a certifying person to be a true copy of\nthe warrant, to be given as soon as practicable to that\nauthorised representative.\nNote:\nSubsection 15(7) deals with cases where the Director-General of\nSecurity is informed of the issue of a warrant under section 11C.\n\n(1B) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1A), of the issue of a warrant; and\n\n(b) the Director-General of Security is informed under\nparagraph (1)(a) that the warrant has been revoked;\nthe Director-General of Security shall cause:\n\n(c) that authorised representative to be informed forthwith of the\nrevocation; and\n\n(d) where, under paragraph (1)(b), the Director-General of\nSecurity receives the instrument of revocation—a copy of the\ninstrument, certified in writing by a certifying person to be a\ntrue copy of the instrument, to be forwarded as soon as\npracticable to that authorised representative.\n\n(3) The Attorney-General shall record on each request in writing for\nthe issue of a warrant received by him or her from the\nDirector-General of Security his or her decision with respect to the\nrequest and shall cause the request to be returned to the\nDirector-General of Security.\n\n(4) Where:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security issues a warrant under\nsection 10; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where the Attorney-General issues or revokes a Part 2-2 warrant,\nhe or she shall cause:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security to be informed forthwith of\nthe issue of the warrant or of the revocation, as the case may\nbe; and\n\n(b) the warrant or the instrument of revocation, as the case may\nbe, to be forwarded, as soon as practicable, to the Director\nGeneral of Security.\n\n(1A) Where:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security is informed under\nparagraph (1)(a) of the issue of a warrant (other than a\nwarrant under section 11C); and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept\ncommunications made to or from a telecommunications\nservice while they are passing over a telecommunications\nsystem operated by a carrier; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising the Organisation to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-2\n\nSection 15\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ba) the execution of the warrant will involve the taking of action\nby the carrier or its employees;\nthe Director-General of Security shall cause:\n\n(c) an authorised representative of that carrier to be informed\nforthwith of the issue of the warrant; and\n\n(d) where, under paragraph (1)(b), the Director-General of\nSecurity receives the warrant—a copy of the warrant,\ncertified in writing by a certifying person to be a true copy of\nthe warrant, to be given as soon as practicable to that\nauthorised representative.\nNote:\nSubsection 15(7) deals with cases where the Director-General of\nSecurity is informed of the issue of a warrant under section 11C.\n\n(1B) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1A), of the issue of a warrant; and\n\n(b) the Director-General of Security is informed under\nparagraph (1)(a) that the warrant has been revoked;\nthe Director-General of Security shall cause:\n\n(c) that authorised representative to be informed forthwith of the\nrevocation; and\n\n(d) where, under par",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-15-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-15-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-15-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-15-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-15-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5ea8ae03dd1bb4ae51fa47e6e2035333360807795259a75518fdd3a59e09bf57"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 How warrants etc. to be dealt with",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where the Attorney-General issues or revokes a Part 2-2 warrant,\nhe or she shall cause:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security to be informed forthwith of\nthe issue of the warrant or of the revocation, as the case may\nbe; and\n\n(b) the warrant or the instrument of revocation, as the case may\nbe, to be forwarded, as soon as practicable, to the Director\nGeneral of Security.\n\n(1A) Where:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security is informed under\nparagraph (1)(a) of the issue of a warrant (other than a\nwarrant under section 11C); and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept\ncommunications made to or from a telecommunications\nservice while they are passing over a telecommunications\nsystem operated by a carrier; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising the Organisation to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-2\n\nSection 15\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ba) the execution of the warrant will involve the taking of action\nby the carrier or its employees;\nthe Director-General of Security shall cause:\n\n(c) an authorised representative of that carrier to be informed\nforthwith of the issue of the warrant; and\n\n(d) where, under paragraph (1)(b), the Director-General of\nSecurity receives the warrant—a copy of the warrant,\ncertified in writing by a certifying person to be a true copy of\nthe warrant, to be given as soon as practicable to that\nauthorised representative.\nNote:\nSubsection 15(7) deals with cases where the Director-General of\nSecurity is informed of the issue of a warrant under section 11C.\n\n(1B) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1A), of the issue of a warrant; and\n\n(b) the Director-General of Security is informed under\nparagraph (1)(a) that the warrant has been revoked;\nthe Director-General of Security shall cause:\n\n(c) that authorised representative to be informed forthwith of the\nrevocation; and\n\n(d) where, under paragraph (1)(b), the Director-General of\nSecurity receives the instrument of revocation—a copy of the\ninstrument, certified in writing by a certifying person to be a\ntrue copy of the instrument, to be forwarded as soon as\npracticable to that authorised representative.\n\n(3) The Attorney-General shall record on each request in writing for\nthe issue of a warrant received by him or her from the\nDirector-General of Security his or her decision with respect to the\nrequest and shall cause the request to be returned to the\nDirector-General of Security.\n\n(4) Where:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security issues a warrant under\nsection 10; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
