    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-17",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "17 Reports to be made to Attorney-General on results of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-17"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.140",
      "values:originalText": "interception\n\n(1) The Director-General of Security shall furnish to the\nAttorney-General, in respect of each Part 2-2 warrant, within 3\nmonths after the expiration or revocation, whichever first occurs,\nof the warrant, a report in writing on the extent to which the\ninterception of communications under the warrant has assisted the\nOrganisation in carrying out its functions.\n\n(2) A report under subsection (1) in relation to a warrant issued under\nsection 9A or 11B must include details of the telecommunications\nservice to or from which each intercepted communication was\nmade.",
      "skos:definition": "interception\n\n(1) The Director-General of Security shall furnish to the\nAttorney-General, in respect of each Part 2-2 warrant, within 3\nmonths after the expiration or revocation, whichever first occurs,\nof the warrant, a report in writing on the extent to which the\ninterception of communications under the warrant has assisted the\nOrganisation in carrying out its functions.\n\n(2) A report under subsection (1) in relation to a warrant issued under\nsection 9A or 11B must include details of the telecommunications\nservice to or from which each intercepted communication was\nmade.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-17-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-17-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "843db2f510567643feae062e16b76e10ab39599d3129b503c925fb271a71a86a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-17",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "17 Reports to be made to Attorney-General on results of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 140,
      "values:originalText": "interception\n\n(1) The Director-General of Security shall furnish to the\nAttorney-General, in respect of each Part 2-2 warrant, within 3\nmonths after the expiration or revocation, whichever first occurs,\nof the warrant, a report in writing on the extent to which the\ninterception of communications under the warrant has assisted the\nOrganisation in carrying out its functions.\n\n(2) A report under subsection (1) in relation to a warrant issued under\nsection 9A or 11B must include details of the telecommunications\nservice to or from which each intercepted communication was\nmade."
    },
