      "cml:integrityHash": "3aab85f2df4f904cfc2e932ec6c5de0170214aec08ec926c30002b842206262d",
      "skos:note": "Issue written certificate with relevant facts for warrant execution"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-18-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18(3) Evidentiary certificates",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 140,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Director-General of Security or the Deputy Director-General\nof Security may issue a written certificate signed by him or her\nsetting out such facts as he or she considers relevant with respect to\nacts or things done:\n\n(a) in order to enable, or in connection with enabling, a warrant\nissued under this Part to be executed; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant issued under\nthis Part."
    },
