    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-30",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30 Emergency requests",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-30"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.143",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n\n(a) a person is a party to a communication passing over a\ntelecommunications system;\n\n(b) as a result of information conveyed by another party to the\ncommunication (in this section referred to as the caller) and\nof any other matters, the first-mentioned person forms the\nhonest belief that either of the following emergencies exist:\n\n(i) another person (whether or not the caller) is dying, is\nbeing seriously injured or has been seriously injured;\n\n(ii) another person (whether or not the caller) is likely to die\nor be seriously injured; and\n\n(c) the first-mentioned person does not know the location of the\ncaller;\nthe first-mentioned person may:\n\n(d) in a case where the first-mentioned person:\n\n(i) is a member of a police force; and\n\n(ii) is of the opinion that tracing the location of the caller is\nlikely to be of assistance in dealing with the emergency;\n\nrequest, or cause another member of a police force to request,\nan employee of a carrier to intercept, or to cause other\nemployees of the carrier to intercept, the communication for\nthe purposes of tracing the location of the caller; or\n\n(e) in a case where the first-mentioned person is not a member of\na police force—inform, or cause another person to inform, a\nmember of a police force of the matters referred to in\nparagraphs (a), (b) and (c).\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where:\n\n(a) a person is a party to a communication passing over a\ntelecommunications system;\n\n(b) as a result of information conveyed by another party to the\ncommunication (in this section referred to as the caller) and\nof any other matters, the first-mentioned person forms the\nhonest belief that either of the following emergencies exist:\n\n(i) another person (whether or not the caller) is dying, is\nbeing seriously injured or has been seriously injured;\n\n(ii) another person (whether or not the caller) is likely to die\nor be seriously injured; and\n\n(c) the first-mentioned person does not know the location of the\ncaller;\nthe first-mentioned person may:\n\n(d) in a case where the first-mentioned person:\n\n(i) is a member of a police force; and\n\n(ii) is of the opinion that tracing the location of the caller is\nlikely to be of assistance in dealing with the emergency;\n\nrequest, or cause another member of a police force to request,\nan employee of a carrier to intercept, or to cause other\nemployees of the carrier to intercept, the communication for\nthe purposes of tracing the location of the caller; or\n\n(e) in a case where the first-mentioned person is not a member of\na police force—inform, or cause another person to inform, a\nmember of a police force of the matters referred to in\nparagraphs (a), (b) and (c).\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-30-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-30-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f418051a49d8fc89cb5a4326b35bbf0d02162f4ddeecf7e81d4a9ba82e6d320d",
      "skos:note": "Request for interception of communication in emergency situations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-30",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30 Emergency requests",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 143,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n\n(a) a person is a party to a communication passing over a\ntelecommunications system;\n\n(b) as a result of information conveyed by another party to the\ncommunication (in this section referred to as the caller) and\nof any other matters, the first-mentioned person forms the\nhonest belief that either of the following emergencies exist:\n\n(i) another person (whether or not the caller) is dying, is\nbeing seriously injured or has been seriously injured;\n\n(ii) another person (whether or not the caller) is likely to die\nor be seriously injured; and\n\n(c) the first-mentioned person does not know the location of the\ncaller;\nthe first-mentioned person may:\n\n(d) in a case where the first-mentioned person:\n\n(i) is a member of a police force; and\n\n(ii) is of the opinion that tracing the location of the caller is\nlikely to be of assistance in dealing with the emergency;\n\nrequest, or cause another member of a police force to request,\nan employee of a carrier to intercept, or to cause other\nemployees of the carrier to intercept, the communication for\nthe purposes of tracing the location of the caller; or\n\n(e) in a case where the first-mentioned person is not a member of\na police force—inform, or cause another person to inform, a\nmember of a police force of the matters referred to in\nparagraphs (a), (b) and (c).\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-30-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-30"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-30-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to intercept communication.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(caller is dying, is being seriously injured or has been seriously injured)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Request interception of communication."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31 Applications for authorisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.145",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The head (however described) of a security authority that has\nfunctions that include activities relating to developing or testing\ntechnologies, or interception capabilities, or a person acting as that\nhead, may request the Attorney-General to authorise, under\nsection 31A, interception of communications passing over a\ntelecommunications system:\n\n(a) if one or more carriers are specified in the request for the\npurposes of this paragraph—by:\n\n(i) employees of the security authority authorised under\nsection 31B; and\n\n(ii) employees of those carriers; or\n\n(b) if no carriers are specified in the request for the purposes of\nparagraph (a)—by employees of the security authority\nauthorised under section 31B.\n\n(2) The request:\n\n(a) must be in writing; and\n\n(b) must include details of the development or testing of\ntechnologies, or interception capabilities, in relation to which\nauthorisation is sought; and\n\n(c) must include details of the extent to which the development\nor testing would involve, or would be likely to involve,\ninterception of communications passing over a\ntelecommunications system; and\n\n(d) must refer to the functions of the authority that the\ndevelopment or testing would support; and\n\n(e) must state the grounds for seeking the authorisation; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The head (however described) of a security authority that has\nfunctions that include activities relating to developing or testing\ntechnologies, or interception capabilities, or a person acting as that\nhead, may request the Attorney-General to authorise, under\nsection 31A, interception of communications passing over a\ntelecommunications system:\n\n(a) if one or more carriers are specified in the request for the\npurposes of this paragraph—by:\n\n(i) employees of the security authority authorised under\nsection 31B; and\n\n(ii) employees of those carriers; or\n\n(b) if no carriers are specified in the request for the purposes of\nparagraph (a)—by employees of the security authority\nauthorised under section 31B.\n\n(2) The request:\n\n(a) must be in writing; and\n\n(b) must include details of the development or testing of\ntechnologies, or interception capabilities, in relation to which\nauthorisation is sought; and\n\n(c) must include details of the extent to which the development\nor testing would involve, or would be likely to involve,\ninterception of communications passing over a\ntelecommunications system; and\n\n(d) must refer to the functions of the authority that the\ndevelopment or testing would support; and\n\n(e) must state the grounds for seeking the authorisation; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3d93cabb09c7f54c18b8b86aa30cfba7538e658614e9f331b8c9f33377aeaf43"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31 Applications for authorisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 145,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The head (however described) of a security authority that has\nfunctions that include activities relating to developing or testing\ntechnologies, or interception capabilities, or a person acting as that\nhead, may request the Attorney-General to authorise, under\nsection 31A, interception of communications passing over a\ntelecommunications system:\n\n(a) if one or more carriers are specified in the request for the\npurposes of this paragraph—by:\n\n(i) employees of the security authority authorised under\nsection 31B; and\n\n(ii) employees of those carriers; or\n\n(b) if no carriers are specified in the request for the purposes of\nparagraph (a)—by employees of the security authority\nauthorised under section 31B.\n\n(2) The request:\n\n(a) must be in writing; and\n\n(b) must include details of the development or testing of\ntechnologies, or interception capabilities, in relation to which\nauthorisation is sought; and\n\n(c) must include details of the extent to which the development\nor testing would involve, or would be likely to involve,\ninterception of communications passing over a\ntelecommunications system; and\n\n(d) must refer to the functions of the authority that the\ndevelopment or testing would support; and\n\n(e) must state the grounds for seeking the authorisation; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
