    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31A(2) Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.146",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The authorisation is subject to:\n\n(a) a condition prohibiting:\n\n(i) interception of communications passing over a\ntelecommunications system except for the purposes of\ndevelopment or testing of technologies, or interception\ncapabilities; or\n\n(ii) communicating, using or recording such\ncommunications except for such purposes; and\n\n(b) any other conditions specified in the authorisation.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nAuthorisation of interception for developing and testing interception capabilities  Part\n2-4\n\nSection 31AA\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The authorisation is subject to:\n\n(a) a condition prohibiting:\n\n(i) interception of communications passing over a\ntelecommunications system except for the purposes of\ndevelopment or testing of technologies, or interception\ncapabilities; or\n\n(ii) communicating, using or recording such\ncommunications except for such purposes; and\n\n(b) any other conditions specified in the authorisation.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nAuthorisation of interception for developing and testing interception capabilities  Part\n2-4\n\nSection 31AA\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "22a228090185a20ac0a432b376f0a6d797c35605fd36400bc469cd2f432829ff",
      "skos:note": "Interception of communications passing over a telecommunications system except for the purposes of development or testing of technologies is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31A(2) Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 146,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The authorisation is subject to:\n\n(a) a condition prohibiting:\n\n(i) interception of communications passing over a\ntelecommunications system except for the purposes of\ndevelopment or testing of technologies, or interception\ncapabilities; or\n\n(ii) communicating, using or recording such\ncommunications except for such purposes; and\n\n(b) any other conditions specified in the authorisation.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nAuthorisation of interception for developing and testing interception capabilities  Part\n2-4\n\nSection 31AA\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
