    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31A(4A) Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31a-ss-4a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.146",
      "values:originalText": "(4A) If paragraph (1)(a) applies to the authorisation, this Part does not\nrequire that an authorised interception must involve:\n\n(a) one or more employees of the security authority referred to in\nthat paragraph; and\n\n(b) one or more employees of a carrier referred to in that\nparagraph;\nacting together or in the presence of each other.",
      "skos:definition": "(4A) If paragraph (1)(a) applies to the authorisation, this Part does not\nrequire that an authorised interception must involve:\n\n(a) one or more employees of the security authority referred to in\nthat paragraph; and\n\n(b) one or more employees of a carrier referred to in that\nparagraph;\nacting together or in the presence of each other.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-4a-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd60d4b5d36242b19e0aaecd9434a430c47a8d785a18fdf9a91ac18a21c16650",
      "skos:note": "Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31a-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31A(4A) Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 146,
      "values:originalText": "(4A) If paragraph (1)(a) applies to the authorisation, this Part does not\nrequire that an authorised interception must involve:\n\n(a) one or more employees of the security authority referred to in\nthat paragraph; and\n\n(b) one or more employees of a carrier referred to in that\nparagraph;\nacting together or in the presence of each other."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-4a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
