      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-4b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31A(4B) Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31a-ss-4b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.146",
      "values:originalText": "(4B) To avoid doubt, subparagraph (2)(a)(ii) has the effect that lawfully\nintercepted information obtained under the authorisation may be\ncommunicated, used or recorded for the purposes of development\nor testing of technologies, or interception capabilities.",
      "skos:definition": "(4B) To avoid doubt, subparagraph (2)(a)(ii) has the effect that lawfully\nintercepted information obtained under the authorisation may be\ncommunicated, used or recorded for the purposes of development\nor testing of technologies, or interception capabilities.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-4b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-4b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dae7f4234df4cc32ab467ca6b4aaeb1b2abab967ecd3bddf473524d5c96be5e9",
      "skos:note": "Authorisation for interception for developing technologies or testing capabilities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31a-ss-4b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31A(4B) Attorney-General may authorise interception for developing",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 146,
      "values:originalText": "(4B) To avoid doubt, subparagraph (2)(a)(ii) has the effect that lawfully\nintercepted information obtained under the authorisation may be\ncommunicated, used or recorded for the purposes of development\nor testing of technologies, or interception capabilities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31a-ss-4b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
