    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31AB Access to stored communications under section 31A",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.148",
      "values:originalText": "authorisations\n\nIn addition to authorising interception of communications, a\nsection 31A authorisation also authorises a person to access a\nstored communication if the section 31A authorisation would have\nauthorised interception of the communication if it were still\npassing over a telecommunications system.",
      "skos:definition": "authorisations\n\nIn addition to authorising interception of communications, a\nsection 31A authorisation also authorises a person to access a\nstored communication if the section 31A authorisation would have\nauthorised interception of the communication if it were still\npassing over a telecommunications system.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31ab-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "12f25ba581da26a77c65a742d0bab1097fa05a824f94cf254588d50eeb242ec1",
      "skos:note": "Authorises access to stored communications under section 31A authorisation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31ab",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31AB Access to stored communications under section 31A",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 148,
      "values:originalText": "authorisations\n\nIn addition to authorising interception of communications, a\nsection 31A authorisation also authorises a person to access a\nstored communication if the section 31A authorisation would have\nauthorised interception of the communication if it were still\npassing over a telecommunications system."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31ab-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31ab"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31B Authorisation of employees of a security authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.148",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following persons:\n\n(a) the head (however described) of a security authority;\n\n(b) an officer of the security authority covered by an approval in\nforce under subsection (2);\nmay, by writing, authorise employees of the authority for the\npurposes of this Part.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nAuthorisation of interception for developing and testing interception capabilities  Part\n2-4\n\nSection 31C\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) The head (however described) of a security authority may, by\nwriting, approve an officer of the authority for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(b).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The following persons:\n\n(a) the head (however described) of a security authority;\n\n(b) an officer of the security authority covered by an approval in\nforce under subsection (2);\nmay, by writing, authorise employees of the authority for the\npurposes of this Part.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nAuthorisation of interception for developing and testing interception capabilities  Part\n2-4\n\nSection 31C\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) The head (however described) of a security authority may, by\nwriting, approve an officer of the authority for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(b).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3eccee1ec3ffab5a8456ced068fa62e34fac02ae49755ea1bfb0c509f0c6e8d5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31B Authorisation of employees of a security authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 148,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following persons:\n\n(a) the head (however described) of a security authority;\n\n(b) an officer of the security authority covered by an approval in\nforce under subsection (2);\nmay, by writing, authorise employees of the authority for the\npurposes of this Part.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nAuthorisation of interception for developing and testing interception capabilities  Part\n2-4\n\nSection 31C\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) The head (however described) of a security authority may, by\nwriting, approve an officer of the authority for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(b)."
    },
