    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31C Destruction of records",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.149",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained, in the course of\ndeveloping or testing technologies or interception\ncapabilities, by interception of communications passing over\na telecommunications system is in a security authority’s\npossession; and\n\n(b) the information or record is no longer required in relation to\nthe development or testing;\nthe head (however described) of the security authority, or a person\nacting as that head, must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) The reference in paragraph (1)(a) to interception of\ncommunications passing over a telecommunications system\nincludes a reference to the accessing of the communications as\nstored communications after they have ceased to pass over a\ntelecommunications system.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained, in the course of\ndeveloping or testing technologies or interception\ncapabilities, by interception of communications passing over\na telecommunications system is in a security authority’s\npossession; and\n\n(b) the information or record is no longer required in relation to\nthe development or testing;\nthe head (however described) of the security authority, or a person\nacting as that head, must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) The reference in paragraph (1)(a) to interception of\ncommunications passing over a telecommunications system\nincludes a reference to the accessing of the communications as\nstored communications after they have ceased to pass over a\ntelecommunications system.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-31c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0f06e3407863aaa29e7b52516fe0a72509314b2dcaa42ffd5cae7e6599d7e732"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-31c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31C Destruction of records",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 149,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained, in the course of\ndeveloping or testing technologies or interception\ncapabilities, by interception of communications passing over\na telecommunications system is in a security authority’s\npossession; and\n\n(b) the information or record is no longer required in relation to\nthe development or testing;\nthe head (however described) of the security authority, or a person\nacting as that head, must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) The reference in paragraph (1)(a) to interception of\ncommunications passing over a telecommunications system\nincludes a reference to the accessing of the communications as\nstored communications after they have ceased to pass over a\ntelecommunications system."
    },
