    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-34",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34 Declaration of an eligible authority of a State as an agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-34"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.151",
      "values:originalText": "Subject to section 35, the Minister may, by legislative instrument\nand at the request of the Premier of a State, declare an eligible\nauthority of that State to be an agency for the purposes of this Act.\nNote:\nThe declaration may also authorise the eligible authority to apply for",
      "skos:definition": "Subject to section 35, the Minister may, by legislative instrument\nand at the request of the Premier of a State, declare an eligible\nauthority of that State to be an agency for the purposes of this Act.\nNote:\nThe declaration may also authorise the eligible authority to apply for",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-34-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2dffda7438416180b1b3edcee36763b05a8c2cadddb0a98c6f406ff7d7de6824",
      "skos:note": "Declaration of an eligible authority of a State as an agency"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-34",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34 Declaration of an eligible authority of a State as an agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 151,
      "values:originalText": "Subject to section 35, the Minister may, by legislative instrument\nand at the request of the Premier of a State, declare an eligible\nauthority of that State to be an agency for the purposes of this Act.\nNote:\nThe declaration may also authorise the eligible authority to apply for"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-34-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-34"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-35",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35 Preconditions for declaration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-35"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.151",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister shall not make a declaration under section 34 in\nrelation to an eligible authority of a State unless he or she is\nsatisfied that the law (in this subsection called the relevant law) of\nthat State makes satisfactory provision:\n\n(a) imposing on the chief officer of the eligible authority\nrequirements corresponding to the requirements that\nsection 80 (other than paragraphs 80(f) and (g)) and\nsection 81 (other than paragraph 81(1)(h), and\nsubsection 81(2), so far as that subsection relates to\nparagraph 81(1)(h)) impose on the chief officer of a\nCommonwealth agency; and\n\n(c) requiring the chief officer of the eligible authority to give to a\nspecified Minister (in this subsection called the responsible\nMinister) of that State, within 3 months after a warrant\nissued to the eligible authority ceases to be in force, a written\nreport about:\n\n(i) the use made by the eligible authority of information\nobtained by interceptions under the warrant; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister shall not make a declaration under section 34 in\nrelation to an eligible authority of a State unless he or she is\nsatisfied that the law (in this subsection called the relevant law) of\nthat State makes satisfactory provision:\n\n(a) imposing on the chief officer of the eligible authority\nrequirements corresponding to the requirements that\nsection 80 (other than paragraphs 80(f) and (g)) and\nsection 81 (other than paragraph 81(1)(h), and\nsubsection 81(2), so far as that subsection relates to\nparagraph 81(1)(h)) impose on the chief officer of a\nCommonwealth agency; and\n\n(c) requiring the chief officer of the eligible authority to give to a\nspecified Minister (in this subsection called the responsible\nMinister) of that State, within 3 months after a warrant\nissued to the eligible authority ceases to be in force, a written\nreport about:\n\n(i) the use made by the eligible authority of information\nobtained by interceptions under the warrant; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-35-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-35-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-35-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-35-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-35-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-35-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b7c109fa1f0e672a694eb467ddc6d9d7621a146b6c3cebf83445c53e2b0c7880",
      "skos:note": "The Minister must ensure that a State's law makes satisfactory provision before making a declaration."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-35",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35 Preconditions for declaration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 151,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister shall not make a declaration under section 34 in\nrelation to an eligible authority of a State unless he or she is\nsatisfied that the law (in this subsection called the relevant law) of\nthat State makes satisfactory provision:\n\n(a) imposing on the chief officer of the eligible authority\nrequirements corresponding to the requirements that\nsection 80 (other than paragraphs 80(f) and (g)) and\nsection 81 (other than paragraph 81(1)(h), and\nsubsection 81(2), so far as that subsection relates to\nparagraph 81(1)(h)) impose on the chief officer of a\nCommonwealth agency; and\n\n(c) requiring the chief officer of the eligible authority to give to a\nspecified Minister (in this subsection called the responsible\nMinister) of that State, within 3 months after a warrant\nissued to the eligible authority ceases to be in force, a written\nreport about:\n\n(i) the use made by the eligible authority of information\nobtained by interceptions under the warrant; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
