      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Minister is making a declaration under section 34.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The chief officer of the eligible authority must give a report about the use made by the eligible authority of information obtained by interceptions under the warrant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-36",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36 State laws requiring copies of documents to be given to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-36"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.154",
      "values:originalText": "responsible Minister\n\n(1) Nothing in this Division is to be taken to preclude a law of a State\nfrom requiring the chief officer of the eligible authority to give to a\nspecified Minister (the responsible Minister) of that State a copy\nof each warrant issued to the eligible authority, and of each\ninstrument under section 52 or 57 revoking such a warrant.\n\n(2) If a State makes a law of the kind mentioned in subsection (1),\nthen, for the purposes of section 63AA, the chief officer of the\neligible authority is taken to be communicating interception\nwarrant information for the purposes of this Part by giving\ndocuments to the responsible Minister to comply with the\nrequirement.",
      "skos:definition": "responsible Minister\n\n(1) Nothing in this Division is to be taken to preclude a law of a State\nfrom requiring the chief officer of the eligible authority to give to a\nspecified Minister (the responsible Minister) of that State a copy\nof each warrant issued to the eligible authority, and of each\ninstrument under section 52 or 57 revoking such a warrant.\n\n(2) If a State makes a law of the kind mentioned in subsection (1),\nthen, for the purposes of section 63AA, the chief officer of the\neligible authority is taken to be communicating interception\nwarrant information for the purposes of this Part by giving\ndocuments to the responsible Minister to comply with the\nrequirement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-36-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-36-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "38252a6462c2c5be4951fc122803524123aab454b9ee976a3eddd62bfac616f0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-36",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36 State laws requiring copies of documents to be given to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 154,
      "values:originalText": "responsible Minister\n\n(1) Nothing in this Division is to be taken to preclude a law of a State\nfrom requiring the chief officer of the eligible authority to give to a\nspecified Minister (the responsible Minister) of that State a copy\nof each warrant issued to the eligible authority, and of each\ninstrument under section 52 or 57 revoking such a warrant.\n\n(2) If a State makes a law of the kind mentioned in subsection (1),\nthen, for the purposes of section 63AA, the chief officer of the\neligible authority is taken to be communicating interception\nwarrant information for the purposes of this Part by giving\ndocuments to the responsible Minister to comply with the\nrequirement."
    },
