    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-37",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "37 Revocation of declaration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-37"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.154",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If requested by the Premier of a State to revoke a declaration in\nforce under section 34 in relation to an eligible authority of that\nState, the Minister shall, by notice in writing published in the\nGazette, revoke the declaration.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (1), the Minister may, by notice in writing\npublished in the Gazette, revoke a declaration in force under\nsection 34 in relation to an eligible authority of a State if, and only\nif, the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the law of that State no longer makes satisfactory provision\nin relation to the authority as mentioned in subsection 35(1);\n\n(b) the extent of compliance with a requirement of a law of that\nState, being a requirement of a kind referred to in\nsubsection 35(1), has been unsatisfactory in so far as the\nrequirement relates to the authority;\n\n(c) no agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2),\nbeing an agreement entered into by that State that relates to\nthe authority, is in force;\n\n(d) the extent of compliance by that State with the terms of an\nagreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nDeclaration of State Law Enforcement Authorities as Agencies  Division 2\n\nSection 38\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nan agreement entered into by that State, has been\nunsatisfactory in so far as the agreement relates to the\nauthority; or\n\n(e) the extent of compliance by the chief officer of the authority,\nor by officers of the authority, with this Act has been\nunsatisfactory.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If requested by the Premier of a State to revoke a declaration in\nforce under section 34 in relation to an eligible authority of that\nState, the Minister shall, by notice in writing published in the\nGazette, revoke the declaration.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (1), the Minister may, by notice in writing\npublished in the Gazette, revoke a declaration in force under\nsection 34 in relation to an eligible authority of a State if, and only\nif, the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the law of that State no longer makes satisfactory provision\nin relation to the authority as mentioned in subsection 35(1);\n\n(b) the extent of compliance with a requirement of a law of that\nState, being a requirement of a kind referred to in\nsubsection 35(1), has been unsatisfactory in so far as the\nrequirement relates to the authority;\n\n(c) no agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2),\nbeing an agreement entered into by that State that relates to\nthe authority, is in force;\n\n(d) the extent of compliance by that State with the terms of an\nagreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nDeclaration of State Law Enforcement Authorities as Agencies  Division 2\n\nSection 38\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nan agreement entered into by that State, has been\nunsatisfactory in so far as the agreement relates to the\nauthority; or\n\n(e) the extent of compliance by the chief officer of the authority,\nor by officers of the authority, with this Act has been\nunsatisfactory.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-37-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-37-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "296fc50da203e199e1e5d66ee930053091b3f7067f53097bfc629f8a3c63105a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-37",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "37 Revocation of declaration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 154,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If requested by the Premier of a State to revoke a declaration in\nforce under section 34 in relation to an eligible authority of that\nState, the Minister shall, by notice in writing published in the\nGazette, revoke the declaration.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (1), the Minister may, by notice in writing\npublished in the Gazette, revoke a declaration in force under\nsection 34 in relation to an eligible authority of a State if, and only\nif, the Minister is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the law of that State no longer makes satisfactory provision\nin relation to the authority as mentioned in subsection 35(1);\n\n(b) the extent of compliance with a requirement of a law of that\nState, being a requirement of a kind referred to in\nsubsection 35(1), has been unsatisfactory in so far as the\nrequirement relates to the authority;\n\n(c) no agreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2),\nbeing an agreement entered into by that State that relates to\nthe authority, is in force;\n\n(d) the extent of compliance by that State with the terms of an\nagreement of the kind referred to in subsection 35(2), being\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nDeclaration of State Law Enforcement Authorities as Agencies  Division 2\n\nSection 38\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nan agreement entered into by that State, has been\nunsatisfactory in so far as the agreement relates to the\nauthority; or\n\n(e) the extent of compliance by the chief officer of the authority,\nor by officers of the authority, with this Act has been\nunsatisfactory."
    },
