    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-38a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "38A Agencies authorised to apply for Part 5.3 warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-38a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.155",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a declaration made under section 34 in\nrelation to an eligible authority of a State.\nAuthorisation\n\n(2) When the Minister makes the declaration, the Minister must, in the\ndeclaration, authorise the eligible authority to apply for Part 5.3\nwarrants if:\n\n(a) the Premier of the State requests that the eligible authority be\nso authorised; and\n\n(b) the Minister is satisfied as mentioned in subsection (4) of this\nsection.\n\n(3) The Minister must amend the declaration to authorise the eligible\nauthority to apply for Part 5.3 warrants if:\n\n(a) the declaration does not already so authorise the eligible\nauthority; and\n\n(b) the Premier of the State requests that the eligible authority be\nso authorised; and\n\n(c) the Minister is satisfied as mentioned in subsection (4).\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a declaration made under section 34 in\nrelation to an eligible authority of a State.\nAuthorisation\n\n(2) When the Minister makes the declaration, the Minister must, in the\ndeclaration, authorise the eligible authority to apply for Part 5.3\nwarrants if:\n\n(a) the Premier of the State requests that the eligible authority be\nso authorised; and\n\n(b) the Minister is satisfied as mentioned in subsection (4) of this\nsection.\n\n(3) The Minister must amend the declaration to authorise the eligible\nauthority to apply for Part 5.3 warrants if:\n\n(a) the declaration does not already so authorise the eligible\nauthority; and\n\n(b) the Premier of the State requests that the eligible authority be\nso authorised; and\n\n(c) the Minister is satisfied as mentioned in subsection (4).\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-38a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-38a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-38a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "151cb73eab170160863e4f7cf75e0ff230dbf244c35b7579ca5d603701359fd7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-38a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "38A Agencies authorised to apply for Part 5.3 warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 155,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a declaration made under section 34 in\nrelation to an eligible authority of a State.\nAuthorisation\n\n(2) When the Minister makes the declaration, the Minister must, in the\ndeclaration, authorise the eligible authority to apply for Part 5.3\nwarrants if:\n\n(a) the Premier of the State requests that the eligible authority be\nso authorised; and\n\n(b) the Minister is satisfied as mentioned in subsection (4) of this\nsection.\n\n(3) The Minister must amend the declaration to authorise the eligible\nauthority to apply for Part 5.3 warrants if:\n\n(a) the declaration does not already so authorise the eligible\nauthority; and\n\n(b) the Premier of the State requests that the eligible authority be\nso authorised; and\n\n(c) the Minister is satisfied as mentioned in subsection (4).\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
