    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-39",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "39 Agency may apply for warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-39"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An agency may apply for a warrant in respect of a\ntelecommunications service or a person to:\n\n(a) for an application made by the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission—an eligible Judge; or\n\n(b) otherwise—an eligible Judge or a nominated ART member.\n\n(2) An application for a warrant shall be made on an agency’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the\nAustralian Federal Police; or\n\n(aa) in the case of the National Anti-Corruption Commission:\n\n(i) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or\n\n(ii) a National Anti-Corruption Deputy Commissioner; or\n\n(iii) a staff member of the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission who is authorised in writing by the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commissioner for the\npurposes of this paragraph; or\n\n(b) in the case of the ACC:\n\n(i) the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC or an examiner;\nor\n\n(ii) a member of a police force who is a member of the staff\nof the ACC; or\n\n(c) in the case of the Police Force of a State—an officer of that\nPolice Force; or\n\n(d) in the case of the Crime Commission (NSW):\n\n(i) a member of the Crime Commission (NSW); or\n\n(ii) a member of the staff of the Crime Commission (NSW);\nor\n\n(e) in the case of the Independent Commission Against\nCorruption (NSW)—an officer of the Independent\nCommission Against Corruption (NSW); or\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nApplications for warrants  Division 3\n\nSection 40\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ea) in the case of the IBAC (Vic.)—an IBAC (Vic.) officer; or\n\n(f) in the case of the Crime and Corruption Commission (Qld)—\na commission officer (within the meaning of the Crime and\nCorruption Act (Qld)); or\n\n(g) in the case of the Law Enforcement Conduct Commission\n(NSW):\n\n(i) the Chief Commissioner of the Commission; or\n\n(ii) the Commissioner for Integrity of the Commission; or\n\n(iii) an Assistant Commissioner of the Commission; or\n\n(iv) a member of the staff of the Law Enforcement Conduct\nCommission (NSW); or\n\n(i) in the case of the Corruption and Crime Commission\n(WA)—an officer of the Corruption and Crime Commission\n(WA); or\n\n(j) in the case of the Independent Commission Against\nCorruption (SA):\n\n(i) the Commissioner of the Independent Commission\nAgainst Corruption (SA); or\n\n(ii) the Deputy Commissioner of the Independent\nCommission Against Corruption (SA); or\n\n(iii) a member of the staff of the Independent Commission\nAgainst Corruption (SA).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An agency may apply for a warrant in respect of a\ntelecommunications service or a person to:\n\n(a) for an application made by the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission—an eligible Judge; or\n\n(b) otherwise—an eligible Judge or a nominated ART member.\n\n(2) An application for a warrant shall be made on an agency’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in the case of the Australian Federal Police—a member of the\nAustralian Federal Police; or\n\n(aa) in the case of the National Anti-Corruption Commission:\n\n(i) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or\n\n(ii) a National Anti-Corruption Deputy Commissioner; or\n\n(iii) a staff member of the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission who is authorised in writing by the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commissioner for the\npurposes of this paragraph; or\n\n(b) in the case of the ACC:\n\n(i) the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC or an examiner;\nor\n\n(ii) a member of a police force who is a member of the staff\nof the ACC; or\n\n(c) in the case of the Police Force of a State—an officer of that\nPolice Force; or\n\n(d) in the case of the Crime Commission (NSW):\n\n(i) a member of the Crime Commission (NSW); or\n\n(ii) a member of the staff of the Crime Commission (NSW);\nor\n\n(e) in the case of the Independent Commission Against\nCorruption (NSW)—an officer of the Independent\nCommission Against Corruption (NSW); or\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nApplications for warrants  Division 3\n\nSection 40\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ea) in the case of the IBAC (Vic.)—an IBAC (Vic.) officer; or\n\n(f) in the case of the Crime and Corruption Commission (Qld)—\na commission officer (within the meaning of the Crime and\nCorruption Act (Qld)); or\n\n(g) in the case of the Law Enforcement Conduct Commission\n(NSW):\n\n(i) the Chief Commissioner of the Commission; or\n\n(ii) the Commissioner for Integrity of the Commission; or\n\n(iii) an Assistant Commissioner of th",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-39-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-39-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "094d2c37744455d4634de5c06a17b2eedb3e171620f9a5ebdb95c841d0e334b3"
    },
