    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-40",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40 Form of application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-40"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.161",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an application for a warrant shall be in\nwriting.\n\n(2) If the person making an application for a warrant on an agency’s\nbehalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an application for a warrant shall be in\nwriting.\n\n(2) If the person making an application for a warrant on an agency’s\nbehalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-40-ss-1"
        },
        {
