      "cml:integrityHash": "2f7a386bc051a0defd7767facc41304dd79f79a9018013ff6efff68ed5b250af",
      "skos:note": "Permits telephone application under urgent circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-40-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40(2) Form of application",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 161,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the person making an application for a warrant on an agency’s\nbehalf:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone;\nthe person may make the application by telephone.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
