      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 164,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A Victorian PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe Judge or nominated ART member about the following matters:\n\n(a) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a\ntelecommunications service—the matters mentioned in\nparagraphs 46(2)(a) to (f), 46(5)(a) to (gb), 46(8)(a) to (e),\n46(10)(a) to (h) or 46(13)(a) to (e), as the case requires;\n\n(b) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a\nperson—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46A(2)(a) to\n(f), 46A(2B)(a) to (gb), 46A(2D)(a) to (e), 46A(2F)(a) to (h)\nor 46A(2H)(a) to (e), as the case requires.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nApplications for warrants  Division 3\n\nSection 45\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPIM may question certain persons"
    },
