    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-44a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44A(3) Application by interception agency of Victoria",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-44a-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.164",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Victorian PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subsection (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the warrant on the\ninterception agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under section 44, is required by the Judge or\nnominated ART member to give further information to the\nJudge or nominated ART member in connection with the\napplication.\nHowever, the Victorian PIM may only do so in the presence of the\neligible Judge or nominated ART member.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The Victorian PIM may, for the purpose of making submissions\nunder subsection (2), question:\n\n(a) the person making the application for the warrant on the\ninterception agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person who, under section 44, is required by the Judge or\nnominated ART member to give further information to the\nJudge or nominated ART member in connection with the\napplication.\nHowever, the Victorian PIM may only do so in the presence of the\neligible Judge or nominated ART member.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-44a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
