    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-45",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45 Application by interception agency of Queensland",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-45"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.165",
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an interception agency of Queensland\napplies, under section 39, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART\nmember for a warrant in respect of a telecommunications service or\na person.\nPIM may make submissions\n\n(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe Judge or nominated ART member about the following matters:\n\n(a) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a\ntelecommunications service—the matters mentioned in\nparagraphs 46(2)(a) to (f), 46(5)(a) to (gb), 46(8)(a) to (e),\n46(10)(a) to (h) or 46(13)(a) to (e), as the case requires;\n\n(b) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a\nperson—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46A(2)(a) to\n(f), 46A(2B)(a) to (gb), 46A(2D)(a) to (e), 46A(2F)(a) to (h)\nor 46A(2H)(a) to (e), as the case requires.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an interception agency of Queensland\napplies, under section 39, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART\nmember for a warrant in respect of a telecommunications service or\na person.\nPIM may make submissions\n\n(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe Judge or nominated ART member about the following matters:\n\n(a) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a\ntelecommunications service—the matters mentioned in\nparagraphs 46(2)(a) to (f), 46(5)(a) to (gb), 46(8)(a) to (e),\n46(10)(a) to (h) or 46(13)(a) to (e), as the case requires;\n\n(b) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a\nperson—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46A(2)(a) to\n(f), 46A(2B)(a) to (gb), 46A(2D)(a) to (e), 46A(2F)(a) to (h)\nor 46A(2H)(a) to (e), as the case requires.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-45-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-45-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-45",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45 Application by interception agency of Queensland",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 165,
      "values:originalText": "Scope\n\n(1) This section applies if an interception agency of Queensland\napplies, under section 39, to an eligible Judge or nominated ART\nmember for a warrant in respect of a telecommunications service or\na person.\nPIM may make submissions\n\n(2) A Queensland PIM may, orally or in writing, make submissions to\nthe Judge or nominated ART member about the following matters:\n\n(a) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a\ntelecommunications service—the matters mentioned in\nparagraphs 46(2)(a) to (f), 46(5)(a) to (gb), 46(8)(a) to (e),\n46(10)(a) to (h) or 46(13)(a) to (e), as the case requires;\n\n(b) in relation to an application for a warrant in respect of a\nperson—the matters mentioned in paragraphs 46A(2)(a) to\n(f), 46A(2B)(a) to (gb), 46A(2D)(a) to (e), 46A(2F)(a) to (h)\nor 46A(2H)(a) to (e), as the case requires.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
