    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-47",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47 Limit on authority conferred by warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-47"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.192",
      "values:originalText": "A warrant issued under section 46 or 46A does not authorise the\ninterception of communications passing over a telecommunications\nsystem that a carrier operates unless:\n\n(a) notification of the issue of the warrant has been received by\nan authorised representative of the carrier under\nsubsection 60(1); and\n\n(b) the interception takes place as a result of action taken by an\nemployee of the carrier.",
      "skos:definition": "A warrant issued under section 46 or 46A does not authorise the\ninterception of communications passing over a telecommunications\nsystem that a carrier operates unless:\n\n(a) notification of the issue of the warrant has been received by\nan authorised representative of the carrier under\nsubsection 60(1); and\n\n(b) the interception takes place as a result of action taken by an\nemployee of the carrier.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-47-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-47-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d2538fe498a8debe2115d2de3d96a543e6ee9baf5bb1e0927145fe3fe8bfda6d",
      "skos:note": "Limit on warrant authority for telecommunications interception"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-47",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47 Limit on authority conferred by warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 192,
      "values:originalText": "A warrant issued under section 46 or 46A does not authorise the\ninterception of communications passing over a telecommunications\nsystem that a carrier operates unless:\n\n(a) notification of the issue of the warrant has been received by\nan authorised representative of the carrier under\nsubsection 60(1); and\n\n(b) the interception takes place as a result of action taken by an\nemployee of the carrier."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-47-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-47"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-47-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "forbid",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits warrant-based interception without carrier notification",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Notification required for warrant issuance",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Interception prohibited"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-48",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48 Issue of warrant for entry on premises",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-48"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.192",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an agency could apply for a warrant under section 46\n(authorising interceptions of communications to or from a service),\nit may instead apply for a warrant under this section that also\nauthorises entry on premises. The agency does so by including in\nthe application that would otherwise have been made under\nsection 46 a request that the warrant also authorise entry on\nspecified premises.\nNote 1\nOnly a Part 5.3 warrant agency may apply for a warrant under\nsection 46 in the circumstances mentioned in subsection 46(4) or (7).\nNote 2:\nOnly a Part 9.10 warrant agency may apply for a warrant under\nsection 46 in the circumstances mentioned in subsection 46(9) or (12).\n\n(2) Where a written application for a warrant includes a request that\nthe warrant authorise entry on specified premises, an affidavit\naccompanying the application shall:\n\n(a) state why it is considered necessary for the warrant to\nauthorise entry on those premises;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 48\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) set out the number of previous applications (if any) for\nwarrants that the agency has made and that requested\nauthorisation of entry on those premises; and\n\n(c) set out the number of warrants (if any) previously issued on\nsuch application.\n\n(3) Where:\n\n(a) an agency applies under this section to an eligible Judge or\nnominated ART member for a warrant in respect of a\ntelecommunications service; and\n\n(b) the Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied that\nsubsection (2) has been complied with in relation to the\napplication; and\n\n(c) section 46 would empower the Judge or nominated ART\nmember to issue a warrant if the application had been made\nunder either of those sections; and\n\n(ca) Division 3 has been complied with in relation to the\napplication; and\n\n(d) the Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied, on the\nbasis of the information given to the Judge or nominated\nART member under this Part in connection with the\napplication, that:\n\n(i) for technical reasons connected with the nature or\noperation of the service or of a telecommunications\nsystem of which the service forms a part; or\n\n(ii) where, if the warrant were issued under section 46,\ncommunications to or from the telecommunications\nservice would be intercepted while passing over a\ntelecommunications system operated by a carrier—\nexecution of the warrant as a result of action taken by\nemployees of that carrier might jeopardise security of\nthe investigation by the agency of a serious offence in\nwhich a person to whom the application relates is\ninvolved or, in the case of a warrant issued in the\ncircumstances mentioned in subsection 46(4) or (9),\nmight jeopardise the achievement of an objective for\nwhich the warrant was issued;\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an agency could apply for a warrant under section 46\n(authorising interceptions of communications to or from a service),\nit may instead apply for a warrant under this section that also\nauthorises entry on premises. The agency does so by including in\nthe application that would otherwise have been made under\nsection 46 a request that the warrant also authorise entry on\nspecified premises.\nNote 1\nOnly a Part 5.3 warrant agency may apply for a warrant under\nsection 46 in the circumstances mentioned in subsection 46(4) or (7).\nNote 2:\nOnly a Part 9.10 warrant agency may apply for a warrant under\nsection 46 in the circumstances mentioned in subsection 46(9) or (12).\n\n(2) Where a written application for a warrant includes a request that\nthe warrant authorise entry on specified premises, an affidavit\naccompanying the application shall:\n\n(a) state why it is considered necessary for the warrant to\nauthorise entry on those premises;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 48\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) set out the number of previous applications (if any) for\nwarrants that the agency has made and that requested\nauthorisation of entry on those premises; and\n\n(c) set out the number of warrants (if any) previously issued on\nsuch application.\n\n(3) Where:\n\n(a) an agency applies under this section to an eligible Judge or\nnominated ART member for a warrant in respect of a\ntelecommunications service; and\n\n(b) the Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied that\nsubsection (2) has been complied with in relation to the\napplication; and\n\n(c) section 46 would empower the Judge or nominated ART\nmember to issue a warrant if the application had been made\nunder either of those sections; and\n\n(ca) Division 3 has been complied with in relation to the\napplication; and\n\n(d) the Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied, on",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-48-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-48-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-48-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5d1671469c7b77c1ebe5e60c5428596426508194ae380b2b89890ca3120bd592"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-48",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48 Issue of warrant for entry on premises",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 192,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an agency could apply for a warrant under section 46\n(authorising interceptions of communications to or from a service),\nit may instead apply for a warrant under this section that also\nauthorises entry on premises. The agency does so by including in\nthe application that would otherwise have been made under\nsection 46 a request that the warrant also authorise entry on\nspecified premises.\nNote 1\nOnly a Part 5.3 warrant agency may apply for a warrant under\nsection 46 in the circumstances mentioned in subsection 46(4) or (7).\nNote 2:\nOnly a Part 9.10 warrant agency may apply for a warrant under\nsection 46 in the circumstances mentioned in subsection 46(9) or (12).\n\n(2) Where a written application for a warrant includes a request that\nthe warrant authorise entry on specified premises, an affidavit\naccompanying the application shall:\n\n(a) state why it is considered necessary for the warrant to\nauthorise entry on those premises;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 48\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) set out the number of previous applications (if any) for\nwarrants that the agency has made and that requested\nauthorisation of entry on those premises; and\n\n(c) set out the number of warrants (if any) previously issued on\nsuch application.\n\n(3) Where:\n\n(a) an agency applies under this section to an eligible Judge or\nnominated ART member for a warrant in respect of a\ntelecommunications service; and\n\n(b) the Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied that\nsubsection (2) has been complied with in relation to the\napplication; and\n\n(c) section 46 would empower the Judge or nominated ART\nmember to issue a warrant if the application had been made\nunder either of those sections; and\n\n(ca) Division 3 has been complied with in relation to the\napplication; and\n\n(d) the Judge or nominated ART member is satisfied, on the\nbasis of the information given to the Judge or nominated\nART member under this Part in connection with the\napplication, that:\n\n(i) for technical reasons connected with the nature or\noperation of the service or of a telecommunications\nsystem of which the service forms a part; or\n\n(ii) where, if the warrant were issued under section 46,\ncommunications to or from the telecommunications\nservice would be intercepted while passing over a\ntelecommunications system operated by a carrier—\nexecution of the warrant as a result of action taken by\nemployees of that carrier might jeopardise security of\nthe investigation by the agency of a serious offence in\nwhich a person to whom the application relates is\ninvolved or, in the case of a warrant issued in the\ncircumstances mentioned in subsection 46(4) or (9),\nmight jeopardise the achievement of an objective for\nwhich the warrant was issued;\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
