    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49-ss-6a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49(6A) Form and content of warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-49-ss-6a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.194",
      "values:originalText": "(6A) To avoid doubt, a warrant issued on the basis that a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order is in force remains in force for the period\nmentioned in subsection (3) even if the order ceases to be in force,\nprovided that the order is replaced by a succeeding Part 5.3\nsupervisory order.\nNote 1:\nIf there is no succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, the warrant must\nbe revoked (see section 57).\nNote 2:\nA control order is not a succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in\nrelation to an extended supervision order, and vice versa (see\nsection 6U).",
      "skos:definition": "(6A) To avoid doubt, a warrant issued on the basis that a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order is in force remains in force for the period\nmentioned in subsection (3) even if the order ceases to be in force,\nprovided that the order is replaced by a succeeding Part 5.3\nsupervisory order.\nNote 1:\nIf there is no succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, the warrant must\nbe revoked (see section 57).\nNote 2:\nA control order is not a succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in\nrelation to an extended supervision order, and vice versa (see\nsection 6U).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49-ss-6a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49-ss-6a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49-ss-6a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49-ss-6a-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49-ss-6a-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49-ss-6a-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8058c52e5aeb25b283926655b2bcde8b895397840413148119c5df9dfab73ea7",
      "skos:note": "Warrant remains in force despite changes to supervisory order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-49-ss-6a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49(6A) Form and content of warrant",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 194,
      "values:originalText": "(6A) To avoid doubt, a warrant issued on the basis that a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order is in force remains in force for the period\nmentioned in subsection (3) even if the order ceases to be in force,\nprovided that the order is replaced by a succeeding Part 5.3\nsupervisory order.\nNote 1:\nIf there is no succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, the warrant must\nbe revoked (see section 57).\nNote 2:\nA control order is not a succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order in\nrelation to an extended supervision order, and vice versa (see\nsection 6U)."
    },
    {
