    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49-ss-6b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49(6B) Form and content of warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-49-ss-6b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.194",
      "values:originalText": "(6B) To avoid doubt, a warrant issued on the basis that a community\nsafety supervision order is in force remains in force for the period\nmentioned in subsection (3) even if the order ceases to be in force,\nprovided that the order is replaced by a succeeding community\nsafety supervision order.\nNote:\nIf there is no succeeding community safety supervision order, the\nwarrant must be revoked (see section 57).\nParticulars of serious offences",
      "skos:definition": "(6B) To avoid doubt, a warrant issued on the basis that a community\nsafety supervision order is in force remains in force for the period\nmentioned in subsection (3) even if the order ceases to be in force,\nprovided that the order is replaced by a succeeding community\nsafety supervision order.\nNote:\nIf there is no succeeding community safety supervision order, the\nwarrant must be revoked (see section 57).\nParticulars of serious offences",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-49"
      },
