    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-52",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52 Judge or nominated ART member may revoke warrant where",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-52"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.198",
      "values:originalText": "section 51 contravened\n\n(1) Where a Judge or nominated ART member who issued a warrant\non a telephone application is satisfied that section 51 has not been\ncomplied with in relation to the warrant, he or she may, by writing\nsigned by him or her, revoke the warrant and shall, if he or she\ndoes so:\n\n(a) immediately inform:\n\n(i) the person who made the application on the agency’s\nbehalf; or\n\n(ii) the chief officer of the agency;\n\nof the revocation; and\n\n(b) give the instrument of revocation to that person, or to the\nchief officer, as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) Where a warrant issued to an agency is revoked under\nsubsection (1), the chief officer of the agency must, as soon as\npracticable, give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the\nSecretary of the Department.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a warrant has been issued to an agency; and\n\n(b) another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority\nunder that warrant (see section 55); and\n\n(c) the warrant is revoked under subsection (1);\nthe chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued\nmust:\n\n(d) immediately inform the chief officer of the other agency or\nthe Director-General of Security (as the case requires) of the\nrevocation; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 54\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(e) give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the person\nreferred to in paragraph (d) as soon as practicable.",
      "skos:definition": "section 51 contravened\n\n(1) Where a Judge or nominated ART member who issued a warrant\non a telephone application is satisfied that section 51 has not been\ncomplied with in relation to the warrant, he or she may, by writing\nsigned by him or her, revoke the warrant and shall, if he or she\ndoes so:\n\n(a) immediately inform:\n\n(i) the person who made the application on the agency’s\nbehalf; or\n\n(ii) the chief officer of the agency;\n\nof the revocation; and\n\n(b) give the instrument of revocation to that person, or to the\nchief officer, as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) Where a warrant issued to an agency is revoked under\nsubsection (1), the chief officer of the agency must, as soon as\npracticable, give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the\nSecretary of the Department.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a warrant has been issued to an agency; and\n\n(b) another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority\nunder that warrant (see section 55); and\n\n(c) the warrant is revoked under subsection (1);\nthe chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued\nmust:\n\n(d) immediately inform the chief officer of the other agency or\nthe Director-General of Security (as the case requires) of the\nrevocation; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 54\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(e) give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the person\nreferred to in paragraph (d) as soon as practicable.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-52-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-52-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-52-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0537e926f2a4ef963a87e9b9ad5ccf8ea7a24b3358a369d2064ea73379c9817e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-52",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52 Judge or nominated ART member may revoke warrant where",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 198,
      "values:originalText": "section 51 contravened\n\n(1) Where a Judge or nominated ART member who issued a warrant\non a telephone application is satisfied that section 51 has not been\ncomplied with in relation to the warrant, he or she may, by writing\nsigned by him or her, revoke the warrant and shall, if he or she\ndoes so:\n\n(a) immediately inform:\n\n(i) the person who made the application on the agency’s\nbehalf; or\n\n(ii) the chief officer of the agency;\n\nof the revocation; and\n\n(b) give the instrument of revocation to that person, or to the\nchief officer, as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) Where a warrant issued to an agency is revoked under\nsubsection (1), the chief officer of the agency must, as soon as\npracticable, give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the\nSecretary of the Department.\n\n(3) If:\n\n(a) a warrant has been issued to an agency; and\n\n(b) another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority\nunder that warrant (see section 55); and\n\n(c) the warrant is revoked under subsection (1);\nthe chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued\nmust:\n\n(d) immediately inform the chief officer of the other agency or\nthe Director-General of Security (as the case requires) of the\nrevocation; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 54\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(e) give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the person\nreferred to in paragraph (d) as soon as practicable."
    },
