      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.198",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n\n(a) a warrant has been issued to an agency; and\n\n(b) another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority\nunder that warrant (see section 55); and\n\n(c) the warrant is revoked under subsection (1);\nthe chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued\nmust:\n\n(d) immediately inform the chief officer of the other agency or\nthe Director-General of Security (as the case requires) of the\nrevocation; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 54\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(e) give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the person\nreferred to in paragraph (d) as soon as practicable.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If:\n\n(a) a warrant has been issued to an agency; and\n\n(b) another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority\nunder that warrant (see section 55); and\n\n(c) the warrant is revoked under subsection (1);\nthe chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued\nmust:\n\n(d) immediately inform the chief officer of the other agency or\nthe Director-General of Security (as the case requires) of the\nrevocation; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 54\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(e) give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the person\nreferred to in paragraph (d) as soon as practicable.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-52"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-52-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-52-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2a495fc3cfa115c5f32ddf5edabeabfb6e609ed1a7301f66ea37e4d5fdf83757",
      "skos:note": "Inform other agency or Director-General of Security about warrant revocation.",
      "dc:description": "Copy of instrument of revocation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-52-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52(3) Judge or nominated ART member may revoke warrant where",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 198,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n\n(a) a warrant has been issued to an agency; and\n\n(b) another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority\nunder that warrant (see section 55); and\n\n(c) the warrant is revoked under subsection (1);\nthe chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued\nmust:\n\n(d) immediately inform the chief officer of the other agency or\nthe Director-General of Security (as the case requires) of the\nrevocation; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 54\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(e) give a copy of the instrument of revocation to the person\nreferred to in paragraph (d) as soon as practicable."
    },
