    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-55",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55 Exercise of authority conferred by warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-55"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.199",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The authority conferred by a Part 2-5 warrant may only be\nexercised by a person in relation to whom an approval under\nsubsection (3) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\n(3) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in\nrelation to whom an appointment under subsection (4) is in force,\nmay approve any of the following persons to exercise the authority\nconferred by warrants (or classes of warrants) issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers (or classes of officers) of the agency or another\nagency;\n\n(b) staff members (or classes of staff members) of the agency or\nanother agency;\n\n(c) ASIO employees (or classes of ASIO employees);\n\n(d) persons assisting the Organisation in the performance of its\nfunctions.\n\n(4) The chief officer of an agency may appoint in writing an officer of\nthe agency to be an approving officer for the purposes of\nsubsection (3).\n\n(5) In spite of subsection (1), a designated officer, or an employee of a\ncarrier, may provide technical assistance to a person who is\nexercising the authority conferred by a warrant.\n\n(6) A reference in subsection (5) to the provision of technical\nassistance includes a reference to:\n\n(a) the doing of any act involved in the interception of a\ncommunication under a warrant, to the extent that the act is\nincidental to the doing of an act referred to in paragraph (b);\nand\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The authority conferred by a Part 2-5 warrant may only be\nexercised by a person in relation to whom an approval under\nsubsection (3) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\n(3) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in\nrelation to whom an appointment under subsection (4) is in force,\nmay approve any of the following persons to exercise the authority\nconferred by warrants (or classes of warrants) issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers (or classes of officers) of the agency or another\nagency;\n\n(b) staff members (or classes of staff members) of the agency or\nanother agency;\n\n(c) ASIO employees (or classes of ASIO employees);\n\n(d) persons assisting the Organisation in the performance of its\nfunctions.\n\n(4) The chief officer of an agency may appoint in writing an officer of\nthe agency to be an approving officer for the purposes of\nsubsection (3).\n\n(5) In spite of subsection (1), a designated officer, or an employee of a\ncarrier, may provide technical assistance to a person who is\nexercising the authority conferred by a warrant.\n\n(6) A reference in subsection (5) to the provision of technical\nassistance includes a reference to:\n\n(a) the doing of any act involved in the interception of a\ncommunication under a warrant, to the extent that the act is\nincidental to the doing of an act referred to in paragraph (b);\nand\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-55-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-55-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-55-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-55-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-55-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a7c196b9369324cb29396a4fcddf8ac6a1551164473184a8036683f7480ca8f7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-55",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55 Exercise of authority conferred by warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 199,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The authority conferred by a Part 2-5 warrant may only be\nexercised by a person in relation to whom an approval under\nsubsection (3) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\n(3) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in\nrelation to whom an appointment under subsection (4) is in force,\nmay approve any of the following persons to exercise the authority\nconferred by warrants (or classes of warrants) issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers (or classes of officers) of the agency or another\nagency;\n\n(b) staff members (or classes of staff members) of the agency or\nanother agency;\n\n(c) ASIO employees (or classes of ASIO employees);\n\n(d) persons assisting the Organisation in the performance of its\nfunctions.\n\n(4) The chief officer of an agency may appoint in writing an officer of\nthe agency to be an approving officer for the purposes of\nsubsection (3).\n\n(5) In spite of subsection (1), a designated officer, or an employee of a\ncarrier, may provide technical assistance to a person who is\nexercising the authority conferred by a warrant.\n\n(6) A reference in subsection (5) to the provision of technical\nassistance includes a reference to:\n\n(a) the doing of any act involved in the interception of a\ncommunication under a warrant, to the extent that the act is\nincidental to the doing of an act referred to in paragraph (b);\nand\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
