    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57 Revocation of warrant by chief officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-57"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.200",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an agency:\n\n(a) may, at any time, by signed writing, revoke a warrant issued\nto the agency; and\n\n(b) must do so, if he or she is satisfied that the grounds on which\nthe warrant was issued to the agency have ceased to exist.\n\n(2) If another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority under\nthe warrant, then before revoking the warrant, the chief officer\nmust inform the chief officer of the other agency or the\nDirector-General of Security (as the case requires) of the proposed\nrevocation.\n\n(3) After revoking the warrant, the chief officer must:\n\n(a) if subsection (2) applies—immediately inform the chief\nofficer of the other agency or the Director-General of\nSecurity (as the case requires) of the revocation; and\n\n(b) in any case—give a copy of the instrument of revocation to\nthe Secretary of the Department as soon as practicable.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 58\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The chief officer of an agency may delegate his or her power under\nparagraph (1)(a) to a certifying officer of the agency.\n\n(5) This section does not apply in relation to a warrant that has ceased\nto be in force.\n\n(6) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order warrant issued on the ground that a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order was in force, that ground is taken to have ceased\nto exist if, and only if, neither that Part 5.3 supervisory order, nor\nany succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, is in force.\n\n(7) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a\ncommunity safety supervision order warrant issued on the ground\nthat a community safety supervision order was in force, that\nground is taken to have ceased to exist if, and only if, neither that\ncommunity safety supervision order, nor any succeeding\ncommunity safety supervision order, is in force.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of an agency:\n\n(a) may, at any time, by signed writing, revoke a warrant issued\nto the agency; and\n\n(b) must do so, if he or she is satisfied that the grounds on which\nthe warrant was issued to the agency have ceased to exist.\n\n(2) If another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority under\nthe warrant, then before revoking the warrant, the chief officer\nmust inform the chief officer of the other agency or the\nDirector-General of Security (as the case requires) of the proposed\nrevocation.\n\n(3) After revoking the warrant, the chief officer must:\n\n(a) if subsection (2) applies—immediately inform the chief\nofficer of the other agency or the Director-General of\nSecurity (as the case requires) of the revocation; and\n\n(b) in any case—give a copy of the instrument of revocation to\nthe Secretary of the Department as soon as practicable.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 58\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The chief officer of an agency may delegate his or her power under\nparagraph (1)(a) to a certifying officer of the agency.\n\n(5) This section does not apply in relation to a warrant that has ceased\nto be in force.\n\n(6) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order warrant issued on the ground that a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order was in force, that ground is taken to have ceased\nto exist if, and only if, neither that Part 5.3 supervisory order, nor\nany succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, is in force.\n\n(7) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a\ncommunity safety supervision order warrant issued on the ground\nthat a community safety supervision order was in force, that\nground is taken to have ceased to exist if, and only if, neither that\ncommunity safety supervision order, nor any succeeding\ncommunity safety supervision ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "19a7e9624886905861eab95db6d6590483522ae9b062ca246c1fec37c6b7844f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-57",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57 Revocation of warrant by chief officer",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 200,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an agency:\n\n(a) may, at any time, by signed writing, revoke a warrant issued\nto the agency; and\n\n(b) must do so, if he or she is satisfied that the grounds on which\nthe warrant was issued to the agency have ceased to exist.\n\n(2) If another agency or the Organisation is exercising authority under\nthe warrant, then before revoking the warrant, the chief officer\nmust inform the chief officer of the other agency or the\nDirector-General of Security (as the case requires) of the proposed\nrevocation.\n\n(3) After revoking the warrant, the chief officer must:\n\n(a) if subsection (2) applies—immediately inform the chief\nofficer of the other agency or the Director-General of\nSecurity (as the case requires) of the revocation; and\n\n(b) in any case—give a copy of the instrument of revocation to\nthe Secretary of the Department as soon as practicable.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 58\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The chief officer of an agency may delegate his or her power under\nparagraph (1)(a) to a certifying officer of the agency.\n\n(5) This section does not apply in relation to a warrant that has ceased\nto be in force.\n\n(6) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order warrant issued on the ground that a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order was in force, that ground is taken to have ceased\nto exist if, and only if, neither that Part 5.3 supervisory order, nor\nany succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, is in force.\n\n(7) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a\ncommunity safety supervision order warrant issued on the ground\nthat a community safety supervision order was in force, that\nground is taken to have ceased to exist if, and only if, neither that\ncommunity safety supervision order, nor any succeeding\ncommunity safety supervision order, is in force."
    },
