    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57(3) Revocation of warrant by chief officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-57-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.200",
      "values:originalText": "(3) After revoking the warrant, the chief officer must:\n\n(a) if subsection (2) applies—immediately inform the chief\nofficer of the other agency or the Director-General of\nSecurity (as the case requires) of the revocation; and\n\n(b) in any case—give a copy of the instrument of revocation to\nthe Secretary of the Department as soon as practicable.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 58\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) After revoking the warrant, the chief officer must:\n\n(a) if subsection (2) applies—immediately inform the chief\nofficer of the other agency or the Director-General of\nSecurity (as the case requires) of the revocation; and\n\n(b) in any case—give a copy of the instrument of revocation to\nthe Secretary of the Department as soon as practicable.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 58\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "919fdc9759daf5e001398bab8ba9c91865d3c032c6f1c3808e5af1713517f8d0",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must inform and provide revocation instrument.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-57-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57(3) Revocation of warrant by chief officer",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 200,
      "values:originalText": "(3) After revoking the warrant, the chief officer must:\n\n(a) if subsection (2) applies—immediately inform the chief\nofficer of the other agency or the Director-General of\nSecurity (as the case requires) of the revocation; and\n\n(b) in any case—give a copy of the instrument of revocation to\nthe Secretary of the Department as soon as practicable.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 58\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
