    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57(6) Revocation of warrant by chief officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-57-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.200",
      "values:originalText": "(6) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order warrant issued on the ground that a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order was in force, that ground is taken to have ceased\nto exist if, and only if, neither that Part 5.3 supervisory order, nor\nany succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, is in force.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order warrant issued on the ground that a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order was in force, that ground is taken to have ceased\nto exist if, and only if, neither that Part 5.3 supervisory order, nor\nany succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, is in force.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-57-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6c93f26c1029b313481f6a53d632398622e0ff57c43e1815e53b7e977016730e",
      "skos:note": "Ground ceases to exist if no Part 5.3 supervisory order is in force."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-57-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57(6) Revocation of warrant by chief officer",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 200,
      "values:originalText": "(6) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order warrant issued on the ground that a Part 5.3\nsupervisory order was in force, that ground is taken to have ceased\nto exist if, and only if, neither that Part 5.3 supervisory order, nor\nany succeeding Part 5.3 supervisory order, is in force."
    },
