        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8d15134cde30881cbc744a21cc08ed89533efc45afef95947cae7d6c402b2b25",
      "skos:note": "Revocation of warrant by chief officer"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-57-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57(7) Revocation of warrant by chief officer",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 200,
      "values:originalText": "(7) For the purposes of the application of subsection (1) to a\ncommunity safety supervision order warrant issued on the ground\nthat a community safety supervision order was in force, that\nground is taken to have ceased to exist if, and only if, neither that\ncommunity safety supervision order, nor any succeeding\ncommunity safety supervision order, is in force."
    },
