    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-59a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59A Notification to Secretary of the Department",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-59a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.202",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a Part 2-5 warrant is issued to an agency, the chief officer of\nthe agency must cause a copy of the warrant to be given to the\nSecretary of the Department as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) Where:\n\n(a) it is proposed, under a warrant issued under section 46A, to\nintercept communications made to or from a\ntelecommunications service; and\n\n(b) the warrant is not a warrant that authorises interception of\ncommunications made by means of a telecommunications\ndevice or telecommunications devices identified in the\nwarrant; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\nthe chief officer must cause the Secretary of the Department to be\ngiven, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the service\nsufficient to identify it.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a Part 2-5 warrant is issued to an agency, the chief officer of\nthe agency must cause a copy of the warrant to be given to the\nSecretary of the Department as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) Where:\n\n(a) it is proposed, under a warrant issued under section 46A, to\nintercept communications made to or from a\ntelecommunications service; and\n\n(b) the warrant is not a warrant that authorises interception of\ncommunications made by means of a telecommunications\ndevice or telecommunications devices identified in the\nwarrant; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\nthe chief officer must cause the Secretary of the Department to be\ngiven, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the service\nsufficient to identify it.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-59a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-59a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ff98c512d039cafa362b7b1948a3e0d8672782cf9c996e83911fc246eb03b9e2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-59a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59A Notification to Secretary of the Department",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 202,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a Part 2-5 warrant is issued to an agency, the chief officer of\nthe agency must cause a copy of the warrant to be given to the\nSecretary of the Department as soon as practicable.\n\n(2) Where:\n\n(a) it is proposed, under a warrant issued under section 46A, to\nintercept communications made to or from a\ntelecommunications service; and\n\n(b) the warrant is not a warrant that authorises interception of\ncommunications made by means of a telecommunications\ndevice or telecommunications devices identified in the\nwarrant; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\nthe chief officer must cause the Secretary of the Department to be\ngiven, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the service\nsufficient to identify it."
    },
