    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-59b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59B Notification to Ombudsman or Inspector-General of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 202,
      "values:originalText": "Intelligence and Security in relation to Part 5.3 warrants\n\n(1) Within 6 months after a Part 5.3 warrant is issued in response to an\napplication by a Commonwealth agency, the chief officer of the\nagency must:\n\n(a) if the agency is the ACC:\n\n(i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nthat the warrant has been issued; and\n\n(ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity a copy of the warrant; and\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) notify the Ombudsman that the warrant has been issued;\nand\n\n(ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the warrant.\n\n(2) As soon as practicable after an officer of the agency contravenes\nany of the following conditions, restrictions or provisions, the chief\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 59C\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nofficer of the agency must notify the Ombudsman or the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security (as the case\nrequires) of the contravention:\n\n(a) a condition or restriction specified in the warrant under\nsubsection 49(2);\n\n(b) the following provisions, to the extent that they apply to the\nwarrant:\n\n(i) paragraph 57(1)(b);\n\n(ii) subsection 63(1);\n\n(iii) subsection 63(2);\n\n(iv) section 79;\n\n(c) section 79AA;\n\n(d) subsection 103B(4).\n\n(3) A failure to comply with subsection (1) or (2) does not affect the\nvalidity of the warrant."
    },
