      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59C(1) Notification to Ombudsman or Inspector-General of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-59c-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.203",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Within 6 months after a Part 9.10 warrant is issued in response to\nan application by a Commonwealth agency, the chief officer of the\nagency must:\n\n(a) if the agency is the ACC:\n\n(i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nthat the warrant has been issued; and\n\n(ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity a copy of the warrant; and\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) notify the Ombudsman that the warrant has been issued;\nand\n\n(ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the warrant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Within 6 months after a Part 9.10 warrant is issued in response to\nan application by a Commonwealth agency, the chief officer of the\nagency must:\n\n(a) if the agency is the ACC:\n\n(i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nthat the warrant has been issued; and\n\n(ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity a copy of the warrant; and\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) notify the Ombudsman that the warrant has been issued;\nand\n\n(ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the warrant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-59c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-59c-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-59c-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d37f17e2b13726c3f8de5c7ad7997c53c3172160159654d89c181db6b4a1b221",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must notify Ombudsman or Inspector-General of warrant issuance within 6 months."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-59c-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59C(1) Notification to Ombudsman or Inspector-General of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 203,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Within 6 months after a Part 9.10 warrant is issued in response to\nan application by a Commonwealth agency, the chief officer of the\nagency must:\n\n(a) if the agency is the ACC:\n\n(i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security\nthat the warrant has been issued; and\n\n(ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity a copy of the warrant; and\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) notify the Ombudsman that the warrant has been issued;\nand\n\n(ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the warrant."
    },
