    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-60",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60 Notification to authorised representative of carrier of issue or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-60"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.204",
      "values:originalText": "revocation of certain warrants\n\n(1) Where:\n\n(a) a warrant (other than a warrant issued under section 48) is\nissued to an agency; and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept\ncommunications to or from a telecommunications service\nwhile they are passing over a telecommunications system\noperated by a carrier;\na certifying officer of the agency shall cause;\n\n(c) an authorised representative of that carrier to be informed\nimmediately of the issue of the warrant; and\n\n(d) a copy of the warrant, certified in writing by a certifying\nofficer of the agency to be a true copy of the warrant, to be\ngiven as soon as practicable to that authorised representative.\n\n(3) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1), of the issue of a warrant; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 60\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the warrant is revoked;\na certifying officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued\nshall cause:\n\n(c) that authorised representative to be informed immediately of\nthe revocation; and\n\n(d) a copy of the instrument of revocation, certified in writing by\na certifying officer of the agency to be a true copy of the\ninstrument, to be given as soon as practicable to that\nauthorised representative.\n\n(4) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1), of the issue of a named person warrant;\nand\n\n(aa) the warrant is not a warrant that authorises interception of\ncommunications made by means of a telecommunications\ndevice or telecommunications devices identified in the\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept\ncommunications made to or from a telecommunications\nservice operated by a carrier; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\na certifying officer of the agency must cause that authorised\nrepresentative to be given, as soon as practicable, a description in\nwriting of the service sufficient to identify it.\n\n(4A) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1), of the issue of a named person warrant;\nand\n\n(b) the warrant is a warrant that authorises interception of\ncommunications made by means of a telecommunications\ndevice or telecommunications devices identified in the\nwarrant; and\n\n(c) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept, by means of a\ntelecommunications device, communications made to or\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "revocation of certain warrants\n\n(1) Where:\n\n(a) a warrant (other than a warrant issued under section 48) is\nissued to an agency; and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept\ncommunications to or from a telecommunications service\nwhile they are passing over a telecommunications system\noperated by a carrier;\na certifying officer of the agency shall cause;\n\n(c) an authorised representative of that carrier to be informed\nimmediately of the issue of the warrant; and\n\n(d) a copy of the warrant, certified in writing by a certifying\nofficer of the agency to be a true copy of the warrant, to be\ngiven as soon as practicable to that authorised representative.\n\n(3) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1), of the issue of a warrant; and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nWarrants authorising agencies to intercept telecommunications  Part 2-5\nWarrants  Division 4\n\nSection 60\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the warrant is revoked;\na certifying officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued\nshall cause:\n\n(c) that authorised representative to be informed immediately of\nthe revocation; and\n\n(d) a copy of the instrument of revocation, certified in writing by\na certifying officer of the agency to be a true copy of the\ninstrument, to be given as soon as practicable to that\nauthorised representative.\n\n(4) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1), of the issue of a named person warrant;\nand\n\n(aa) the warrant is not a warrant that authorises interception of\ncommunications made by means of a telecommunications\ndevice or telecommunications devices identified in the\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept\ncommunications made to or from a telecommunications\nservice operated by a carrier; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\na certifying officer of the agenc",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-60-ss-1"
        },
