      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.204",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1), of the issue of a named person warrant;\nand\n\n(aa) the warrant is not a warrant that authorises interception of\ncommunications made by means of a telecommunications\ndevice or telecommunications devices identified in the\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept\ncommunications made to or from a telecommunications\nservice operated by a carrier; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\na certifying officer of the agency must cause that authorised\nrepresentative to be given, as soon as practicable, a description in\nwriting of the service sufficient to identify it.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1), of the issue of a named person warrant;\nand\n\n(aa) the warrant is not a warrant that authorises interception of\ncommunications made by means of a telecommunications\ndevice or telecommunications devices identified in the\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to intercept\ncommunications made to or from a telecommunications\nservice operated by a carrier; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\na certifying officer of the agency must cause that authorised\nrepresentative to be given, as soon as practicable, a description in\nwriting of the service sufficient to identify it.",
