    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-61-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "61(4) Evidentiary certificates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-61-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.206",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A certifying officer of an agency may issue a written certificate\nsigned by him or her setting out such facts as he or she considers\nrelevant with respect to:\n\n(a) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in\nconnection with the execution of a Part 2-5 warrant; or\n\n(b) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in\nconnection with:\n\n(i) the communication by a person to another person of; or\n\n(ii) the making use of; or\n\n(iii) the making of a record of; or\n\n(iv) the custody of a record of; or\n\n(v) the giving in evidence of;\n\ninformation obtained by the execution of such a warrant.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A certifying officer of an agency may issue a written certificate\nsigned by him or her setting out such facts as he or she considers\nrelevant with respect to:\n\n(a) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in\nconnection with the execution of a Part 2-5 warrant; or\n\n(b) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in\nconnection with:\n\n(i) the communication by a person to another person of; or\n\n(ii) the making use of; or\n\n(iii) the making of a record of; or\n\n(iv) the custody of a record of; or\n\n(v) the giving in evidence of;\n\ninformation obtained by the execution of such a warrant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-61"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-61-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-61-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2617fd1ad22cb760208596a4e7bab30acf677d3d4b0e2e6c6bf4e408c6a67cea",
      "skos:note": "Certifying officer must issue written certificate with relevant facts."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-61-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "61(4) Evidentiary certificates",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 206,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A certifying officer of an agency may issue a written certificate\nsigned by him or her setting out such facts as he or she considers\nrelevant with respect to:\n\n(a) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in\nconnection with the execution of a Part 2-5 warrant; or\n\n(b) anything done by an officer or staff member of the agency in\nconnection with:\n\n(i) the communication by a person to another person of; or\n\n(ii) the making use of; or\n\n(iii) the making of a record of; or\n\n(iv) the custody of a record of; or\n\n(v) the giving in evidence of;\n\ninformation obtained by the execution of such a warrant."
    },
