        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "63B Dealing in information by employees of carriers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-63b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.223",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An employee of a carrier may, in the performance of his or her\nduties as such an employee, communicate or make use of, or cause\nto be communicated, information (being information that has been\nlawfully obtained or obtained by intercepting a communication in\ncontravention of subsection 7(1)) relating to:\n\n(a) the operation or maintenance of a telecommunications\nnetwork operated by the carrier; or\n\n(b) the supply of services by the carrier by means of a\ntelecommunications network.\n\n(2) An employee of a carrier may communicate or cause to be\ncommunicated to another carrier, or to an employee of another\ncarrier, information (being information that has been lawfully\nobtained or obtained by intercepting a communication in\ncontravention of subsection 7(1)) relating to:\n\n(a) the operation or maintenance of a telecommunications\nnetwork operated by the other carrier; or\n\n(b) the supply of services by the other carrier by means of a\ntelecommunications network;\nif the communication of the information is for the purpose of the\ncarrying on by the other carrier of its business relating to the\nsupply of services by means of a telecommunications network\noperated by the other carrier.\n\n(3) An employee of a carrier may, in the performance of his or her\nduties as such an employee, communicate or make use of, or cause\nto be communicated, interception warrant information if the\ninformation is reasonably necessary to enable the interception of a\ncommunication under a warrant.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An employee of a carrier may, in the performance of his or her\nduties as such an employee, communicate or make use of, or cause\nto be communicated, information (being information that has been\nlawfully obtained or obtained by intercepting a communication in\ncontravention of subsection 7(1)) relating to:\n\n(a) the operation or maintenance of a telecommunications\nnetwork operated by the carrier; or\n\n(b) the supply of services by the carrier by means of a\ntelecommunications network.\n\n(2) An employee of a carrier may communicate or cause to be\ncommunicated to another carrier, or to an employee of another\ncarrier, information (being information that has been lawfully\nobtained or obtained by intercepting a communication in\ncontravention of subsection 7(1)) relating to:\n\n(a) the operation or maintenance of a telecommunications\nnetwork operated by the other carrier; or\n\n(b) the supply of services by the other carrier by means of a\ntelecommunications network;\nif the communication of the information is for the purpose of the\ncarrying on by the other carrier of its business relating to the\nsupply of services by means of a telecommunications network\noperated by the other carrier.\n\n(3) An employee of a carrier may, in the performance of his or her\nduties as such an employee, communicate or make use of, or cause\nto be communicated, interception warrant information if the\ninformation is reasonably necessary to enable the interception of a\ncommunication under a warrant.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bb4485d18fe704ccac61aa8e12e9f064844a921bc8c2f06112f9cfed9137812a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-63b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63B Dealing in information by employees of carriers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 223,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An employee of a carrier may, in the performance of his or her\nduties as such an employee, communicate or make use of, or cause\nto be communicated, information (being information that has been\nlawfully obtained or obtained by intercepting a communication in\ncontravention of subsection 7(1)) relating to:\n\n(a) the operation or maintenance of a telecommunications\nnetwork operated by the carrier; or\n\n(b) the supply of services by the carrier by means of a\ntelecommunications network.\n\n(2) An employee of a carrier may communicate or cause to be\ncommunicated to another carrier, or to an employee of another\ncarrier, information (being information that has been lawfully\nobtained or obtained by intercepting a communication in\ncontravention of subsection 7(1)) relating to:\n\n(a) the operation or maintenance of a telecommunications\nnetwork operated by the other carrier; or\n\n(b) the supply of services by the other carrier by means of a\ntelecommunications network;\nif the communication of the information is for the purpose of the\ncarrying on by the other carrier of its business relating to the\nsupply of services by means of a telecommunications network\noperated by the other carrier.\n\n(3) An employee of a carrier may, in the performance of his or her\nduties as such an employee, communicate or make use of, or cause\nto be communicated, interception warrant information if the\ninformation is reasonably necessary to enable the interception of a\ncommunication under a warrant.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
