        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "629de83187bb240313aa9370ab9dbe1f8198a92d4b7fa680f07eb5e38bf3e52f",
      "skos:note": "Employee may communicate interception warrant information in performance of duties."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-63b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63B(3) Dealing in information by employees of carriers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 223,
      "values:originalText": "(3) An employee of a carrier may, in the performance of his or her\nduties as such an employee, communicate or make use of, or cause\nto be communicated, interception warrant information if the\ninformation is reasonably necessary to enable the interception of a\ncommunication under a warrant.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63b-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63b-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "May",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits action under certain conditions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Employee has duty to intercept communications.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Employee may communicate interception warrant information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "63D Dealing in information for disciplinary purposes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-63d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.225",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a person engaged in network protection\nduties in relation to a computer network if:\n\n(a) the network is operated by, or on behalf of, a Commonwealth\nagency, security authority or eligible authority of a State; and\n\n(b) the duties are of a kind referred to in paragraph (b) of the\ndefinition of network protection duties in subsection 5(1).\n\n(2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), the person may communicate or\nmake use of, or cause to be communicated, lawfully intercepted\ninformation that was obtained by intercepting a communication\nunder paragraph 7(2)(aaa) if the communication or use is for the\npurpose of:\n\n(a) determining whether disciplinary action should be taken in\nrelation to a use of the network by an employee, office holder\nor contractor of the agency or authority; or\n\n(b) taking disciplinary action in relation to a use of the network\nby such an employee, office holder or contractor in a case\nwhere the use is not an appropriate use of the network by that\nemployee, office holder or contractor; or\n\n(c) reviewing a decision to take such disciplinary action.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a person engaged in network protection\nduties in relation to a computer network if:\n\n(a) the network is operated by, or on behalf of, a Commonwealth\nagency, security authority or eligible authority of a State; and\n\n(b) the duties are of a kind referred to in paragraph (b) of the\ndefinition of network protection duties in subsection 5(1).\n\n(2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), the person may communicate or\nmake use of, or cause to be communicated, lawfully intercepted\ninformation that was obtained by intercepting a communication\nunder paragraph 7(2)(aaa) if the communication or use is for the\npurpose of:\n\n(a) determining whether disciplinary action should be taken in\nrelation to a use of the network by an employee, office holder\nor contractor of the agency or authority; or\n\n(b) taking disciplinary action in relation to a use of the network\nby such an employee, office holder or contractor in a case\nwhere the use is not an appropriate use of the network by that\nemployee, office holder or contractor; or\n\n(c) reviewing a decision to take such disciplinary action.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-63d-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "01ef7955ce1786b6624a15d872229a6c126b1bf6bdf2fca0ef5db33d2c68d01e"
    },
    {
