    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-64a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "64A Dealing in connection with Inspector-General’s functions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-64a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.227",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may, in connection with an IGIS official exercising a\npower, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official,\ncommunicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of,\nthe following:\n\n(a) information obtained by intercepting a communication\npassing over a telecommunications system (whether or not\nthat information is lawfully intercepted information);\n\n(b) interception warrant information.\n\n(2) This section applies despite any other provision of this Part.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may, in connection with an IGIS official exercising a\npower, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official,\ncommunicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of,\nthe following:\n\n(a) information obtained by intercepting a communication\npassing over a telecommunications system (whether or not\nthat information is lawfully intercepted information);\n\n(b) interception warrant information.\n\n(2) This section applies despite any other provision of this Part.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-64a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-64a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5f19b05adc13f0f31c2701e12a27d97d1d8af62e4260d2ebcdb088a4336fa66d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-64a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "64A Dealing in connection with Inspector-General’s functions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 227,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may, in connection with an IGIS official exercising a\npower, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official,\ncommunicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of,\nthe following:\n\n(a) information obtained by intercepting a communication\npassing over a telecommunications system (whether or not\nthat information is lawfully intercepted information);\n\n(b) interception warrant information.\n\n(2) This section applies despite any other provision of this Part.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
