    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "65(2) Dealing in information obtained by Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-65-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.228",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper\nperformance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or\npowers:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the\nconditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in\nwriting:\n\n(i) communicate that information to another person (the\nsecond person); and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 65\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) use that information; and\n\n(c) make a record of that information;\nand the second person, and any other person to whom that\ninformation is communicated under this subsection may\ncommunicate it to another person, and use and make a record of it.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper\nperformance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or\npowers:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the\nconditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in\nwriting:\n\n(i) communicate that information to another person (the\nsecond person); and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 65\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) use that information; and\n\n(c) make a record of that information;\nand the second person, and any other person to whom that\ninformation is communicated under this subsection may\ncommunicate it to another person, and use and make a record of it.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b52422beac69900214e084249891ce14d6595b33650715e70a97f79177accdb8",
      "skos:note": "A person may communicate, use, and make a record of foreign intelligence information under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-65-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "65(2) Dealing in information obtained by Organisation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 228,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper\nperformance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or\npowers:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the\nconditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in\nwriting:\n\n(i) communicate that information to another person (the\nsecond person); and\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 65\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) use that information; and\n\n(c) make a record of that information;\nand the second person, and any other person to whom that\ninformation is communicated under this subsection may\ncommunicate it to another person, and use and make a record of it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "May",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to communicate, use, and make a record of foreign intelligence information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Attorney-General has approved the purposes and conditions.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person may communicate, use, and make a record of the information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "65(3) Dealing in information obtained by Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-65-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.228",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsections (1), (1A), (1B) and (2) do not apply to information:\n\n(a) obtained by a person referred to in paragraph 55(3)(c) or (d)\nby intercepting a communication when exercising authority\nunder a warrant issued to an agency; or\n\n(b) communicated, in accordance with section 66, to a person\nreferred to in paragraph 55(3)(c); or\n\n(c) that is interception warrant information in relation to a\nwarrant issued to an agency;\nunless the information has been communicated to the\nDirector-General of Security under section 68.\nNote:\nSee subsection 64(4) for when the Director-General of Security may\ncommunicate information, referred to in paragraph (3)(a), (b) or (c) of\nthis section, that has not been communicated under section 68.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Subsections (1), (1A), (1B) and (2) do not apply to information:\n\n(a) obtained by a person referred to in paragraph 55(3)(c) or (d)\nby intercepting a communication when exercising authority\nunder a warrant issued to an agency; or\n\n(b) communicated, in accordance with section 66, to a person\nreferred to in paragraph 55(3)(c); or\n\n(c) that is interception warrant information in relation to a\nwarrant issued to an agency;\nunless the information has been communicated to the\nDirector-General of Security under section 68.\nNote:\nSee subsection 64(4) for when the Director-General of Security may\ncommunicate information, referred to in paragraph (3)(a), (b) or (c) of\nthis section, that has not been communicated under section 68.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f33c223aae33299d456460a8f078681b64c9aa067cdafa2c583fee923a770749",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from subsections (1), (1A), (1B) and (2)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-65-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "65(3) Dealing in information obtained by Organisation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 228,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsections (1), (1A), (1B) and (2) do not apply to information:\n\n(a) obtained by a person referred to in paragraph 55(3)(c) or (d)\nby intercepting a communication when exercising authority\nunder a warrant issued to an agency; or\n\n(b) communicated, in accordance with section 66, to a person\nreferred to in paragraph 55(3)(c); or\n\n(c) that is interception warrant information in relation to a\nwarrant issued to an agency;\nunless the information has been communicated to the\nDirector-General of Security under section 68.\nNote:\nSee subsection 64(4) for when the Director-General of Security may\ncommunicate information, referred to in paragraph (3)(a), (b) or (c) of\nthis section, that has not been communicated under section 68."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
