    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "65A Employee of carrier may communicate information to agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-65a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.230",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An employee of a carrier may, for a purpose or purposes set out in\nsubsection (2), and for no other purpose, communicate to an officer\nof an agency:\n\n(a) lawfully intercepted information other than foreign\nintelligence information or information obtained under a\nsection 31A authorisation; or\n\n(b) interception warrant information.\n\n(2) The purposes are purposes connected with:\n\n(a) the investigation by the agency of a serious offence; or\n\n(b) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 66\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) determining whether a Part 5.3 supervisory order has\nbeen, or is being, complied with;\n\n(v) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 104 (control\norders) or Division 105A (post-sentence orders) of the\nCriminal Code;\n\n(vi) a preventative detention order law;\n\n(vii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, a post-sentence\ndetention law or a post-sentence supervision law; or\n\n(c) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether a community safety supervision\norder has been, or is being, complied with;\n\n(iii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 395 of the\nCriminal Code (community safety orders).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An employee of a carrier may, for a purpose or purposes set out in\nsubsection (2), and for no other purpose, communicate to an officer\nof an agency:\n\n(a) lawfully intercepted information other than foreign\nintelligence information or information obtained under a\nsection 31A authorisation; or\n\n(b) interception warrant information.\n\n(2) The purposes are purposes connected with:\n\n(a) the investigation by the agency of a serious offence; or\n\n(b) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 66\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) determining whether a Part 5.3 supervisory order has\nbeen, or is being, complied with;\n\n(v) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 104 (control\norders) or Division 105A (post-sentence orders) of the\nCriminal Code;\n\n(vi) a preventative detention order law;\n\n(vii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, a post-sentence\ndetention law or a post-sentence supervision law; or\n\n(c) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether a community safety supervision\norder has been, or is being, complied with;\n\n(iii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 395 of the\nCriminal Code (community safety orders).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-65a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b09d0968636d15575766b88a3c803fd00a34fad88d0f03e1f29d27e26d34ab62"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-65a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "65A Employee of carrier may communicate information to agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 230,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An employee of a carrier may, for a purpose or purposes set out in\nsubsection (2), and for no other purpose, communicate to an officer\nof an agency:\n\n(a) lawfully intercepted information other than foreign\nintelligence information or information obtained under a\nsection 31A authorisation; or\n\n(b) interception warrant information.\n\n(2) The purposes are purposes connected with:\n\n(a) the investigation by the agency of a serious offence; or\n\n(b) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 66\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) determining whether a Part 5.3 supervisory order has\nbeen, or is being, complied with;\n\n(v) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 104 (control\norders) or Division 105A (post-sentence orders) of the\nCriminal Code;\n\n(vi) a preventative detention order law;\n\n(vii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, a post-sentence\ndetention law or a post-sentence supervision law; or\n\n(c) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether a community safety supervision\norder has been, or is being, complied with;\n\n(iii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 395 of the\nCriminal Code (community safety orders)."
    },
