        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.230",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The purposes are purposes connected with:\n\n(a) the investigation by the agency of a serious offence; or\n\n(b) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 66\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) determining whether a Part 5.3 supervisory order has\nbeen, or is being, complied with;\n\n(v) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 104 (control\norders) or Division 105A (post-sentence orders) of the\nCriminal Code;\n\n(vi) a preventative detention order law;\n\n(vii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, a post-sentence\ndetention law or a post-sentence supervision law; or\n\n(c) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether a community safety supervision\norder has been, or is being, complied with;\n\n(iii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 395 of the\nCriminal Code (community safety orders).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The purposes are purposes connected with:\n\n(a) the investigation by the agency of a serious offence; or\n\n(b) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 66\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) determining whether a Part 5.3 supervisory order has\nbeen, or is being, complied with;\n\n(v) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 104 (control\norders) or Division 105A (post-sentence orders) of the\nCriminal Code;\n\n(vi) a preventative detention order law;\n\n(vii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, a post-sentence\ndetention law or a post-sentence supervision law; or\n\n(c) any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether a community safety supervision\norder has been, or is being, complied with;\n\n(iii) the performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of\na power, by a person, court or other body under, or in\nrelation to a matter arising under, Division 395 of the\nCriminal Code (community safety orders).",
      "values:partOf": {
