    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-66",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "66 Interceptor may communicate to officer who applied for warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-66"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.231",
      "values:originalText": "or authorised person\n\n(1) A person who has intercepted a communication under a warrant\nissued to an agency may communicate information obtained by the\ninterception to:\n\n(a) the officer of the agency who applied for the warrant on the\nagency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person in relation to whom an authorisation under\nsubsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of an agency, or an authorising officer of an\nagency for whom an appointment under subsection (4) is in force,\nmay authorise in writing a person (or class of person) referred to in\nany of paragraphs 55(3)(a) to (c) to receive information obtained\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "or authorised person\n\n(1) A person who has intercepted a communication under a warrant\nissued to an agency may communicate information obtained by the\ninterception to:\n\n(a) the officer of the agency who applied for the warrant on the\nagency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person in relation to whom an authorisation under\nsubsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of an agency, or an authorising officer of an\nagency for whom an appointment under subsection (4) is in force,\nmay authorise in writing a person (or class of person) referred to in\nany of paragraphs 55(3)(a) to (c) to receive information obtained\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-66-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-66-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "17dba3c4b53c669562942a1ecb0cf944e73a57a5737dd857d13704f9e29b4812"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-66",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "66 Interceptor may communicate to officer who applied for warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 231,
      "values:originalText": "or authorised person\n\n(1) A person who has intercepted a communication under a warrant\nissued to an agency may communicate information obtained by the\ninterception to:\n\n(a) the officer of the agency who applied for the warrant on the\nagency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) a person in relation to whom an authorisation under\nsubsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of an agency, or an authorising officer of an\nagency for whom an appointment under subsection (4) is in force,\nmay authorise in writing a person (or class of person) referred to in\nany of paragraphs 55(3)(a) to (c) to receive information obtained\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
