      "values:originalText": "(1C) The purposes are purposes connected with:\n\n(a) if the warrant under which the information was obtained\nrelates to an investigation—the investigation; or\n\n(b) if the information was obtained under a Part 5.3 warrant\nissued on the basis that a Part 5.3 supervisory order was in\nforce in relation to a person—any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether the Part 5.3 supervisory order has\nbeen, or is being, complied with; or\n\n(c) if the information was obtained under any Part 5.3 warrant—\nthe performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of a\npower, by a person, court or other body under, or in relation\nto a matter arising under:\n\n(i) Division 104 (control orders) or Division 105A\n(post-sentence orders) of the Criminal Code; or\n\n(ii) a post-sentence detention order or a post-sentence\nsupervision order; or\n\n(iii) a preventative detention order law; or\n\n(d) if the information was obtained under a Part 9.10 warrant\nissued on the basis that a community safety supervision order\nwas in force in relation to a person—any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether the community safety supervision\norder has been, or is being, complied with; or\n\n(e) if the information was obtained under any Part 9.10\nwarrant—the performance of a function or duty, or the\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1C) The purposes are purposes connected with:\n\n(a) if the warrant under which the information was obtained\nrelates to an investigation—the investigation; or\n\n(b) if the information was obtained under a Part 5.3 warrant\nissued on the basis that a Part 5.3 supervisory order was in\nforce in relation to a person—any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether the Part 5.3 supervisory order has\nbeen, or is being, complied with; or\n\n(c) if the information was obtained under any Part 5.3 warrant—\nthe performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of a\npower, by a person, court or other body under, or in relation\nto a matter arising under:\n\n(i) Division 104 (control orders) or Division 105A\n(post-sentence orders) of the Criminal Code; or\n\n(ii) a post-sentence detention order or a post-sentence\nsupervision order; or\n\n(iii) a preventative detention order law; or\n\n(d) if the information was obtained under a Part 9.10 warrant\nissued on the basis that a community safety supervision order\nwas in force in relation to a person—any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether the community safety supervision\norder has been, or is being, complied with; or\n\n(e) if the information was obtained under any Part 9.10\nwarrant—the performance of a function or duty, or the\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-67"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-67-ss-1c-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-67-ss-1c-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "940dc55fcd36af6d1cd335cdf28ed820202b8d5120508ba3b933013ff33f44d9",
      "skos:note": "The purposes are purposes connected with the investigation, achieving a Part 5.3 object, determining compliance, or performing a function/duty related to specific laws."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-67-ss-1c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "67(1C) Dealing for permitted purposes",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 232,
      "values:originalText": "(1C) The purposes are purposes connected with:\n\n(a) if the warrant under which the information was obtained\nrelates to an investigation—the investigation; or\n\n(b) if the information was obtained under a Part 5.3 warrant\nissued on the basis that a Part 5.3 supervisory order was in\nforce in relation to a person—any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 5.3 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether the Part 5.3 supervisory order has\nbeen, or is being, complied with; or\n\n(c) if the information was obtained under any Part 5.3 warrant—\nthe performance of a function or duty, or the exercise of a\npower, by a person, court or other body under, or in relation\nto a matter arising under:\n\n(i) Division 104 (control orders) or Division 105A\n(post-sentence orders) of the Criminal Code; or\n\n(ii) a post-sentence detention order or a post-sentence\nsupervision order; or\n\n(iii) a preventative detention order law; or\n\n(d) if the information was obtained under a Part 9.10 warrant\nissued on the basis that a community safety supervision order\nwas in force in relation to a person—any of the following:\n\n(i) achieving a Part 9.10 object;\n\n(ii) determining whether the community safety supervision\norder has been, or is being, complied with; or\n\n(e) if the information was obtained under any Part 9.10\nwarrant—the performance of a function or duty, or the\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
