        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.242",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The person may communicate the relevant information to:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General; or\n\n(aa) the Minister; or\n\n(b) the Director of Public Prosecutions; or\n\n(c) the Commissioner of Police; or\n\n(ca) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or\n\n(cb) the Inspector of the National Anti-Corruption Commission;\nor\n\n(d) the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The person may communicate the relevant information to:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General; or\n\n(aa) the Minister; or\n\n(b) the Director of Public Prosecutions; or\n\n(c) the Commissioner of Police; or\n\n(ca) the National Anti-Corruption Commissioner; or\n\n(cb) the Inspector of the National Anti-Corruption Commission;\nor\n\n(d) the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-71"
      },
