      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.243",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsections (1A), (2) and (3), a person to whom\ninformation has, in accordance with section 63A,\nsubsection 63B(2), 63C(2) or 63D(2), section 64A or 67,\nsubsection 71(3) or this subsection, been communicated for a\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsections (1A), (2) and (3), a person to whom\ninformation has, in accordance with section 63A,\nsubsection 63B(2), 63C(2) or 63D(2), section 64A or 67,\nsubsection 71(3) or this subsection, been communicated for a\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
