    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-77-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "77(4) Intercepted material and interception warrant information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-77-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.247",
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purpose of determining the extent (if any) to which\nsection 63AA, 74, 75A, 76 or 76A permits a person to give\ninterception warrant information in evidence in a proceeding:\n\n(a) a person may:\n\n(i) communicate the information to another person; or\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(4) For the purpose of determining the extent (if any) to which\nsection 63AA, 74, 75A, 76 or 76A permits a person to give\ninterception warrant information in evidence in a proceeding:\n\n(a) a person may:\n\n(i) communicate the information to another person; or\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-77"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-77-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-77-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "092f4838bd9b60827a7f984b2fcf80d3ab178eb1adcada5818652a69d0edc377",
      "skos:note": "A person may communicate interception warrant information to another person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-77-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "77(4) Intercepted material and interception warrant information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 247,
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purpose of determining the extent (if any) to which\nsection 63AA, 74, 75A, 76 or 76A permits a person to give\ninterception warrant information in evidence in a proceeding:\n\n(a) a person may:\n\n(i) communicate the information to another person; or\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-77-ss-4-norm",
