    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-79ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "79AB Destruction of restricted records—information obtained",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-79ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.249",
      "values:originalText": "before a community safety supervision order came into\nforce\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a restricted record is in the possession of an agency; and\n\n(b) the restricted record relates to an interception authorised by a\ncommunity safety supervision order warrant; and\n\n(c) the warrant was issued for the purpose, or for purposes that\ninclude the purpose, of obtaining information that would be\nlikely to assist in connection with determining whether the\nrelevant community safety supervision order, or any\nsucceeding community safety supervision order, has been, or\nis being, complied with; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "before a community safety supervision order came into\nforce\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a restricted record is in the possession of an agency; and\n\n(b) the restricted record relates to an interception authorised by a\ncommunity safety supervision order warrant; and\n\n(c) the warrant was issued for the purpose, or for purposes that\ninclude the purpose, of obtaining information that would be\nlikely to assist in connection with determining whether the\nrelevant community safety supervision order, or any\nsucceeding community safety supervision order, has been, or\nis being, complied with; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-79ab-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-79ab-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c59720a8fbdadc310eec0a57a22956ef281bb5efb0791e901a1083dea6c20eeb",
      "skos:note": "Prohibition on destroying restricted records obtained before a community safety supervision order came into force."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-79ab",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "79AB Destruction of restricted records—information obtained",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 249,
      "values:originalText": "before a community safety supervision order came into\nforce\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a restricted record is in the possession of an agency; and\n\n(b) the restricted record relates to an interception authorised by a\ncommunity safety supervision order warrant; and\n\n(c) the warrant was issued for the purpose, or for purposes that\ninclude the purpose, of obtaining information that would be\nlikely to assist in connection with determining whether the\nrelevant community safety supervision order, or any\nsucceeding community safety supervision order, has been, or\nis being, complied with; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-79ab-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
