      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.250",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The responsible person must cause the restricted record to be\ndestroyed as soon as practicable after becoming satisfied that the\nrestricted record is not likely to be required:\n\n(a) for the purpose of enabling a person to perform the person’s\nnetwork protection duties in relation to the network; or\n\n(b) if the network is operated by, or on behalf of, a\nCommonwealth agency, security authority or eligible\nauthority of a State—for any of the following purposes:\n\n(i) determining whether disciplinary action should be taken\nin relation to a use of the network by an employee,\noffice holder or contractor of the agency or authority;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 79A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) taking disciplinary action in relation to a use of the\nnetwork by such an employee, office holder or\ncontractor in a case where the use is not an appropriate\nuse of the network by that employee, office holder or\ncontractor;\n\n(iii) reviewing a decision to take such disciplinary action.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The responsible person must cause the restricted record to be\ndestroyed as soon as practicable after becoming satisfied that the\nrestricted record is not likely to be required:\n\n(a) for the purpose of enabling a person to perform the person’s\nnetwork protection duties in relation to the network; or\n\n(b) if the network is operated by, or on behalf of, a\nCommonwealth agency, security authority or eligible\nauthority of a State—for any of the following purposes:\n\n(i) determining whether disciplinary action should be taken\nin relation to a use of the network by an employee,\noffice holder or contractor of the agency or authority;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 79A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) taking disciplinary action in relation to a use of the\nnetwork by such an employee, office holder or\ncontractor in a case where the use is not an appropriate\nuse of the network by that employee, office holder or\ncontractor;\n\n(iii) reviewing a decision to take such disciplinary action.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-79a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-79a-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-79a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b5ba0b968d811f0f9ce407ba4e6a2c91437baa39bf3b46d8a378ebfe3a0bd0d",
      "skos:note": "Responsible person must ensure restricted record is destroyed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-79a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "79A(2) Responsible person for a computer network must ensure",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 250,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The responsible person must cause the restricted record to be\ndestroyed as soon as practicable after becoming satisfied that the\nrestricted record is not likely to be required:\n\n(a) for the purpose of enabling a person to perform the person’s\nnetwork protection duties in relation to the network; or\n\n(b) if the network is operated by, or on behalf of, a\nCommonwealth agency, security authority or eligible\nauthority of a State—for any of the following purposes:\n\n(i) determining whether disciplinary action should be taken\nin relation to a use of the network by an employee,\noffice holder or contractor of the agency or authority;\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nDealing with intercepted information etc.  Part 2-6\n\nSection 79A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) taking disciplinary action in relation to a use of the\nnetwork by such an employee, office holder or\ncontractor in a case where the use is not an appropriate\nuse of the network by that employee, office holder or\ncontractor;\n\n(iii) reviewing a decision to take such disciplinary action.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
