    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-84",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "84 Reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-84"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.261",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman shall, as soon as practicable, and in any event\nwithin 3 months, after the end of each financial year, report to the\nMinister in writing, in relation to each Commonwealth agency,\nabout the results of the inspections under subsections 83(1), (3) and\n(4), during that financial year, of the agency’s records.\nNote:\nThe Ombudsman does not report to the Minister in relation to the\nACC, as the Ombudsman does not inspect the records of that agency\nunder subsections 83(1), (3) and (4) (see subsection 83(1AA)).\n\n(1A) The Ombudsman must include in each report under subsection (1)\nin relation to a financial year:\n\n(a) a summary of the inspections conducted in the financial year\nunder section 83; and\n\n(b) particulars of any deficiencies identified that impact on the\nintegrity of the telecommunications interception regime\nestablished by this Act; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Ombudsman shall, as soon as practicable, and in any event\nwithin 3 months, after the end of each financial year, report to the\nMinister in writing, in relation to each Commonwealth agency,\nabout the results of the inspections under subsections 83(1), (3) and\n(4), during that financial year, of the agency’s records.\nNote:\nThe Ombudsman does not report to the Minister in relation to the\nACC, as the Ombudsman does not inspect the records of that agency\nunder subsections 83(1), (3) and (4) (see subsection 83(1AA)).\n\n(1A) The Ombudsman must include in each report under subsection (1)\nin relation to a financial year:\n\n(a) a summary of the inspections conducted in the financial year\nunder section 83; and\n\n(b) particulars of any deficiencies identified that impact on the\nintegrity of the telecommunications interception regime\nestablished by this Act; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-84-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-84-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e29346d91fb5724389debb833fcb7f417bf512d27fcbd62d6188fc72bf0c74da"
    },
