    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "87 Power to obtain relevant information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-87"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.264",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where the Ombudsman has reason to believe that an officer of an\nagency is able to give information relevant to an inspection under\nthis Part of the agency’s records, subsections (2) and (3) have\neffect.\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may, by writing given to the officer, require the\nofficer to give the information to the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) by writing signed by the officer; and\n\n(b) at a specified place and within a specified period.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nKeeping and inspection of interception records  Part 2-7\n\nSection 87\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may, by writing given to the officer, require the\nofficer to attend:\n\n(a) before a specified inspecting officer;\n\n(b) at a specified place; and\n\n(c) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nin order to answer questions relevant to the inspection.\n\n(4) Where the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) has reason to believe that an officer of an agency is able to\ngive information relevant to an inspection under this Part of\nthe agency’s records; and\n\n(b) does not know the officer’s identity;\nthe Ombudsman may, by writing given to the chief officer of the\nagency, require the chief officer, or a person nominated by the\nchief officer, to attend:\n\n(c) before a specified inspecting officer;\n\n(d) at a specified place; and\n\n(e) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nin order to answer questions relevant to the inspection.\n\n(5) The place, and the period or the time and day, specified in a\nrequirement under this section shall be reasonable having regard to\nthe circumstances in which the requirement is made.\n\n(6) A person must not refuse:\n\n(a) to attend before a person; or\n\n(b) to give information; or\n\n(c) to answer questions;\nwhen required to do so under this section.\nPenalty for an offence against this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where the Ombudsman has reason to believe that an officer of an\nagency is able to give information relevant to an inspection under\nthis Part of the agency’s records, subsections (2) and (3) have\neffect.\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may, by writing given to the officer, require the\nofficer to give the information to the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) by writing signed by the officer; and\n\n(b) at a specified place and within a specified period.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nKeeping and inspection of interception records  Part 2-7\n\nSection 87\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may, by writing given to the officer, require the\nofficer to attend:\n\n(a) before a specified inspecting officer;\n\n(b) at a specified place; and\n\n(c) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nin order to answer questions relevant to the inspection.\n\n(4) Where the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) has reason to believe that an officer of an agency is able to\ngive information relevant to an inspection under this Part of\nthe agency’s records; and\n\n(b) does not know the officer’s identity;\nthe Ombudsman may, by writing given to the chief officer of the\nagency, require the chief officer, or a person nominated by the\nchief officer, to attend:\n\n(c) before a specified inspecting officer;\n\n(d) at a specified place; and\n\n(e) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nin order to answer questions relevant to the inspection.\n\n(5) The place, and the period or the time and day, specified in a\nrequirement under this section shall be reasonable having regard to\nthe circumstances in which the requirement is made.\n\n(6) A person must not refuse:\n\n(a) to attend before a person; or\n\n(b) to give information; or\n\n(c) to answer questions;\nwhen required to do so under this section.\nPenalty for an offence against this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7b28fb8038529e265c3b2689ee8e1f4c11d9e1af1393ddafed0e530efe745829"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-87",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "87 Power to obtain relevant information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 264,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where the Ombudsman has reason to believe that an officer of an\nagency is able to give information relevant to an inspection under\nthis Part of the agency’s records, subsections (2) and (3) have\neffect.\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may, by writing given to the officer, require the\nofficer to give the information to the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) by writing signed by the officer; and\n\n(b) at a specified place and within a specified period.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nKeeping and inspection of interception records  Part 2-7\n\nSection 87\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may, by writing given to the officer, require the\nofficer to attend:\n\n(a) before a specified inspecting officer;\n\n(b) at a specified place; and\n\n(c) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nin order to answer questions relevant to the inspection.\n\n(4) Where the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) has reason to believe that an officer of an agency is able to\ngive information relevant to an inspection under this Part of\nthe agency’s records; and\n\n(b) does not know the officer’s identity;\nthe Ombudsman may, by writing given to the chief officer of the\nagency, require the chief officer, or a person nominated by the\nchief officer, to attend:\n\n(c) before a specified inspecting officer;\n\n(d) at a specified place; and\n\n(e) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nin order to answer questions relevant to the inspection.\n\n(5) The place, and the period or the time and day, specified in a\nrequirement under this section shall be reasonable having regard to\nthe circumstances in which the requirement is made.\n\n(6) A person must not refuse:\n\n(a) to attend before a person; or\n\n(b) to give information; or\n\n(c) to answer questions;\nwhen required to do so under this section.\nPenalty for an offence against this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
