    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "87(4) Power to obtain relevant information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-87-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.264",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) has reason to believe that an officer of an agency is able to\ngive information relevant to an inspection under this Part of\nthe agency’s records; and\n\n(b) does not know the officer’s identity;\nthe Ombudsman may, by writing given to the chief officer of the\nagency, require the chief officer, or a person nominated by the\nchief officer, to attend:\n\n(c) before a specified inspecting officer;\n\n(d) at a specified place; and\n\n(e) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nin order to answer questions relevant to the inspection.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) has reason to believe that an officer of an agency is able to\ngive information relevant to an inspection under this Part of\nthe agency’s records; and\n\n(b) does not know the officer’s identity;\nthe Ombudsman may, by writing given to the chief officer of the\nagency, require the chief officer, or a person nominated by the\nchief officer, to attend:\n\n(c) before a specified inspecting officer;\n\n(d) at a specified place; and\n\n(e) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nin order to answer questions relevant to the inspection.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-87-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "841f654f51fced3009c3ccc5f969a9ec8766111cd6d5d0d6f48840010aa0d5a7",
      "skos:note": "The Ombudsman may require the chief officer to attend an inspection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-87-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "87(4) Power to obtain relevant information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 264,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) has reason to believe that an officer of an agency is able to\ngive information relevant to an inspection under this Part of\nthe agency’s records; and\n\n(b) does not know the officer’s identity;\nthe Ombudsman may, by writing given to the chief officer of the\nagency, require the chief officer, or a person nominated by the\nchief officer, to attend:\n\n(c) before a specified inspecting officer;\n\n(d) at a specified place; and\n\n(e) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nin order to answer questions relevant to the inspection."
    },
