    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "92 Application of Ombudsman Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-92"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.268",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 11A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 does not apply in\nrelation to the exercise or proposed exercise of a power, or the\nperformance or the proposed performance of a function, of the\nOmbudsman under this Part.\n\n(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the\nOmbudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything\nthat an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this Part.\n\n(3) Subject to section 88 of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and (8)\nof the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this Part and\nso apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer;\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully intercepted information;\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Part;\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 11A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 does not apply in\nrelation to the exercise or proposed exercise of a power, or the\nperformance or the proposed performance of a function, of the\nOmbudsman under this Part.\n\n(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the\nOmbudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything\nthat an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this Part.\n\n(3) Subject to section 88 of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and (8)\nof the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this Part and\nso apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer;\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully intercepted information;\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Part;\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8ea1ed4f1e8617622878b48fa15c094ea5d3cf97b3855b1662ec61ebdf6e3855"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-92",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92 Application of Ombudsman Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 268,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 11A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 does not apply in\nrelation to the exercise or proposed exercise of a power, or the\nperformance or the proposed performance of a function, of the\nOmbudsman under this Part.\n\n(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the\nOmbudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything\nthat an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this Part.\n\n(3) Subject to section 88 of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and (8)\nof the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this Part and\nso apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer;\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully intercepted information;\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Part;\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted."
    },
    {
