      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Exclude",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Excluding inspecting officer's actions from Ombudsman Act reference",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the Ombudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything that an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this Part.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "An inspection officer's actions are excluded from the Ombudsman Act reference"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Justify",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Justification of exclusion as an obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the Ombudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything that an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this Part.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The exclusion is justified as an obligation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Imply",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implication of exclusion on Ombudsman Act reference",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the Ombudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything that an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this Part.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The exclusion implies that the Ombudsman Act reference does not include the inspection officer's actions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-2-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Justify",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Justification of exclusion as a prohibition",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the Ombudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything that an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this Part.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The exclusion is justified as a prohibition"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "92(3) Application of Ombudsman Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-92-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.268",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subject to section 88 of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and (8)\nof the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this Part and\nso apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer;\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully intercepted information;\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Part;\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Subject to section 88 of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and (8)\nof the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this Part and\nso apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer;\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully intercepted information;\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Part;\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b6ca2fbf6c265c6c9f10a36c989d3d0d5b6ee544a2cfbd7b4d297bd4f07ca12d",
      "skos:note": "Application of Ombudsman Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-92-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "92(3) Application of Ombudsman Act",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 268,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subject to section 88 of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and (8)\nof the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this Part and\nso apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer;\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully intercepted information;\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Part;\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "applies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Ombudsman Act applies to this Part",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) Subject to section 88 of this Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "92A Exchange of information between Ombudsman or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-92a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.268",
      "values:originalText": "Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security and State\ninspecting authorities\nDefinitions\n\n(1) In this section:\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nKeeping and inspection of interception records  Part 2-7\n\nSection 92A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nState agency means an eligible authority of a State that is an\nagency.\nState inspecting authority, in relation to a State agency, means the\nauthority that, under the law of the State concerned, has the\nfunction of making inspections of the kind referred to in\nparagraph 35(1)(h) of this Act, or section 9A of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986, when the\nState agency is exercising powers under the law of that State that is\nof a similar nature to this Act.\nExchange of information between Ombudsman and State\ninspecting authorities\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may give information that:\n\n(a) relates to a State agency; and\n\n(b) was obtained by the Ombudsman under this Act;\nto the authority that is the State inspecting authority in relation to\nthe agency.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may only give information to an authority under\nsubsection (2) if the Ombudsman is satisfied that the giving of the\ninformation is necessary to enable the authority to perform its\nfunctions in relation to the State agency.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may receive from a State inspecting authority\ninformation relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions under this Act.\nExchange of information between IGIS and State inspecting\nauthorities\n\n(5) The Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security may give\ninformation that:\n\n(a) relates to a State agency; and\n\n(b) was obtained by an IGIS official under the Inspector-General\nof Intelligence and Security Act 1986; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security and State\ninspecting authorities\nDefinitions\n\n(1) In this section:\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nKeeping and inspection of interception records  Part 2-7\n\nSection 92A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nState agency means an eligible authority of a State that is an\nagency.\nState inspecting authority, in relation to a State agency, means the\nauthority that, under the law of the State concerned, has the\nfunction of making inspections of the kind referred to in\nparagraph 35(1)(h) of this Act, or section 9A of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986, when the\nState agency is exercising powers under the law of that State that is\nof a similar nature to this Act.\nExchange of information between Ombudsman and State\ninspecting authorities\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may give information that:\n\n(a) relates to a State agency; and\n\n(b) was obtained by the Ombudsman under this Act;\nto the authority that is the State inspecting authority in relation to\nthe agency.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may only give information to an authority under\nsubsection (2) if the Ombudsman is satisfied that the giving of the\ninformation is necessary to enable the authority to perform its\nfunctions in relation to the State agency.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may receive from a State inspecting authority\ninformation relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions under this Act.\nExchange of information between IGIS and State inspecting\nauthorities\n\n(5) The Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security may give\ninformation that:\n\n(a) relates to a State agency; and\n\n(b) was obtained by an IGIS official under the Inspector-General\nof Intelligence and Security Act 1986; and\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-92a-ss-2"
        },
