    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-96",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "96 Annual reports by State authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-96"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.274",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the chief officer of an eligible authority\nof a State shall, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3\nmonths, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report\nthat:\n\n(a) if information that section 102 or 102A requires to be set out\nin the Minister’s report under Division 2 relating to the year\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nReports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8\nReports to the Minister  Division 1\n\nSection 97\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nending on that 30 June can be derived from the authority’s\nrecords—sets out that information; or\n\n(b) in any other case—states that no such information can be so\nderived.\n\n(1A) A report under subsection (1) must include a statement of the total\nexpenditure (including expenditure of a capital nature) incurred by\nthe eligible authority concerned in connection with the execution\nof warrants during the year to which the report relates.\n\n(2) Where a Minister of a State has given to the Minister a written\nreport that sets out the information that, but for this subsection,\nsubsections (1) and (1A) would require to be set out in a report by\nthe chief officer of an eligible authority of that State, the chief\nofficer need not give to the Minister the last-mentioned report.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the chief officer of an eligible authority\nof a State shall, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3\nmonths, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report\nthat:\n\n(a) if information that section 102 or 102A requires to be set out\nin the Minister’s report under Division 2 relating to the year\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nReports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8\nReports to the Minister  Division 1\n\nSection 97\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nending on that 30 June can be derived from the authority’s\nrecords—sets out that information; or\n\n(b) in any other case—states that no such information can be so\nderived.\n\n(1A) A report under subsection (1) must include a statement of the total\nexpenditure (including expenditure of a capital nature) incurred by\nthe eligible authority concerned in connection with the execution\nof warrants during the year to which the report relates.\n\n(2) Where a Minister of a State has given to the Minister a written\nreport that sets out the information that, but for this subsection,\nsubsections (1) and (1A) would require to be set out in a report by\nthe chief officer of an eligible authority of that State, the chief\nofficer need not give to the Minister the last-mentioned report.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-96-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-96-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-96-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2e942d6012dbeabbcac5ee0ca3c7427ca0fe6474df2dfb8e804ba6e417238909"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-96",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "96 Annual reports by State authorities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 274,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the chief officer of an eligible authority\nof a State shall, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3\nmonths, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report\nthat:\n\n(a) if information that section 102 or 102A requires to be set out\nin the Minister’s report under Division 2 relating to the year\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nReports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8\nReports to the Minister  Division 1\n\nSection 97\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nending on that 30 June can be derived from the authority’s\nrecords—sets out that information; or\n\n(b) in any other case—states that no such information can be so\nderived.\n\n(1A) A report under subsection (1) must include a statement of the total\nexpenditure (including expenditure of a capital nature) incurred by\nthe eligible authority concerned in connection with the execution\nof warrants during the year to which the report relates.\n\n(2) Where a Minister of a State has given to the Minister a written\nreport that sets out the information that, but for this subsection,\nsubsections (1) and (1A) would require to be set out in a report by\nthe chief officer of an eligible authority of that State, the chief\nofficer need not give to the Minister the last-mentioned report."
    },
