    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-103",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "103 Other information to be included in report",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-103"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.284",
      "values:originalText": "The report must set out:\n\n(a) the total expenditure (including expenditure of a capital\nnature) incurred by agencies to which the report relates in\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nReports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8\nReports by the Minister  Division 2\n\nSection 103\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nconnection with the execution of warrants during the year to\nwhich the report relates; and\n\n(aa) for:\n\n(i) each Commonwealth agency; and\n\n(ii) each eligible authority of a State, where the eligible\nauthority was an agency at any time during the year to\nwhich the report relates;\n\nthe amount worked out using the formula:\n\nwhere:\n\nTotal warrant expenditure means the total expenditure\n(including expenditure of a capital nature) incurred by the\nagency or the authority, as the case requires, in connection\nwith the execution of warrants during the year to which the\nreport relates.\n\nNumber of warrants means the number of warrants to which\nthe total warrant expenditure relates; and\n\n(ab) information about the availability of judges to issue warrants\nunder Part 2-5 and the extent to which nominated ART\nmembers have been used for that purpose, but not including\ninformation that would identify a particular judge or ART\nmember; and\n\n(ac) for:\n\n(i) each Commonwealth agency; and\n\n(ii) each eligible authority of a State, where the eligible\nauthority was an agency at any time during the year to\nwhich the report relates;\n\nthe number (if any) of interceptions carried out on behalf of\neach other such Commonwealth agency or eligible authority;\nand\n\n(aca) the number (if any) of interceptions carried out by the\nOrganisation on behalf of:\n\n(i) each Commonwealth agency; and\nTotal warrant expenditure\nNumber of warrants\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "The report must set out:\n\n(a) the total expenditure (including expenditure of a capital\nnature) incurred by agencies to which the report relates in\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nReports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8\nReports by the Minister  Division 2\n\nSection 103\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nconnection with the execution of warrants during the year to\nwhich the report relates; and\n\n(aa) for:\n\n(i) each Commonwealth agency; and\n\n(ii) each eligible authority of a State, where the eligible\nauthority was an agency at any time during the year to\nwhich the report relates;\n\nthe amount worked out using the formula:\n\nwhere:\n\nTotal warrant expenditure means the total expenditure\n(including expenditure of a capital nature) incurred by the\nagency or the authority, as the case requires, in connection\nwith the execution of warrants during the year to which the\nreport relates.\n\nNumber of warrants means the number of warrants to which\nthe total warrant expenditure relates; and\n\n(ab) information about the availability of judges to issue warrants\nunder Part 2-5 and the extent to which nominated ART\nmembers have been used for that purpose, but not including\ninformation that would identify a particular judge or ART\nmember; and\n\n(ac) for:\n\n(i) each Commonwealth agency; and\n\n(ii) each eligible authority of a State, where the eligible\nauthority was an agency at any time during the year to\nwhich the report relates;\n\nthe number (if any) of interceptions carried out on behalf of\neach other such Commonwealth agency or eligible authority;\nand\n\n(aca) the number (if any) of interceptions carried out by the\nOrganisation on behalf of:\n\n(i) each Commonwealth agency; and\nTotal warrant expenditure\nNumber of warrants\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-103-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-103-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-103-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de023cc2baad261938bf4d6b4b9d91be16e288a9d0f95831e60f1c587f94b664",
      "skos:note": "Must provide total warrant expenditure, number of warrants, and information about judges and interceptions.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-103",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "103 Other information to be included in report",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 284,
      "values:originalText": "The report must set out:\n\n(a) the total expenditure (including expenditure of a capital\nnature) incurred by agencies to which the report relates in\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nReports about interceptions under Parts 2-3 and 2-5  Part 2-8\nReports by the Minister  Division 2\n\nSection 103\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nconnection with the execution of warrants during the year to\nwhich the report relates; and\n\n(aa) for:\n\n(i) each Commonwealth agency; and\n\n(ii) each eligible authority of a State, where the eligible\nauthority was an agency at any time during the year to\nwhich the report relates;\n\nthe amount worked out using the formula:\n\nwhere:\n\nTotal warrant expenditure means the total expenditure\n(including expenditure of a capital nature) incurred by the\nagency or the authority, as the case requires, in connection\nwith the execution of warrants during the year to which the\nreport relates.\n\nNumber of warrants means the number of warrants to which\nthe total warrant expenditure relates; and\n\n(ab) information about the availability of judges to issue warrants\nunder Part 2-5 and the extent to which nominated ART\nmembers have been used for that purpose, but not including\ninformation that would identify a particular judge or ART\nmember; and\n\n(ac) for:\n\n(i) each Commonwealth agency; and\n\n(ii) each eligible authority of a State, where the eligible\nauthority was an agency at any time during the year to\nwhich the report relates;\n\nthe number (if any) of interceptions carried out on behalf of\neach other such Commonwealth agency or eligible authority;\nand\n\n(aca) the number (if any) of interceptions carried out by the\nOrganisation on behalf of:\n\n(i) each Commonwealth agency; and\nTotal warrant expenditure\nNumber of warrants\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
    {
