    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-105-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "105(3) Contravention of section 7 or 63",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-105-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.290",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Notwithstanding that an offence against subsection 7(1) or\nsection 63 is an indictable offence, a court of summary jurisdiction\nmay hear and determine proceedings in respect of such an offence\nif, and only if:\n\n(a) the proceedings are brought in the name of the\nAttorney-General or the Director of Public Prosecutions;\n\n(b) the defendant and the prosecutor consent; and\n\n(c) the court is satisfied that it is proper for the court to hear and\ndetermine proceedings in respect of the offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Notwithstanding that an offence against subsection 7(1) or\nsection 63 is an indictable offence, a court of summary jurisdiction\nmay hear and determine proceedings in respect of such an offence\nif, and only if:\n\n(a) the proceedings are brought in the name of the\nAttorney-General or the Director of Public Prosecutions;\n\n(b) the defendant and the prosecutor consent; and\n\n(c) the court is satisfied that it is proper for the court to hear and\ndetermine proceedings in respect of the offence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-105"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-105-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-105-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8cf5a5a78a5eb555c2a5e514eddafb513f30b2ab1ccc160b1f0e56b46df3389f",
      "skos:note": "Court may hear and determine proceedings in respect of an indictable offence under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-105-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "105(3) Contravention of section 7 or 63",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 290,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Notwithstanding that an offence against subsection 7(1) or\nsection 63 is an indictable offence, a court of summary jurisdiction\nmay hear and determine proceedings in respect of such an offence\nif, and only if:\n\n(a) the proceedings are brought in the name of the\nAttorney-General or the Director of Public Prosecutions;\n\n(b) the defendant and the prosecutor consent; and\n\n(c) the court is satisfied that it is proper for the court to hear and\ndetermine proceedings in respect of the offence."
    },
