    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-106",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "106 Obstruction",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 290,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person shall not obstruct or hinder a person acting under a\nwarrant.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nOffences  Part 2-9\n\nSection 107\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person obstructing or hindering\nhas a reasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."
    },
