      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.291",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsection (1) and paragraph (2)(a) do not apply if the person first\nmentioned in subsection (1) or (2) has a reasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Subsection (1) and paragraph (2)(a) do not apply if the person first\nmentioned in subsection (1) or (2) has a reasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
