    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107A(2) Civil remedies—unlawful interception or communication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.292",
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of this section, a person is an aggrieved person if,\nand only if:\n\n(a) the person was a party to the communication; or\n\n(b) the communication was made on the person’s behalf.\nInterception—civil court remedy",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For the purposes of this section, a person is an aggrieved person if,\nand only if:\n\n(a) the person was a party to the communication; or\n\n(b) the communication was made on the person’s behalf.\nInterception—civil court remedy",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "efe12e479d2479a44d0aaaa1851dd9bcac8cb13668acc3c592d0a4a23ed00f17",
      "skos:note": "Definition of aggrieved person for civil remedies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107A(2) Civil remedies—unlawful interception or communication",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 292,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of this section, a person is an aggrieved person if,\nand only if:\n\n(a) the person was a party to the communication; or\n\n(b) the communication was made on the person’s behalf.\nInterception—civil court remedy"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-2-norm",
