    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107A(3) Civil remedies—unlawful interception or communication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107a-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.292",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a person (in this subsection called the defendant):\n\n(a) so intercepted the communication; or\n\n(b) did an act or thing referred to in paragraph 7(1)(b) or (c) in\nrelation to the interception;\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the interception by making such\norders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate.\nNote:\nParagraphs 7(1)(b) and (c) deal with the authorisation or enabling of\ninterception etc.\nCommunication—civil court remedy",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If a person (in this subsection called the defendant):\n\n(a) so intercepted the communication; or\n\n(b) did an act or thing referred to in paragraph 7(1)(b) or (c) in\nrelation to the interception;\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the interception by making such\norders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate.\nNote:\nParagraphs 7(1)(b) and (c) deal with the authorisation or enabling of\ninterception etc.\nCommunication—civil court remedy",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aee8c97e64416e9aec9769cde6b35162cf153378ddc0653b90e5759387e09623",
      "skos:note": "Grant remedial relief in respect of interception"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107A(3) Civil remedies—unlawful interception or communication",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 292,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a person (in this subsection called the defendant):\n\n(a) so intercepted the communication; or\n\n(b) did an act or thing referred to in paragraph 7(1)(b) or (c) in\nrelation to the interception;\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the interception by making such\norders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate.\nNote:\nParagraphs 7(1)(b) and (c) deal with the authorisation or enabling of\ninterception etc.\nCommunication—civil court remedy"
    },
