      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.292",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by intercepting the communication;\nand\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nCivil remedies  Part 2-10\n\nSection 107A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person (in this subsection called the defendant)\ncommunicated the information to another person in\ncontravention of section 63;\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the communication of the\ninformation by making such orders against the defendant as the\ncourt considers appropriate.\nInterception—criminal court remedy",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by intercepting the communication;\nand\n\nInterception of telecommunications  Chapter 2\nCivil remedies  Part 2-10\n\nSection 107A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a person (in this subsection called the defendant)\ncommunicated the information to another person in\ncontravention of section 63;\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the communication of the\ninformation by making such orders against the defendant as the\ncourt considers appropriate.\nInterception—criminal court remedy",
