    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107A(5) Civil remedies—unlawful interception or communication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107a-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.292",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the\ndefendant) of an offence against subsection 7(1) constituted by:\n\n(a) the interception; or\n\n(b) the doing of an act or thing referred to in paragraph 7(1)(b) or\n(c) in relation to the interception;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the interception by\nmaking such orders against the defendant as the court considers\nappropriate.\nNote:\nParagraphs 7(1)(b) and (c) deal with the authorisation or enabling of\ninterception etc.\nCommunication—criminal court remedy",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the\ndefendant) of an offence against subsection 7(1) constituted by:\n\n(a) the interception; or\n\n(b) the doing of an act or thing referred to in paragraph 7(1)(b) or\n(c) in relation to the interception;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the interception by\nmaking such orders against the defendant as the court considers\nappropriate.\nNote:\nParagraphs 7(1)(b) and (c) deal with the authorisation or enabling of\ninterception etc.\nCommunication—criminal court remedy",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cc28bb3f1fcf304d10c44fee2ff26f31b16076ebd17d419dbe3a27bea66d9306",
      "skos:note": "Court may grant remedial relief to aggrieved person if convicted of offence against subsection 7(1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107A(5) Civil remedies—unlawful interception or communication",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 292,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the\ndefendant) of an offence against subsection 7(1) constituted by:\n\n(a) the interception; or\n\n(b) the doing of an act or thing referred to in paragraph 7(1)(b) or\n(c) in relation to the interception;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the interception by\nmaking such orders against the defendant as the court considers\nappropriate.\nNote:\nParagraphs 7(1)(b) and (c) deal with the authorisation or enabling of\ninterception etc.\nCommunication—criminal court remedy"
    },
