    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107A(6) Civil remedies—unlawful interception or communication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107a-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.292",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by intercepting the communication;\nand\n\n(b) the information was communicated to a person in\ncontravention of section 63; and\n\n(c) a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the\ndefendant) of an offence against section 63 constituted by\nthe communication of the information;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the communication\nof the information by making such orders against the defendant as\nthe court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by intercepting the communication;\nand\n\n(b) the information was communicated to a person in\ncontravention of section 63; and\n\n(c) a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the\ndefendant) of an offence against section 63 constituted by\nthe communication of the information;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the communication\nof the information by making such orders against the defendant as\nthe court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107a-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9532b99d8ff434f27785180efd64c110ee79df4368112458f2d5324ca2a760c6",
      "skos:note": "Court may grant remedial relief to aggrieved person if defendant is convicted of an offence against section 63"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107a-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107A(6) Civil remedies—unlawful interception or communication",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 292,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by intercepting the communication;\nand\n\n(b) the information was communicated to a person in\ncontravention of section 63; and\n\n(c) a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the\ndefendant) of an offence against section 63 constituted by\nthe communication of the information;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the communication\nof the information by making such orders against the defendant as\nthe court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 2  Interception of telecommunications"
    },
