    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107F Extended meaning of conviction—orders under section 19B of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.296",
      "values:originalText": "the Crimes Act 1914\n\nA reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence\nincludes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of\nthe Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence.\nNote:\nSection 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found\na person to have committed an offence to take action without\nproceeding to record a conviction.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nOutline of this Part  Division 1\n\nSection 107G\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nChapter 3—Preserving and accessing stored\ncommunications",
      "skos:definition": "the Crimes Act 1914\n\nA reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence\nincludes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of\nthe Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence.\nNote:\nSection 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found\na person to have committed an offence to take action without\nproceeding to record a conviction.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nOutline of this Part  Division 1\n\nSection 107G\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nChapter 3—Preserving and accessing stored\ncommunications",
