    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107P Condition for giving a foreign preservation notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.304",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An entity mentioned in the following table may request the\nAustralian Federal Police to arrange for the preservation of stored\ncommunications that:\n\n(a) relate to a specified person or specified telecommunications\nservice; and\n\n(b) are held by a carrier; and\n\n(c) are relevant to an investigation, investigative proceeding, or\nproceeding relating to a serious foreign contravention;\nif the entity intends to make a request (an access request) under a\nprovision mentioned in the table to the Attorney-General to arrange\nfor access to those stored communications.\n\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nForeign preservation notices  Division 3\n\nSection 107Q\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nRequesting access to stored communications\nItem\nThis entity:\nMay make an access request under:\na foreign country\nparagraph 15B(d) of the Mutual\nAssistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987\nthe International Criminal Court\nparagraph 78A(b) of the International\nCriminal Court Act 2002\na War Crimes Tribunal\nparagraph 34A(b) of the International\nWar Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\n\n(2) The request by the entity to the Australian Federal Police must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) name the entity or the entity’s authority concerned with the\nserious foreign contravention; and\n\n(c) specify the serious foreign contravention that is the subject of\nthe investigation, investigative proceeding or proceeding; and\n\n(d) specify information identifying the stored communications to\nbe preserved and the relationship between those\ncommunications and the serious foreign contravention; and\n\n(e) specify any information the entity has that identifies the\ncarrier that holds the stored communications; and\n\n(f) if the stored communications relate to a specified person—\nspecify any information the entity has that identifies the\ntelecommunications service to which the stored\ncommunications relate; and\n\n(g) specify the reasons why the stored communications need to\nbe preserved; and\n\n(h) specify that the entity intends to make an access request for\nthe stored communications.\n107Q  When a foreign preservation notice is in force\n\nA foreign preservation notice:\n\n(a) comes into force when the carrier receives it; and\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the earlier of the following times:\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An entity mentioned in the following table may request the\nAustralian Federal Police to arrange for the preservation of stored\ncommunications that:\n\n(a) relate to a specified person or specified telecommunications\nservice; and\n\n(b) are held by a carrier; and\n\n(c) are relevant to an investigation, investigative proceeding, or\nproceeding relating to a serious foreign contravention;\nif the entity intends to make a request (an access request) under a\nprovision mentioned in the table to the Attorney-General to arrange\nfor access to those stored communications.\n\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nForeign preservation notices  Division 3\n\nSection 107Q\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nRequesting access to stored communications\nItem\nThis entity:\nMay make an access request under:\na foreign country\nparagraph 15B(d) of the Mutual\nAssistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987\nthe International Criminal Court\nparagraph 78A(b) of the International\nCriminal Court Act 2002\na War Crimes Tribunal\nparagraph 34A(b) of the International\nWar Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\n\n(2) The request by the entity to the Australian Federal Police must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) name the entity or the entity’s authority concerned with the\nserious foreign contravention; and\n\n(c) specify the serious foreign contravention that is the subject of\nthe investigation, investigative proceeding or proceeding; and\n\n(d) specify information identifying the stored communications to\nbe preserved and the relationship between those\ncommunications and the serious foreign contravention; and\n\n(e) specify any information the entity has that identifies the\ncarrier that holds the stored communications; and\n\n(f) if the stored communications relate to a specified person—\nspecify any information the entity has that identifies the\ntelecommunications service to which the stored\ncommunications relate; and\n\n(g) spec",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107p-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cfbf796e748658fef1bb09c2bcf1d4615339ad7aa1026dc36fc233482b552911"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107P Condition for giving a foreign preservation notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 304,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An entity mentioned in the following table may request the\nAustralian Federal Police to arrange for the preservation of stored\ncommunications that:\n\n(a) relate to a specified person or specified telecommunications\nservice; and\n\n(b) are held by a carrier; and\n\n(c) are relevant to an investigation, investigative proceeding, or\nproceeding relating to a serious foreign contravention;\nif the entity intends to make a request (an access request) under a\nprovision mentioned in the table to the Attorney-General to arrange\nfor access to those stored communications.\n\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nForeign preservation notices  Division 3\n\nSection 107Q\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nRequesting access to stored communications\nItem\nThis entity:\nMay make an access request under:\na foreign country\nparagraph 15B(d) of the Mutual\nAssistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987\nthe International Criminal Court\nparagraph 78A(b) of the International\nCriminal Court Act 2002\na War Crimes Tribunal\nparagraph 34A(b) of the International\nWar Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\n\n(2) The request by the entity to the Australian Federal Police must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) name the entity or the entity’s authority concerned with the\nserious foreign contravention; and\n\n(c) specify the serious foreign contravention that is the subject of\nthe investigation, investigative proceeding or proceeding; and\n\n(d) specify information identifying the stored communications to\nbe preserved and the relationship between those\ncommunications and the serious foreign contravention; and\n\n(e) specify any information the entity has that identifies the\ncarrier that holds the stored communications; and\n\n(f) if the stored communications relate to a specified person—\nspecify any information the entity has that identifies the\ntelecommunications service to which the stored\ncommunications relate; and\n\n(g) specify the reasons why the stored communications need to\nbe preserved; and\n\n(h) specify that the entity intends to make an access request for\nthe stored communications.\n107Q  When a foreign preservation notice is in force\n\nA foreign preservation notice:\n\n(a) comes into force when the carrier receives it; and\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the earlier of the following times:\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107p-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107P(1) Condition for giving a foreign preservation notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107p-ss-1"
      },
