      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.306",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) an entity requests under section 107P the Australian Federal\nPolice to arrange for the preservation of stored\ncommunications that are held by a carrier; and\n\n(b) in response to the request, the Australian Federal Police gives\na foreign preservation notice to the carrier in relation to those\nstored communications under subsection 107N(1); and\n\n(c) the entity makes an access request to the Attorney-General to\narrange for access to those communications; and\n\n(d) the Attorney-General refuses that access request;\nthen the Australian Federal Police must, by the third working day\nafter it is notified of the refusal, revoke the preservation notice by\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nForeign preservation notices  Division 3\n\nSection 107S\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ngiving the carrier to whom it was given written notice of the\nrevocation.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If:\n\n(a) an entity requests under section 107P the Australian Federal\nPolice to arrange for the preservation of stored\ncommunications that are held by a carrier; and\n\n(b) in response to the request, the Australian Federal Police gives\na foreign preservation notice to the carrier in relation to those\nstored communications under subsection 107N(1); and\n\n(c) the entity makes an access request to the Attorney-General to\narrange for access to those communications; and\n\n(d) the Attorney-General refuses that access request;\nthen the Australian Federal Police must, by the third working day\nafter it is notified of the refusal, revoke the preservation notice by\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nForeign preservation notices  Division 3\n\nSection 107S\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ngiving the carrier to whom it was given written notice of the\nrevocation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107r"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107r-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107r-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ed74e2115b0dbf44fc52f32edee2eae46ae8b5e52ccb0836fd92b766efc6881e",
      "skos:note": "Must revoke foreign preservation notice within 3 working days after refusal of access request."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107r-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107R(2) Revoking a foreign preservation notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 306,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If:\n\n(a) an entity requests under section 107P the Australian Federal\nPolice to arrange for the preservation of stored\ncommunications that are held by a carrier; and\n\n(b) in response to the request, the Australian Federal Police gives\na foreign preservation notice to the carrier in relation to those\nstored communications under subsection 107N(1); and\n\n(c) the entity makes an access request to the Attorney-General to\narrange for access to those communications; and\n\n(d) the Attorney-General refuses that access request;\nthen the Australian Federal Police must, by the third working day\nafter it is notified of the refusal, revoke the preservation notice by\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nForeign preservation notices  Division 3\n\nSection 107S\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\ngiving the carrier to whom it was given written notice of the\nrevocation."
    },
