      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.306",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n\n(a) an entity requests under section 107P the Australian Federal\nPolice to arrange for the preservation of stored\ncommunications that are held by a carrier; and\n\n(b) in response to the request, the Australian Federal Police gives\na foreign preservation notice to the carrier in relation to those\nstored communications under subsection 107N(1); and\n\n(c) the entity withdraws the request;\nthen the Australian Federal Police must, by the third working day\nafter it is notified of the withdrawal, revoke the preservation notice\nby giving the carrier to whom it was given written notice of the\nrevocation.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If:\n\n(a) an entity requests under section 107P the Australian Federal\nPolice to arrange for the preservation of stored\ncommunications that are held by a carrier; and\n\n(b) in response to the request, the Australian Federal Police gives\na foreign preservation notice to the carrier in relation to those\nstored communications under subsection 107N(1); and\n\n(c) the entity withdraws the request;\nthen the Australian Federal Police must, by the third working day\nafter it is notified of the withdrawal, revoke the preservation notice\nby giving the carrier to whom it was given written notice of the\nrevocation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107r"
      },
