    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107S Persons who act on the AFP’s behalf",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.307",
      "values:originalText": "A foreign preservation notice must be given or revoked on behalf\nof the Australian Federal Police by an authorised officer of the\nAustralian Federal Police.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "A foreign preservation notice must be given or revoked on behalf\nof the Australian Federal Police by an authorised officer of the\nAustralian Federal Police.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107s-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107s-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c4c94ef6a7647fb1687dfe877ada9facb7cad51c570754f4f6d778869e0dfdc9",
      "skos:note": "Must provide foreign preservation notice on behalf of AFP",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107S Persons who act on the AFP’s behalf",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 307,
      "values:originalText": "A foreign preservation notice must be given or revoked on behalf\nof the Australian Federal Police by an authorised officer of the\nAustralian Federal Police.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107s-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107s"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107s-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to provide notice",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107T Evidentiary certificates relating to actions by carriers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.308",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier or a body corporate of\nwhich the carrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(b) the secretary of a carrier or a body corporate of which the\ncarrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(c) an employee of a carrier authorised in writing for the\npurposes of this paragraph by a person referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b);\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\ndone by, or in relation to, employees of the carrier in order to\ncomply with a preservation notice.\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubsection (1) and purporting to be signed by a person referred to\nin paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of that subsection:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in an exempt proceeding, is conclusive evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a body\ncorporate is a subsidiary of another body corporate is to be\ndetermined in the same manner as the question is determined under\nthe Corporations Act 2001.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier or a body corporate of\nwhich the carrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(b) the secretary of a carrier or a body corporate of which the\ncarrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(c) an employee of a carrier authorised in writing for the\npurposes of this paragraph by a person referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b);\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\ndone by, or in relation to, employees of the carrier in order to\ncomply with a preservation notice.\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubsection (1) and purporting to be signed by a person referred to\nin paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of that subsection:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in an exempt proceeding, is conclusive evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a body\ncorporate is a subsidiary of another body corporate is to be\ndetermined in the same manner as the question is determined under\nthe Corporations Act 2001.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107t-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107t-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107t-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b5ede274cd7792a59c5f915f22afaee10b013148dd22b6fca1faf43935935a2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107T Evidentiary certificates relating to actions by carriers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 308,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier or a body corporate of\nwhich the carrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(b) the secretary of a carrier or a body corporate of which the\ncarrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(c) an employee of a carrier authorised in writing for the\npurposes of this paragraph by a person referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b);\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\ndone by, or in relation to, employees of the carrier in order to\ncomply with a preservation notice.\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubsection (1) and purporting to be signed by a person referred to\nin paragraph (a), (b) or (c) of that subsection:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in an exempt proceeding, is conclusive evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a body\ncorporate is a subsidiary of another body corporate is to be\ndetermined in the same manner as the question is determined under\nthe Corporations Act 2001."
    },
    {
