    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107u",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "107U Evidentiary certificates relating to actions by issuing agencies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107u"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.308",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certifying official of an issuing agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by him or her setting out such facts as he or she\nconsiders relevant with respect to anything done by an officer or\nstaff member of the agency in connection with a preservation\nnotice.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nProvisions relating to preservation notices  Division 4\n\nSection 107V\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under this section\nby a certifying official of an issuing agency and purporting to be\nsigned by him or her:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in an exempt proceeding, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A certifying official of an issuing agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by him or her setting out such facts as he or she\nconsiders relevant with respect to anything done by an officer or\nstaff member of the agency in connection with a preservation\nnotice.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nProvisions relating to preservation notices  Division 4\n\nSection 107V\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under this section\nby a certifying official of an issuing agency and purporting to be\nsigned by him or her:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in an exempt proceeding, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107u-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-107u-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5832ae3be726d2da12d619f0f072050051b7f0122366ec3cb615eafcf7573c15"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-107u",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "107U Evidentiary certificates relating to actions by issuing agencies",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 308,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certifying official of an issuing agency may issue a written\ncertificate signed by him or her setting out such facts as he or she\nconsiders relevant with respect to anything done by an officer or\nstaff member of the agency in connection with a preservation\nnotice.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nPreserving stored communications  Part 3-1A\nProvisions relating to preservation notices  Division 4\n\nSection 107V\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under this section\nby a certifying official of an issuing agency and purporting to be\nsigned by him or her:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in an exempt proceeding, is prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document."
    },
