    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-110a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "110A Meaning of criminal law-enforcement agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-110a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.315",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each of the following is a criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(b) a Police Force of a State;\n\n(c) the National Anti-Corruption Commission;\n\n(d) the ACC;\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Each of the following is a criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(b) a Police Force of a State;\n\n(c) the National Anti-Corruption Commission;\n\n(d) the ACC;\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-110a-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4a543b611bf027f1d07f36ece0603f86bb95ae65be1c28351b1c5e72041fcda9",
      "skos:note": "Defines criminal law-enforcement agencies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-110a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "110A Meaning of criminal law-enforcement agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 315,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Each of the following is a criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(b) a Police Force of a State;\n\n(c) the National Anti-Corruption Commission;\n\n(d) the ACC;\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
