    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-110b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "110B Declarations in relation to the Immigration and Border",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-110b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.319",
      "values:originalText": "Protection Department\nProvisions of Chapter 3 or 4 that do not apply to the Immigration\nand Border Protection Department\n\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that:\n\n(a) a specified provision in Chapter 3 or 4, referring to a criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency, does not apply in relation to the\nImmigration and Border Protection Department; or\n\n(b) a specified provision in Chapter 4, referring to an\nenforcement agency, does not apply in relation to the\nImmigration and Border Protection Department.\nProvisions of Chapter 3 or 4 that have a limited application to the\nImmigration and Border Protection Department\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that:\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "Protection Department\nProvisions of Chapter 3 or 4 that do not apply to the Immigration\nand Border Protection Department\n\n(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that:\n\n(a) a specified provision in Chapter 3 or 4, referring to a criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency, does not apply in relation to the\nImmigration and Border Protection Department; or\n\n(b) a specified provision in Chapter 4, referring to an\nenforcement agency, does not apply in relation to the\nImmigration and Border Protection Department.\nProvisions of Chapter 3 or 4 that have a limited application to the\nImmigration and Border Protection Department\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that:\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-110b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-110b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2db1e50ab29babc06f9eb903e305816700d86a54d5ac03c0bc80d657e959e1c5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-110b",
