    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-111",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "111 Form of applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-111"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.320",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The application must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the agency’s behalf\nmay make the application by telephone if the person:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\n\n(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the\npurposes of subsection (2). However, each person must be entitled\nunder section 110 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The application must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the agency’s behalf\nmay make the application by telephone if the person:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\n\n(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the\npurposes of subsection (2). However, each person must be entitled\nunder section 110 to make applications on the agency’s behalf.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-111-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-111-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-111-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "143e799f53edca7f72e68bb16dd054b34263c116be61977364f47ceb73f3446c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-111",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "111 Form of applications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 320,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The application must be in writing.\n\n(2) However, a person making the application on the agency’s behalf\nmay make the application by telephone if the person:\n\n(a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to\nwhom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under\nsubsection (3); and\n\n(b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make\nthe application by telephone.\n\n(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may, in\nwriting, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the\npurposes of subsection (2). However, each person must be entitled\nunder section 110 to make applications on the agency’s behalf."
    },
