    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-113",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "113 Affidavits to accompany written applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-113"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.320",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The application must, if it is in writing, be accompanied by an\naffidavit complying with this section.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nApplications for warrants  Division 1\n\nSection 114\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the\napplication is based.\n\n(3) Despite subsection (1), a written application may be accompanied\nby 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, but\nfor this subsection, this section would have required an affidavit\naccompanying the application to set out.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The application must, if it is in writing, be accompanied by an\naffidavit complying with this section.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nApplications for warrants  Division 1\n\nSection 114\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the\napplication is based.\n\n(3) Despite subsection (1), a written application may be accompanied\nby 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, but\nfor this subsection, this section would have required an affidavit\naccompanying the application to set out.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-113-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-113-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-113-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ff91fab41d5d75e5d15efc056d0a74b6f93c633ffb48a325e425698aca7c7913"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-113",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "113 Affidavits to accompany written applications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 320,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The application must, if it is in writing, be accompanied by an\naffidavit complying with this section.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nApplications for warrants  Division 1\n\nSection 114\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the\napplication is based.\n\n(3) Despite subsection (1), a written application may be accompanied\nby 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, but\nfor this subsection, this section would have required an affidavit\naccompanying the application to set out."
    },
