    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-118",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "118 Form and content of stored communications warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-118"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.324",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A stored communications warrant:\n\n(a) must be in accordance with the prescribed form; and\n\n(b) must be signed by the issuing authority who issues it.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nIssuing of warrants  Division 2\n\nSection 119\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) A stored communications warrant may specify conditions or\nrestrictions relating to accessing stored communications under the\nwarrant.\n\n(3) A stored communications warrant must set out short particulars of\neach serious contravention or serious foreign contravention in\nrelation to which the issuing authority issuing the warrant was\nsatisfied, on the application for the warrant, as mentioned in\nsubparagraph 116(1)(d)(i) or (ii), as the case may be.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A stored communications warrant:\n\n(a) must be in accordance with the prescribed form; and\n\n(b) must be signed by the issuing authority who issues it.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nIssuing of warrants  Division 2\n\nSection 119\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) A stored communications warrant may specify conditions or\nrestrictions relating to accessing stored communications under the\nwarrant.\n\n(3) A stored communications warrant must set out short particulars of\neach serious contravention or serious foreign contravention in\nrelation to which the issuing authority issuing the warrant was\nsatisfied, on the application for the warrant, as mentioned in\nsubparagraph 116(1)(d)(i) or (ii), as the case may be.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-118-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-118-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-118-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a401baf04b9c6831c85b2b43c3a403e934e92728833440be185151a8597181d6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-118",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "118 Form and content of stored communications warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 324,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A stored communications warrant:\n\n(a) must be in accordance with the prescribed form; and\n\n(b) must be signed by the issuing authority who issues it.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nIssuing of warrants  Division 2\n\nSection 119\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(2) A stored communications warrant may specify conditions or\nrestrictions relating to accessing stored communications under the\nwarrant.\n\n(3) A stored communications warrant must set out short particulars of\neach serious contravention or serious foreign contravention in\nrelation to which the issuing authority issuing the warrant was\nsatisfied, on the application for the warrant, as mentioned in\nsubparagraph 116(1)(d)(i) or (ii), as the case may be."
    },
