    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "119 Duration of stored communications warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-119"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.325",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A stored communications warrant remains in force:\n\n(a) until it is first executed; or\n\n(b) until the end of the period of 5 days after the day on which it\nwas issued;\nwhichever occurs sooner.\n\n(2) However, if the warrant relates to more than one\ntelecommunications service and those services are not all operated\nby the same carrier, the warrant remains in force, to the extent that\nit relates to a telecommunications service operated by a particular\ncarrier:\n\n(a) until it is first executed in relation to a telecommunications\nservice operated by that particular carrier; or\n\n(b) until the end of the period of 5 days after the day on which it\nwas issued;\nwhichever occurs sooner.\n\n(3) An issuing authority must not vary a stored communications\nwarrant by extending the period for which it is to be in force.\n\n(4) This section does not prevent the issue of a further warrant in\nrespect of the person in respect of whom the warrant was issued.\n\n(5) However, if the further warrant relates to the same\ntelecommunications service as the previous warrant, it must not be\nissued within 3 days after the day on which the previous warrant\nwas executed or (if subsection (2) applies) was last executed.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A stored communications warrant remains in force:\n\n(a) until it is first executed; or\n\n(b) until the end of the period of 5 days after the day on which it\nwas issued;\nwhichever occurs sooner.\n\n(2) However, if the warrant relates to more than one\ntelecommunications service and those services are not all operated\nby the same carrier, the warrant remains in force, to the extent that\nit relates to a telecommunications service operated by a particular\ncarrier:\n\n(a) until it is first executed in relation to a telecommunications\nservice operated by that particular carrier; or\n\n(b) until the end of the period of 5 days after the day on which it\nwas issued;\nwhichever occurs sooner.\n\n(3) An issuing authority must not vary a stored communications\nwarrant by extending the period for which it is to be in force.\n\n(4) This section does not prevent the issue of a further warrant in\nrespect of the person in respect of whom the warrant was issued.\n\n(5) However, if the further warrant relates to the same\ntelecommunications service as the previous warrant, it must not be\nissued within 3 days after the day on which the previous warrant\nwas executed or (if subsection (2) applies) was last executed.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "86e483c9830b6cedaec5256334882b6e9afa2a7db1af488101801003bd081b08"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-119",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "119 Duration of stored communications warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 325,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A stored communications warrant remains in force:\n\n(a) until it is first executed; or\n\n(b) until the end of the period of 5 days after the day on which it\nwas issued;\nwhichever occurs sooner.\n\n(2) However, if the warrant relates to more than one\ntelecommunications service and those services are not all operated\nby the same carrier, the warrant remains in force, to the extent that\nit relates to a telecommunications service operated by a particular\ncarrier:\n\n(a) until it is first executed in relation to a telecommunications\nservice operated by that particular carrier; or\n\n(b) until the end of the period of 5 days after the day on which it\nwas issued;\nwhichever occurs sooner.\n\n(3) An issuing authority must not vary a stored communications\nwarrant by extending the period for which it is to be in force.\n\n(4) This section does not prevent the issue of a further warrant in\nrespect of the person in respect of whom the warrant was issued.\n\n(5) However, if the further warrant relates to the same\ntelecommunications service as the previous warrant, it must not be\nissued within 3 days after the day on which the previous warrant\nwas executed or (if subsection (2) applies) was last executed.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
