    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "119(5) Duration of stored communications warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-119-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.325",
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, if the further warrant relates to the same\ntelecommunications service as the previous warrant, it must not be\nissued within 3 days after the day on which the previous warrant\nwas executed or (if subsection (2) applies) was last executed.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(5) However, if the further warrant relates to the same\ntelecommunications service as the previous warrant, it must not be\nissued within 3 days after the day on which the previous warrant\nwas executed or (if subsection (2) applies) was last executed.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "20c2d6549f713c692679c770b88e0a01969e669bfcd9b1dec406a4d9fcadbb20",
      "skos:note": "No new warrant can be issued within 3 days of the previous warrant's execution."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-119-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "119(5) Duration of stored communications warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 325,
      "values:originalText": "(5) However, if the further warrant relates to the same\ntelecommunications service as the previous warrant, it must not be\nissued within 3 days after the day on which the previous warrant\nwas executed or (if subsection (2) applies) was last executed.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-119-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
