      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "120(3) Stored communications warrants issued on telephone",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-120-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.326",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An issuing authority may, by writing signed by him or her, revoke\na warrant that he or she issued on a telephone application if\nsatisfied that subsection (2) has not been complied with in relation\nto the warrant. If he or she does so, he or she must:\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nHow warrants etc. are dealt with  Division 3\n\nSection 121\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) forthwith inform the person who made the application on the\ncriminal law-enforcement agency’s behalf, or the chief\nofficer of the criminal law-enforcement agency, of the\nrevocation; and\n\n(b) give the instrument of revocation to that person, or to the\nchief officer, as soon as practicable.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An issuing authority may, by writing signed by him or her, revoke\na warrant that he or she issued on a telephone application if\nsatisfied that subsection (2) has not been complied with in relation\nto the warrant. If he or she does so, he or she must:\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nHow warrants etc. are dealt with  Division 3\n\nSection 121\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) forthwith inform the person who made the application on the\ncriminal law-enforcement agency’s behalf, or the chief\nofficer of the criminal law-enforcement agency, of the\nrevocation; and\n\n(b) give the instrument of revocation to that person, or to the\nchief officer, as soon as practicable.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-3-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-3-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "674f9036edda9d93f71b0f7bf8e3e981d7d480c91e56bf480043aeca4b94865a",
      "skos:note": "Revocation of warrant issued on telephone application",
      "dc:description": "inform the person who made the application and give the instrument of revocation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-120-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "120(3) Stored communications warrants issued on telephone",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 326,
      "values:originalText": "(3) An issuing authority may, by writing signed by him or her, revoke\na warrant that he or she issued on a telephone application if\nsatisfied that subsection (2) has not been complied with in relation\nto the warrant. If he or she does so, he or she must:\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nHow warrants etc. are dealt with  Division 3\n\nSection 121\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) forthwith inform the person who made the application on the\ncriminal law-enforcement agency’s behalf, or the chief\nofficer of the criminal law-enforcement agency, of the\nrevocation; and\n\n(b) give the instrument of revocation to that person, or to the\nchief officer, as soon as practicable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-3-norm",
