      "cml:premiseText": "Issuing authority must comply with subsection (2) before revoking warrant",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Issuing authority has an obligation to comply with subsection (2)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "120(4) Stored communications warrants issued on telephone",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-120-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.326",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The chief officer of that agency must, if another criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency is exercising authority under the warrant:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of the other agency to be informed\nforthwith of the revocation; and\n\n(b) cause a copy of the instrument of revocation to be given as\nsoon as practicable to the chief officer of the other agency.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The chief officer of that agency must, if another criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency is exercising authority under the warrant:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of the other agency to be informed\nforthwith of the revocation; and\n\n(b) cause a copy of the instrument of revocation to be given as\nsoon as practicable to the chief officer of the other agency.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
