          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-120-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1415124e3f0df82d4d6787d7ba051f1e33c20d95d495779bbb52db93ca49a7f9",
      "skos:note": "Inform other agencies of warrant revocation",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-120-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "120(4) Stored communications warrants issued on telephone",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 326,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The chief officer of that agency must, if another criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency is exercising authority under the warrant:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of the other agency to be informed\nforthwith of the revocation; and\n\n(b) cause a copy of the instrument of revocation to be given as\nsoon as practicable to the chief officer of the other agency."
    },
    {
