      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-122",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "122 Revocation of stored communications warrants by chief officers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-122"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.327",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency to which a\nstored communications warrant has been issued must, on being\nsatisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have\nceased to exist:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of any other criminal law-enforcement\nagency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be\ninformed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant;\nand\n\n(b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency to which a\nstored communications warrant has been issued must, on being\nsatisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have\nceased to exist:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of any other criminal law-enforcement\nagency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be\ninformed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant;\nand\n\n(b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-122-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-122-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "045d7461e9692f36bc761401f7b1af89205b0a29533f974bd33eda33d7c48123",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must inform and revoke stored communications warrant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-122",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "122 Revocation of stored communications warrants by chief officers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 327,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency to which a\nstored communications warrant has been issued must, on being\nsatisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have\nceased to exist:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of any other criminal law-enforcement\nagency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be\ninformed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant;\nand\n\n(b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-122-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-122"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-122-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Chief officer has an obligation to inform and revoke the warrant.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-123",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "123 What happens when stored communications warrants are",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-123"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.328",
      "values:originalText": "revoked\n\n(1) Upon revoking a stored communications warrant, the chief officer\nof a criminal law-enforcement agency must cause the chief officer\nof any other criminal law-enforcement agency that is exercising\nauthority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the\nrevocation.\n\n(2) If an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder section 121, of the issue of a stored communications warrant\nand that warrant is subsequently revoked, the chief officer of the\ncriminal law-enforcement agency to which the warrant was issued\nmust:\n\n(a) cause that authorised representative to be informed forthwith\nof the revocation; and\n\n(b) cause a copy of the instrument of revocation, certified in\nwriting by a certifying officer to be a true copy of the\ninstrument, to be given as soon as practicable to that\nauthorised representative.",
      "skos:definition": "revoked\n\n(1) Upon revoking a stored communications warrant, the chief officer\nof a criminal law-enforcement agency must cause the chief officer\nof any other criminal law-enforcement agency that is exercising\nauthority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the\nrevocation.\n\n(2) If an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder section 121, of the issue of a stored communications warrant\nand that warrant is subsequently revoked, the chief officer of the\ncriminal law-enforcement agency to which the warrant was issued\nmust:\n\n(a) cause that authorised representative to be informed forthwith\nof the revocation; and\n\n(b) cause a copy of the instrument of revocation, certified in\nwriting by a certifying officer to be a true copy of the\ninstrument, to be given as soon as practicable to that\nauthorised representative.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-123-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-123-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4bb47f186df233e48b09d241ee4defb821add0c35ac8311469fe1522c6813dd5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-123",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "123 What happens when stored communications warrants are",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 328,
      "values:originalText": "revoked\n\n(1) Upon revoking a stored communications warrant, the chief officer\nof a criminal law-enforcement agency must cause the chief officer\nof any other criminal law-enforcement agency that is exercising\nauthority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the\nrevocation.\n\n(2) If an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder section 121, of the issue of a stored communications warrant\nand that warrant is subsequently revoked, the chief officer of the\ncriminal law-enforcement agency to which the warrant was issued\nmust:\n\n(a) cause that authorised representative to be informed forthwith\nof the revocation; and\n\n(b) cause a copy of the instrument of revocation, certified in\nwriting by a certifying officer to be a true copy of the\ninstrument, to be given as soon as practicable to that\nauthorised representative."
    },
