    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-124",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "124 Access to additional telecommunications services under stored",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-124"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.328",
      "values:originalText": "communications warrants\n\n(1) If:\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nHow warrants etc. are dealt with  Division 3\n\nSection 124\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder section 121, of the issue of a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to access stored\ncommunications that, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over a telecommunications\nservice operated by a carrier; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\nthe chief officer must cause that authorised representative to be\ngiven, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the service\nsufficient to identify it.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1) of the issue of a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was\nissued, or a certifying officer of that agency, is satisfied that\nit is no longer necessary to access stored communications\nthat, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over that service;\nthe chief officer or the certifying officer must cause:\n\n(c) that authorised representative to be informed forthwith of the\nfact; and\n\n(d) confirmation in writing of the fact to be given as soon as\npracticable to that authorised representative.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "communications warrants\n\n(1) If:\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nHow warrants etc. are dealt with  Division 3\n\nSection 124\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder section 121, of the issue of a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to access stored\ncommunications that, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over a telecommunications\nservice operated by a carrier; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\nthe chief officer must cause that authorised representative to be\ngiven, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the service\nsufficient to identify it.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1) of the issue of a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was\nissued, or a certifying officer of that agency, is satisfied that\nit is no longer necessary to access stored communications\nthat, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over that service;\nthe chief officer or the certifying officer must cause:\n\n(c) that authorised representative to be informed forthwith of the\nfact; and\n\n(d) confirmation in writing of the fact to be given as soon as\npracticable to that authorised representative.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-124-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-124-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "39712abe38de2a4afea0a93254e75e5d2578f89acf04aec385899c0a1422e4c9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-124",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "124 Access to additional telecommunications services under stored",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 328,
      "values:originalText": "communications warrants\n\n(1) If:\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nHow warrants etc. are dealt with  Division 3\n\nSection 124\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder section 121, of the issue of a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to access stored\ncommunications that, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over a telecommunications\nservice operated by a carrier; and\n\n(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\nthe chief officer must cause that authorised representative to be\ngiven, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the service\nsufficient to identify it.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) an authorised representative of a carrier has been informed,\nunder subsection (1) of the issue of a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was\nissued, or a certifying officer of that agency, is satisfied that\nit is no longer necessary to access stored communications\nthat, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over that service;\nthe chief officer or the certifying officer must cause:\n\n(c) that authorised representative to be informed forthwith of the\nfact; and\n\n(d) confirmation in writing of the fact to be given as soon as\npracticable to that authorised representative.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
