    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-127",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "127 Exercise of authority conferred by warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-127"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.330",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The authority conferred by a stored communications warrant may\nonly be exercised by a person in relation to whom an approval\nunder subsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency, or an\nofficer of a criminal law-enforcement agency in relation to whom\nan appointment under subsection (3) is in force, may approve any\nof the following persons to exercise the authority conferred by\nwarrants (or classes of warrants) issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers (or classes of officers) of the agency or another\ncriminal law-enforcement agency;\n\n(b) staff members (or classes of staff members) of the agency or\nanother criminal law-enforcement agency.\n\n(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nappoint in writing an officer of the agency to be an approving\nofficer for the purposes of subsection (2).\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nProvisions relating to execution of warrants  Division 4\n\nSection 128\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The authority conferred by a stored communications warrant may\nonly be exercised by a person in relation to whom an approval\nunder subsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency, or an\nofficer of a criminal law-enforcement agency in relation to whom\nan appointment under subsection (3) is in force, may approve any\nof the following persons to exercise the authority conferred by\nwarrants (or classes of warrants) issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers (or classes of officers) of the agency or another\ncriminal law-enforcement agency;\n\n(b) staff members (or classes of staff members) of the agency or\nanother criminal law-enforcement agency.\n\n(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nappoint in writing an officer of the agency to be an approving\nofficer for the purposes of subsection (2).\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nProvisions relating to execution of warrants  Division 4\n\nSection 128\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-127-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-127-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-127-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e91223c77dc1dd53c76d0d2ea1640d283637917bcdc8b0b03e5bdf281d36ddec"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-127",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "127 Exercise of authority conferred by warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 330,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The authority conferred by a stored communications warrant may\nonly be exercised by a person in relation to whom an approval\nunder subsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency, or an\nofficer of a criminal law-enforcement agency in relation to whom\nan appointment under subsection (3) is in force, may approve any\nof the following persons to exercise the authority conferred by\nwarrants (or classes of warrants) issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers (or classes of officers) of the agency or another\ncriminal law-enforcement agency;\n\n(b) staff members (or classes of staff members) of the agency or\nanother criminal law-enforcement agency.\n\n(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nappoint in writing an officer of the agency to be an approving\nofficer for the purposes of subsection (2).\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nProvisions relating to execution of warrants  Division 4\n\nSection 128\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
