      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.330",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nappoint in writing an officer of the agency to be an approving\nofficer for the purposes of subsection (2).\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nProvisions relating to execution of warrants  Division 4\n\nSection 128\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nappoint in writing an officer of the agency to be an approving\nofficer for the purposes of subsection (2).\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nAccess by criminal law-enforcement agencies to stored communications  Part 3-3\nProvisions relating to execution of warrants  Division 4\n\nSection 128\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
