    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-129",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "129 Evidentiary certificates relating to actions by carriers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-129"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.331",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier or a body corporate of\nwhich the carrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(b) the secretary of a carrier or a body corporate of which the\ncarrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(c) an employee of a carrier authorised in writing for the\npurposes of this paragraph by a person referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b);\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier or a body corporate of\nwhich the carrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(b) the secretary of a carrier or a body corporate of which the\ncarrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(c) an employee of a carrier authorised in writing for the\npurposes of this paragraph by a person referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b);\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-129-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-129-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "683df0664c8a229d59744b33d29e664a71869fe9bdd501ec19b050776e52596b",
      "skos:note": "Authorized personnel may issue written certificates"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-129",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "129 Evidentiary certificates relating to actions by carriers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 331,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier or a body corporate of\nwhich the carrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(b) the secretary of a carrier or a body corporate of which the\ncarrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(c) an employee of a carrier authorised in writing for the\npurposes of this paragraph by a person referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b);\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-129-norm",
