      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.333",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person obstructing or hindering\nhas a reasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person obstructing or hindering\nhas a reasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-132"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-132-ss-2-norm"
        },
