        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ec648e55aa0cdf42b59e87288feca51dfabfd024f3aa332db0acc349bc454b86",
      "skos:note": "A reasonable excuse is a valid reason for obstructing or hindering"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-132-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "132(2) Obstruction",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 333,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person obstructing or hindering\nhas a reasonable excuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-132-ss-2-norm",
