      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-135",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "135 Dealing in information by employees of carriers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-135"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.335",
      "values:originalText": "Communicating information to the appropriate criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency\n\n(1) An employee of a carrier may communicate information obtained\nby accessing stored communications under a stored\ncommunications warrant to:\n\n(a) the officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency who\napplied for the warrant on the agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) an officer of the agency in relation to whom an authorisation\nunder subsection (2) by the chief officer of the agency is in\nforce in relation to the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nauthorise in writing officers, or classes of officers, of the agency to\nreceive information obtained by accessing stored communications\nunder stored communications warrants, or classes of such warrants,\nissued to the agency.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "Communicating information to the appropriate criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency\n\n(1) An employee of a carrier may communicate information obtained\nby accessing stored communications under a stored\ncommunications warrant to:\n\n(a) the officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency who\napplied for the warrant on the agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) an officer of the agency in relation to whom an authorisation\nunder subsection (2) by the chief officer of the agency is in\nforce in relation to the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nauthorise in writing officers, or classes of officers, of the agency to\nreceive information obtained by accessing stored communications\nunder stored communications warrants, or classes of such warrants,\nissued to the agency.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-135-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-135-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "922847df38b24cb2c4231a3c306935f6db0a53f4e780e77caca2ebfc3986cb80"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-135",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "135 Dealing in information by employees of carriers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 335,
      "values:originalText": "Communicating information to the appropriate criminal\nlaw-enforcement agency\n\n(1) An employee of a carrier may communicate information obtained\nby accessing stored communications under a stored\ncommunications warrant to:\n\n(a) the officer of the criminal law-enforcement agency who\napplied for the warrant on the agency’s behalf; or\n\n(b) an officer of the agency in relation to whom an authorisation\nunder subsection (2) by the chief officer of the agency is in\nforce in relation to the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a criminal law-enforcement agency may\nauthorise in writing officers, or classes of officers, of the agency to\nreceive information obtained by accessing stored communications\nunder stored communications warrants, or classes of such warrants,\nissued to the agency.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
