    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-137",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "137 Dealing in information obtained by Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-137"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.338",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General of Security may, in accordance with\nsubsection 18(3) or (4A), or subsection 19A(4) of the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation Act 1979, communicate the\nfollowing to another person:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information;\n\n(aa) preservation notice information;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(1A) The Director-General of Security may:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved by the Attorney-General in\nwriting; and\n\n(b) subject to the conditions (if any) specified by the\nAttorney-General in writing;\ncommunicate foreign intelligence information to another person\n(the second person), other than a person to whom the\nDirector-General could communicate the information under\nsubsection (1) or 136(2).\n\n(1B) The second person to whom the foreign intelligence information is\ncommunicated under subsection (1A), and any other person to\nwhom that information is communicated under this subsection,\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nPermitted dealings with accessed information  Division 2\n\nSection 138\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nmay communicate it to another person, and use and make a record\nof it.\n\n(2) The communication under subsection (1) or (1A) may be made by\nthe Director-General of Security personally or by a person\nauthorised by the Director-General.\n\n(3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper\nperformance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or\npowers:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the\nconditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in\nwriting:\n\n(i) communicate that information to another person (the\nsecond person); and\n\n(ii) use that information; and\n\n(b) make a record of that information;\nand the second person, and any other person to whom that\ninformation is communicated under this subsection, may\ncommunicate it to another person, and use and make a record of it.\n\n(4) An approval or a condition under subsection (1A) or (3) is not a\nlegislative instrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General of Security may, in accordance with\nsubsection 18(3) or (4A), or subsection 19A(4) of the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation Act 1979, communicate the\nfollowing to another person:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information;\n\n(aa) preservation notice information;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(1A) The Director-General of Security may:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved by the Attorney-General in\nwriting; and\n\n(b) subject to the conditions (if any) specified by the\nAttorney-General in writing;\ncommunicate foreign intelligence information to another person\n(the second person), other than a person to whom the\nDirector-General could communicate the information under\nsubsection (1) or 136(2).\n\n(1B) The second person to whom the foreign intelligence information is\ncommunicated under subsection (1A), and any other person to\nwhom that information is communicated under this subsection,\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nPermitted dealings with accessed information  Division 2\n\nSection 138\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nmay communicate it to another person, and use and make a record\nof it.\n\n(2) The communication under subsection (1) or (1A) may be made by\nthe Director-General of Security personally or by a person\nauthorised by the Director-General.\n\n(3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper\nperformance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or\npowers:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the\nconditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in\nwriting:\n\n(i) communicate that information to another person (the\nsecond person); and\n\n(ii) use that information; and\n\n(b) make a record of that information;\nand the second person, and any other person to whom that\ninformation is communicated under this subs",
