    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-137-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "137(3) Dealing in information obtained by Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-137-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.338",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper\nperformance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or\npowers:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the\nconditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in\nwriting:\n\n(i) communicate that information to another person (the\nsecond person); and\n\n(ii) use that information; and\n\n(b) make a record of that information;\nand the second person, and any other person to whom that\ninformation is communicated under this subsection, may\ncommunicate it to another person, and use and make a record of it.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper\nperformance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or\npowers:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the\nconditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in\nwriting:\n\n(i) communicate that information to another person (the\nsecond person); and\n\n(ii) use that information; and\n\n(b) make a record of that information;\nand the second person, and any other person to whom that\ninformation is communicated under this subsection, may\ncommunicate it to another person, and use and make a record of it.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-137"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-137-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-137-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "130041812bc1bcdc07e2ddd1319f604f12b280d3ae5863686d117d7104521922",
      "skos:note": "A person may communicate and use foreign intelligence information under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-137-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "137(3) Dealing in information obtained by Organisation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 338,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated under subsection (1) may, in the proper\nperformance or exercise of the person’s functions, duties or\npowers:\n\n(a) for the purposes (if any) approved, and subject to the\nconditions (if any) specified, by the Attorney-General in\nwriting:\n\n(i) communicate that information to another person (the\nsecond person); and\n\n(ii) use that information; and\n\n(b) make a record of that information;\nand the second person, and any other person to whom that\ninformation is communicated under this subsection, may\ncommunicate it to another person, and use and make a record of it."
    },
