    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-138",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "138 Employee of carrier may communicate information to criminal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-138"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.339",
      "values:originalText": "law-enforcement agency\n\n(1) An employee of a carrier may, for a purpose or purposes connected\nwith the investigation by the Australian Communications and\nMedia Authority of a serious contravention or with the\nperformance of its functions relating to enforcement of the Spam\nAct 2003, and for no other purpose, communicate to an officer or\nstaff member of the authority the following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence\ninformation;\n\n(aa) preservation notice information;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "law-enforcement agency\n\n(1) An employee of a carrier may, for a purpose or purposes connected\nwith the investigation by the Australian Communications and\nMedia Authority of a serious contravention or with the\nperformance of its functions relating to enforcement of the Spam\nAct 2003, and for no other purpose, communicate to an officer or\nstaff member of the authority the following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence\ninformation;\n\n(aa) preservation notice information;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-138-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-138-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "81990b739616e615ea7d20baed38861abacd0eba8eb573f33a8945ae2f8cb8d4",
      "skos:note": "Employee may communicate information to law enforcement agency for investigation purposes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-138",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "138 Employee of carrier may communicate information to criminal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 339,
      "values:originalText": "law-enforcement agency\n\n(1) An employee of a carrier may, for a purpose or purposes connected\nwith the investigation by the Australian Communications and\nMedia Authority of a serious contravention or with the\nperformance of its functions relating to enforcement of the Spam\nAct 2003, and for no other purpose, communicate to an officer or\nstaff member of the authority the following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence\ninformation;\n\n(aa) preservation notice information;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-138-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-138"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-138-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission granted",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Employee may communicate information",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Authority may receive information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-139aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "139AA Dealing in connection with Inspector-General’s functions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-139aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.342",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may, in connection with an IGIS official exercising a\npower, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official,\ncommunicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of,\nthe following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information;\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nPermitted dealings with accessed information  Division 2\n\nSection 139A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) information obtained by accessing a stored communication\n(whether or not that information is lawfully accessed\ninformation);\n\n(c) preservation notice information;\n\n(d) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) This section applies despite any other provision of this Part.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may, in connection with an IGIS official exercising a\npower, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official,\ncommunicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of,\nthe following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information;\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nPermitted dealings with accessed information  Division 2\n\nSection 139A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) information obtained by accessing a stored communication\n(whether or not that information is lawfully accessed\ninformation);\n\n(c) preservation notice information;\n\n(d) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) This section applies despite any other provision of this Part.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-139aa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-139aa-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a47e3bed936f3d7eb1b3804ff17bf00f36c30ff4abb93880c13d73685b928151"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-139aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "139AA Dealing in connection with Inspector-General’s functions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 342,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may, in connection with an IGIS official exercising a\npower, or performing a function or duty, as an IGIS official,\ncommunicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of,\nthe following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information;\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nPermitted dealings with accessed information  Division 2\n\nSection 139A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) information obtained by accessing a stored communication\n(whether or not that information is lawfully accessed\ninformation);\n\n(c) preservation notice information;\n\n(d) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) This section applies despite any other provision of this Part."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-139aa-ss-1",
