    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-139a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "139A Dealing for integrity purposes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-139a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.343",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An officer or staff member of a Commonwealth agency may, for\none or more purposes referred to in subsection (2), and for no other\npurpose (other than a purpose referred to in subsection 139(2) or\n(4A) or 139B(2), if applicable), communicate to another person,\nmake use of, or make a record of the following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence\ninformation;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) The purposes are:\n\n(a) a permitted purpose mentioned in the table in section 6S in\nrelation to the agency or another Commonwealth agency; or\n\n(b) purposes connected with the keeping of records by the\nagency under Part 3-5.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An officer or staff member of a Commonwealth agency may, for\none or more purposes referred to in subsection (2), and for no other\npurpose (other than a purpose referred to in subsection 139(2) or\n(4A) or 139B(2), if applicable), communicate to another person,\nmake use of, or make a record of the following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence\ninformation;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) The purposes are:\n\n(a) a permitted purpose mentioned in the table in section 6S in\nrelation to the agency or another Commonwealth agency; or\n\n(b) purposes connected with the keeping of records by the\nagency under Part 3-5.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-139a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-139a-ss-4a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-139a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "609be1a42b78785790dc533808a429df35e5f457e634454eb1d2fb751b65439d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-139a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "139A Dealing for integrity purposes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 343,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An officer or staff member of a Commonwealth agency may, for\none or more purposes referred to in subsection (2), and for no other\npurpose (other than a purpose referred to in subsection 139(2) or\n(4A) or 139B(2), if applicable), communicate to another person,\nmake use of, or make a record of the following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence\ninformation;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) The purposes are:\n\n(a) a permitted purpose mentioned in the table in section 6S in\nrelation to the agency or another Commonwealth agency; or\n\n(b) purposes connected with the keeping of records by the\nagency under Part 3-5."
    },
