    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-143",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "143 Giving information in evidence in exempt proceeding",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-143"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.346",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may give lawfully accessed information (other than\nforeign intelligence information) in evidence in an exempt\nproceeding.\n\n(2) For the purposes of applying subsection (1) in relation to\ninformation, the question whether or not a stored communication\nwas accessed in contravention of subsection 108(1) may be\ndetermined on the balance of probabilities.\n\n(3) A person may give stored communications warrant information in\nevidence in an exempt proceeding.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nPermitted dealings with accessed information  Division 2\n\nSection 144\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may give lawfully accessed information (other than\nforeign intelligence information) in evidence in an exempt\nproceeding.\n\n(2) For the purposes of applying subsection (1) in relation to\ninformation, the question whether or not a stored communication\nwas accessed in contravention of subsection 108(1) may be\ndetermined on the balance of probabilities.\n\n(3) A person may give stored communications warrant information in\nevidence in an exempt proceeding.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nPermitted dealings with accessed information  Division 2\n\nSection 144\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
