    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "144 Giving information in evidence if communication unlawfully",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-144"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.347",
      "values:originalText": "accessed\n\n(1) A person may give, in evidence in an exempt proceeding,\ninformation obtained by accessing stored communications obtained\nin contravention of subsection 108(1) if:\n\n(a) the access was purportedly under a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the court in which, or the tribunal, body, authority or person\nbefore which, the proceeding is held is satisfied that:\n\n(i) but for an irregularity, the access would not have\nconstituted a contravention of subsection 108(1); and\n\n(ii) the irregularity is not a substantial defect or irregularity;\nand\n\n(iii) in all the circumstances, the irregularity should be\ndisregarded.\n\n(2) A reference in subsection (1) to an irregularity is a reference to a\ndefect or irregularity:\n\n(a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting\nto be a warrant; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the\npurported execution of a document purporting to be a\nwarrant.",
      "skos:definition": "accessed\n\n(1) A person may give, in evidence in an exempt proceeding,\ninformation obtained by accessing stored communications obtained\nin contravention of subsection 108(1) if:\n\n(a) the access was purportedly under a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the court in which, or the tribunal, body, authority or person\nbefore which, the proceeding is held is satisfied that:\n\n(i) but for an irregularity, the access would not have\nconstituted a contravention of subsection 108(1); and\n\n(ii) the irregularity is not a substantial defect or irregularity;\nand\n\n(iii) in all the circumstances, the irregularity should be\ndisregarded.\n\n(2) A reference in subsection (1) to an irregularity is a reference to a\ndefect or irregularity:\n\n(a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting\nto be a warrant; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the\npurported execution of a document purporting to be a\nwarrant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "92f1432e8df80ee099902ef467d6680a9825ea5433a13a1f37850b91fcb799d5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-144",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "144 Giving information in evidence if communication unlawfully",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 347,
      "values:originalText": "accessed\n\n(1) A person may give, in evidence in an exempt proceeding,\ninformation obtained by accessing stored communications obtained\nin contravention of subsection 108(1) if:\n\n(a) the access was purportedly under a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the court in which, or the tribunal, body, authority or person\nbefore which, the proceeding is held is satisfied that:\n\n(i) but for an irregularity, the access would not have\nconstituted a contravention of subsection 108(1); and\n\n(ii) the irregularity is not a substantial defect or irregularity;\nand\n\n(iii) in all the circumstances, the irregularity should be\ndisregarded.\n\n(2) A reference in subsection (1) to an irregularity is a reference to a\ndefect or irregularity:\n\n(a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting\nto be a warrant; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the\npurported execution of a document purporting to be a\nwarrant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "144(1) Giving information in evidence if communication unlawfully",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-144-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.347",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may give, in evidence in an exempt proceeding,\ninformation obtained by accessing stored communications obtained\nin contravention of subsection 108(1) if:\n\n(a) the access was purportedly under a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the court in which, or the tribunal, body, authority or person\nbefore which, the proceeding is held is satisfied that:\n\n(i) but for an irregularity, the access would not have\nconstituted a contravention of subsection 108(1); and\n\n(ii) the irregularity is not a substantial defect or irregularity;\nand\n\n(iii) in all the circumstances, the irregularity should be\ndisregarded.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may give, in evidence in an exempt proceeding,\ninformation obtained by accessing stored communications obtained\nin contravention of subsection 108(1) if:\n\n(a) the access was purportedly under a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the court in which, or the tribunal, body, authority or person\nbefore which, the proceeding is held is satisfied that:\n\n(i) but for an irregularity, the access would not have\nconstituted a contravention of subsection 108(1); and\n\n(ii) the irregularity is not a substantial defect or irregularity;\nand\n\n(iii) in all the circumstances, the irregularity should be\ndisregarded.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144-ss-1-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e974dd4d6a8f803671b5a3f3eb9f320ac05df2c1ab530a9110f250c7dd669667",
      "skos:note": "Allowing access to stored communications in certain circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-144-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "144(1) Giving information in evidence if communication unlawfully",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 347,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may give, in evidence in an exempt proceeding,\ninformation obtained by accessing stored communications obtained\nin contravention of subsection 108(1) if:\n\n(a) the access was purportedly under a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the court in which, or the tribunal, body, authority or person\nbefore which, the proceeding is held is satisfied that:\n\n(i) but for an irregularity, the access would not have\nconstituted a contravention of subsection 108(1); and\n\n(ii) the irregularity is not a substantial defect or irregularity;\nand\n\n(iii) in all the circumstances, the irregularity should be\ndisregarded."
    },
    {
