        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "144(2) Giving information in evidence if communication unlawfully",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-144-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.347",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A reference in subsection (1) to an irregularity is a reference to a\ndefect or irregularity:\n\n(a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting\nto be a warrant; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the\npurported execution of a document purporting to be a\nwarrant.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A reference in subsection (1) to an irregularity is a reference to a\ndefect or irregularity:\n\n(a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting\nto be a warrant; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the\npurported execution of a document purporting to be a\nwarrant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4350c6a05d48bb0c4c1bffc66c11a3810a20f4ebab4d2cf3399f31714586bbb5",
      "skos:note": "Prohibiting communication of certain information in evidence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-144-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "144(2) Giving information in evidence if communication unlawfully",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 347,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A reference in subsection (1) to an irregularity is a reference to a\ndefect or irregularity:\n\n(a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting\nto be a warrant; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the\npurported execution of a document purporting to be a\nwarrant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-144-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
