      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "PERMIT",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permits action",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-146",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "146 Giving information in evidence in civil proceedings for remedial",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-146"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.348",
      "values:originalText": "relief\n\n(1) A person may give information obtained by accessing a stored\ncommunication in contravention of subsection 108(1) in evidence\nin a proceeding by way of an application under section 165 for\nremedial relief in respect of:\n\n(a) the access; or\n\n(b) the communication (in contravention of section 133) of\ninformation obtained by the access.\n\n(2) A person may give preservation notice information or stored\ncommunications warrant information in evidence in a proceeding\nby way of an application under section 165.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nAdmissibility of evidence  Division 3\n\nSection 147\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "relief\n\n(1) A person may give information obtained by accessing a stored\ncommunication in contravention of subsection 108(1) in evidence\nin a proceeding by way of an application under section 165 for\nremedial relief in respect of:\n\n(a) the access; or\n\n(b) the communication (in contravention of section 133) of\ninformation obtained by the access.\n\n(2) A person may give preservation notice information or stored\ncommunications warrant information in evidence in a proceeding\nby way of an application under section 165.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nAdmissibility of evidence  Division 3\n\nSection 147\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-146-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-146-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ea6a344e27604dcb67a09c548bcf44b13628c54debf48bcf37139db8f9f9dd86"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-146",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "146 Giving information in evidence in civil proceedings for remedial",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 348,
      "values:originalText": "relief\n\n(1) A person may give information obtained by accessing a stored\ncommunication in contravention of subsection 108(1) in evidence\nin a proceeding by way of an application under section 165 for\nremedial relief in respect of:\n\n(a) the access; or\n\n(b) the communication (in contravention of section 133) of\ninformation obtained by the access.\n\n(2) A person may give preservation notice information or stored\ncommunications warrant information in evidence in a proceeding\nby way of an application under section 165.\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nDealing with accessed information etc.  Part 3-4\nAdmissibility of evidence  Division 3\n\nSection 147\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
