    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-148",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "148 Stored communications warrant information inadmissible",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-148"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.349",
      "values:originalText": "except as provided\n\n(1) Stored communications warrant information is admissible in\nevidence in a proceeding only to the extent that section 143, 145 or\n146 permits a person to give stored communications warrant\ninformation in evidence in that proceeding.\n\n(2) For the purpose of determining the extent (if any) to which\nsection 143, 145 or 146 permits a person to give stored\ncommunications warrant information in evidence in a proceeding:\n\n(a) a person may:\n\n(i) communicate the information to another person; or\n\n(ii) make use of the information; or\n\n(iii) make a record of the information; or\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "except as provided\n\n(1) Stored communications warrant information is admissible in\nevidence in a proceeding only to the extent that section 143, 145 or\n146 permits a person to give stored communications warrant\ninformation in evidence in that proceeding.\n\n(2) For the purpose of determining the extent (if any) to which\nsection 143, 145 or 146 permits a person to give stored\ncommunications warrant information in evidence in a proceeding:\n\n(a) a person may:\n\n(i) communicate the information to another person; or\n\n(ii) make use of the information; or\n\n(iii) make a record of the information; or\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-148-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-148-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4d415861e1f5689920c7cfbd38d14ed7dc70ce8d6ba76c1e3d05016f4ea331fb"
    },
