        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "forbid",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits admissibility of records obtained by accessing stored communications",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-150",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "150 Destruction of records",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-150"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.351",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a\nstored communication (whether or not in contravention of\nsubsection 108(1)) is in a criminal law-enforcement agency’s\npossession; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information\nor record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to\nin subsection 139(2) or (4A), 139A(2) or 139B(2);\nthe chief officer must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed forthwith.\n\n(2) The chief officer must, as soon as practicable, and in any event\nwithin 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written\nreport that sets out the extent to which information and records\nwere destroyed in accordance with this section.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a\nstored communication (whether or not in contravention of\nsubsection 108(1)) is in a criminal law-enforcement agency’s\npossession; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information\nor record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to\nin subsection 139(2) or (4A), 139A(2) or 139B(2);\nthe chief officer must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed forthwith.\n\n(2) The chief officer must, as soon as practicable, and in any event\nwithin 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written\nreport that sets out the extent to which information and records\nwere destroyed in accordance with this section.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-150-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-150-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "085d5e7155f0aa7a250679b548526a2798ee1f0c8bd23edd8df38a27c9ad0c4d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-150",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "150 Destruction of records",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 351,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a\nstored communication (whether or not in contravention of\nsubsection 108(1)) is in a criminal law-enforcement agency’s\npossession; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information\nor record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to\nin subsection 139(2) or (4A), 139A(2) or 139B(2);\nthe chief officer must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed forthwith.\n\n(2) The chief officer must, as soon as practicable, and in any event\nwithin 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written\nreport that sets out the extent to which information and records\nwere destroyed in accordance with this section.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
