    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-150-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "150(1) Destruction of records",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 351,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a\nstored communication (whether or not in contravention of\nsubsection 108(1)) is in a criminal law-enforcement agency’s\npossession; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information\nor record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to\nin subsection 139(2) or (4A), 139A(2) or 139B(2);\nthe chief officer must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed forthwith."
    },
