    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-158a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "158A Functions of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-158a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.354",
      "values:originalText": "Security\n\n(1) Under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986,\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security has functions in\nrelation to preservation notices given by the Organisation.\n\n(2) In particular, the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security has\nthe function of:\n\n(a) inquiring into any matter that relates to compliance by the\nOrganisation with this Act (see subparagraph 8(1)(a)(i) of\nthat Act); and\n\n(b) conducting such inspections of the Organisation as the\nInspector-General considers appropriate for the purpose of\ngiving effect to the objects of that Act (see section 9A of that\nAct).\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nReports about access to stored communications  Part 3-6\nReports to the Minister  Division 1\n\nSection 159\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "Security\n\n(1) Under the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986,\nthe Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security has functions in\nrelation to preservation notices given by the Organisation.\n\n(2) In particular, the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security has\nthe function of:\n\n(a) inquiring into any matter that relates to compliance by the\nOrganisation with this Act (see subparagraph 8(1)(a)(i) of\nthat Act); and\n\n(b) conducting such inspections of the Organisation as the\nInspector-General considers appropriate for the purpose of\ngiving effect to the objects of that Act (see section 9A of that\nAct).\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nReports about access to stored communications  Part 3-6\nReports to the Minister  Division 1\n\nSection 159\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
