    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-160",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "160 Minister may seek further information from Commonwealth",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-160"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.355",
      "values:originalText": "agency\n\n(1) The Minister may, by writing, request the chief officer of a\ncriminal law-enforcement agency to give to the Minister in writing\nspecified information that:\n\n(a) the Minister needs in connection with preparing a report\nunder Division 2; and\n\n(b) is not contained in a report by the chief officer under\nsection 159.\n\n(2) To the extent that it is practicable to do so, the chief officer must\ncomply with the request.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "agency\n\n(1) The Minister may, by writing, request the chief officer of a\ncriminal law-enforcement agency to give to the Minister in writing\nspecified information that:\n\n(a) the Minister needs in connection with preparing a report\nunder Division 2; and\n\n(b) is not contained in a report by the chief officer under\nsection 159.\n\n(2) To the extent that it is practicable to do so, the chief officer must\ncomply with the request.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-160-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-160-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c4b2af4722ee54e317672875b2d8cf49aa884bf5820ec6091114fea5ec6560e4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-160",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "160 Minister may seek further information from Commonwealth",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 355,
      "values:originalText": "agency\n\n(1) The Minister may, by writing, request the chief officer of a\ncriminal law-enforcement agency to give to the Minister in writing\nspecified information that:\n\n(a) the Minister needs in connection with preparing a report\nunder Division 2; and\n\n(b) is not contained in a report by the chief officer under\nsection 159.\n\n(2) To the extent that it is practicable to do so, the chief officer must\ncomply with the request.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
