    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-161a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "161A Report to contain information about preservation notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-161a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.356",
      "values:originalText": "Domestic preservation notices\n\n(1) The report must set out, for each criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about domestic preservation notices\nthat were given by the agency during that year; and\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about revocation notices given by the\nagency under section 107L during that year.\nForeign preservation notices\n\n(2) If the criminal law-enforcement agency is the Australian Federal\nPolice, the report must also set out:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about foreign preservation notices that\nwere given by the agency during that year; and\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about revocation notices given by the\nagency under section 107R during that year.",
      "skos:definition": "Domestic preservation notices\n\n(1) The report must set out, for each criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about domestic preservation notices\nthat were given by the agency during that year; and\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about revocation notices given by the\nagency under section 107L during that year.\nForeign preservation notices\n\n(2) If the criminal law-enforcement agency is the Australian Federal\nPolice, the report must also set out:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about foreign preservation notices that\nwere given by the agency during that year; and\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about revocation notices given by the\nagency under section 107R during that year.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-161a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-161a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "150987780245512eb080caa1e7fc04c5a96bbad861c90c7538d7b90830b5336a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-161a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "161A Report to contain information about preservation notices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 356,
      "values:originalText": "Domestic preservation notices\n\n(1) The report must set out, for each criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about domestic preservation notices\nthat were given by the agency during that year; and\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about revocation notices given by the\nagency under section 107L during that year.\nForeign preservation notices\n\n(2) If the criminal law-enforcement agency is the Australian Federal\nPolice, the report must also set out:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about foreign preservation notices that\nwere given by the agency during that year; and\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about revocation notices given by the\nagency under section 107R during that year."
    },
