    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-162",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "162 Report to set out how many applications made and warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-162"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.356",
      "values:originalText": "issued\n\n(1) The report must set out, for each criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that the agency made during that\nyear; and\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nReports about access to stored communications  Part 3-6\nReports by the Minister  Division 2\n\nSection 162\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about telephone applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that the agency made during that\nyear; and\n\n(c) the relevant statistics about international assistance\napplications that the agency made during that year; and\n\n(d) for each international offence for the agency—the offence (if\nany), under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory, that is of the same, or a substantially similar,\nnature to the international offence.\n\n(2) The report must set out:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that were made during that year;\nand\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about telephone applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that were made during that year;\nand\n\n(ba) the relevant statistics about international assistance\napplications that were made during that year; and\n\n(c) the relevant statistics about renewal applications made during\nthat year; and\n\n(d) how many stored communications warrants issued on\napplications made during that year specified conditions or\nrestrictions relating to access to stored communications under\nthe warrants; and\n\n(e) for each international offence for each enforcement agency—\nthe offence (if any), under a law of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory, that is of the same, or a substantially\nsimilar, nature to the international offence.\n\n(3) An international offence, for an enforcement agency, is:\n\n(a) an offence against a law of a foreign country; or\n\n(b) a crime within the jurisdiction of the ICC; or\n\n(c) a War Crimes Tribunal offence;\nin respect of which a stored communications warrant was issued as\na result of an international assistance application made by the\nagency during the year.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "issued\n\n(1) The report must set out, for each criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that the agency made during that\nyear; and\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nReports about access to stored communications  Part 3-6\nReports by the Minister  Division 2\n\nSection 162\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about telephone applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that the agency made during that\nyear; and\n\n(c) the relevant statistics about international assistance\napplications that the agency made during that year; and\n\n(d) for each international offence for the agency—the offence (if\nany), under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory, that is of the same, or a substantially similar,\nnature to the international offence.\n\n(2) The report must set out:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that were made during that year;\nand\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about telephone applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that were made during that year;\nand\n\n(ba) the relevant statistics about international assistance\napplications that were made during that year; and\n\n(c) the relevant statistics about renewal applications made during\nthat year; and\n\n(d) how many stored communications warrants issued on\napplications made during that year specified conditions or\nrestrictions relating to access to stored communications under\nthe warrants; and\n\n(e) for each international offence for each enforcement agency—\nthe offence (if any), under a law of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory, that is of the same, or a substantially\nsimilar, nature to the international offence.\n\n(3) An international offence, for an enforcement agency, is:\n\n(a) an offence against a law of a foreign country; or\n\n(b) a crime within the jurisdiction of the ICC; or\n\n(c) a War",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-162-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-162-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-162-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c91a3cc769f870fddc83082ba1274ed09441626dfe257c2c434684373a72e4ad"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-162",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "162 Report to set out how many applications made and warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 356,
      "values:originalText": "issued\n\n(1) The report must set out, for each criminal law-enforcement agency:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that the agency made during that\nyear; and\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nReports about access to stored communications  Part 3-6\nReports by the Minister  Division 2\n\nSection 162\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about telephone applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that the agency made during that\nyear; and\n\n(c) the relevant statistics about international assistance\napplications that the agency made during that year; and\n\n(d) for each international offence for the agency—the offence (if\nany), under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory, that is of the same, or a substantially similar,\nnature to the international offence.\n\n(2) The report must set out:\n\n(a) the relevant statistics about applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that were made during that year;\nand\n\n(b) the relevant statistics about telephone applications for stored\ncommunications warrants that were made during that year;\nand\n\n(ba) the relevant statistics about international assistance\napplications that were made during that year; and\n\n(c) the relevant statistics about renewal applications made during\nthat year; and\n\n(d) how many stored communications warrants issued on\napplications made during that year specified conditions or\nrestrictions relating to access to stored communications under\nthe warrants; and\n\n(e) for each international offence for each enforcement agency—\nthe offence (if any), under a law of the Commonwealth, a\nState or a Territory, that is of the same, or a substantially\nsimilar, nature to the international offence.\n\n(3) An international offence, for an enforcement agency, is:\n\n(a) an offence against a law of a foreign country; or\n\n(b) a crime within the jurisdiction of the ICC; or\n\n(c) a War Crimes Tribunal offence;\nin respect of which a stored communications warrant was issued as\na result of an international assistance application made by the\nagency during the year.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
