    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-164",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "164 Annual reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-164"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.359",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister must cause a copy of a report under Division 2 to be\nlaid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of\nthat House after the report is prepared.\n\n(2) A report under Division 2 must not be made in a manner that is\nlikely to enable the identification of a person.\n\n(3) For the purposes of section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901, a report that Division 2 requires to be prepared as soon as\npracticable after 30 June in a calendar year is taken to be a periodic\nreport:\n\n(a) that this Act requires a person to give to the Minister; and\n\n(b) that relates to the administration of Parts 3-3, 3-4 and 3-5\nduring the year ending on that 30 June.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister must cause a copy of a report under Division 2 to be\nlaid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of\nthat House after the report is prepared.\n\n(2) A report under Division 2 must not be made in a manner that is\nlikely to enable the identification of a person.\n\n(3) For the purposes of section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901, a report that Division 2 requires to be prepared as soon as\npracticable after 30 June in a calendar year is taken to be a periodic\nreport:\n\n(a) that this Act requires a person to give to the Minister; and\n\n(b) that relates to the administration of Parts 3-3, 3-4 and 3-5\nduring the year ending on that 30 June.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-164-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-164-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-164-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a3a49bb6abfe20c79039cc52a3171bdd1320f0a4fcc0d153585d647a9c753a2f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-164",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "164 Annual reports",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 359,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister must cause a copy of a report under Division 2 to be\nlaid before each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of\nthat House after the report is prepared.\n\n(2) A report under Division 2 must not be made in a manner that is\nlikely to enable the identification of a person.\n\n(3) For the purposes of section 34C of the Acts Interpretation Act\n1901, a report that Division 2 requires to be prepared as soon as\npracticable after 30 June in a calendar year is taken to be a periodic\nreport:\n\n(a) that this Act requires a person to give to the Minister; and\n\n(b) that relates to the administration of Parts 3-3, 3-4 and 3-5\nduring the year ending on that 30 June.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications"
    },
