    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "165(3) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-165-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.360",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a person (the defendant):\n\n(a) so accessed the communication; or\n\n(b) did an act or thing referred to in subparagraph 108(1)(a)(ii) or\n(iii) in relation to the access;\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the access by making such\norders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate.\nNote:\nSubparagraphs 108(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) deal with the authorisation or\nenabling of access etc.\nCommunication—civil court remedy",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If a person (the defendant):\n\n(a) so accessed the communication; or\n\n(b) did an act or thing referred to in subparagraph 108(1)(a)(ii) or\n(iii) in relation to the access;\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the access by making such\norders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate.\nNote:\nSubparagraphs 108(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) deal with the authorisation or\nenabling of access etc.\nCommunication—civil court remedy",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e05de7226f9566c6e3d9f0d4316a6e185253cbd2818c70978230e490e1b9896b",
      "skos:note": "Grant remedial relief in respect of access by defendant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-165-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "165(3) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 360,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If a person (the defendant):\n\n(a) so accessed the communication; or\n\n(b) did an act or thing referred to in subparagraph 108(1)(a)(ii) or\n(iii) in relation to the access;\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the access by making such\norders against the defendant as the court considers appropriate.\nNote:\nSubparagraphs 108(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) deal with the authorisation or\nenabling of access etc.\nCommunication—civil court remedy"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to grant remedial relief",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "165(4) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-165-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.360",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by accessing the communication;\nand\n\n(b) a person (the defendant) communicated the information to\nanother person in contravention of section 133;\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nCivil remedies  Part 3-7\n\nSection 165\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the communication of the\ninformation by making such orders against the defendant as the\ncourt considers appropriate.\nAccess—criminal court remedy",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by accessing the communication;\nand\n\n(b) a person (the defendant) communicated the information to\nanother person in contravention of section 133;\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nCivil remedies  Part 3-7\n\nSection 165\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the communication of the\ninformation by making such orders against the defendant as the\ncourt considers appropriate.\nAccess—criminal court remedy",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5f1fd29353c8d5915e50644e0eacde7e3a1dfc1ec16501eb9b37dfbaaf8e432f",
      "skos:note": "Grant remedial relief against defendant for unlawful access or communication"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-165-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "165(4) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 360,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by accessing the communication;\nand\n\n(b) a person (the defendant) communicated the information to\nanother person in contravention of section 133;\n\nPreserving and accessing stored communications  Chapter 3\nCivil remedies  Part 3-7\n\nSection 165\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe Federal Court of Australia or a court of a State or Territory\nmay, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the aggrieved\nperson remedial relief in respect of the communication of the\ninformation by making such orders against the defendant as the\ncourt considers appropriate.\nAccess—criminal court remedy"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to grant remedial relief",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
