    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "165(5) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-165-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.360",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a court convicts a person (the defendant) of an offence against\nsubsection 108(1) constituted by:\n\n(a) the access; or\n\n(b) the doing of an act or thing referred to in\nsubparagraph 108(1)(a)(ii) or (iii) in relation to the access;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the access by making\nsuch orders against the defendant as the court considers\nappropriate.\nNote:\nSubparagraphs 108(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) deal with the authorisation or\nenabling of access etc.\nCommunication—criminal court remedy",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If a court convicts a person (the defendant) of an offence against\nsubsection 108(1) constituted by:\n\n(a) the access; or\n\n(b) the doing of an act or thing referred to in\nsubparagraph 108(1)(a)(ii) or (iii) in relation to the access;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the access by making\nsuch orders against the defendant as the court considers\nappropriate.\nNote:\nSubparagraphs 108(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) deal with the authorisation or\nenabling of access etc.\nCommunication—criminal court remedy",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c94a245a605a7e86d47c2191406652b0dfb1880bbe34255ac4ec106613a3e972",
      "skos:note": "Court may grant remedial relief to an aggrieved person if convicted of unlawful access or communication."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-165-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "165(5) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 360,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a court convicts a person (the defendant) of an offence against\nsubsection 108(1) constituted by:\n\n(a) the access; or\n\n(b) the doing of an act or thing referred to in\nsubparagraph 108(1)(a)(ii) or (iii) in relation to the access;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the access by making\nsuch orders against the defendant as the court considers\nappropriate.\nNote:\nSubparagraphs 108(1)(a)(ii) and (iii) deal with the authorisation or\nenabling of access etc.\nCommunication—criminal court remedy"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court has an obligation to grant remedial relief.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-165-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "165(6) Civil remedies—unlawful access or communication",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-165-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.360",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by accessing the communication;\nand\n\n(b) the information was communicated to a person in\ncontravention of section 133; and\n\n(c) a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the\ndefendant) of an offence against section 133 constituted by\nthe communication of the information;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the communication\nof the information by making such orders against the defendant as\nthe court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If:\n\n(a) information was obtained by accessing the communication;\nand\n\n(b) the information was communicated to a person in\ncontravention of section 133; and\n\n(c) a court convicts a person (in this subsection called the\ndefendant) of an offence against section 133 constituted by\nthe communication of the information;\nthe court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, grant the\naggrieved person remedial relief in respect of the communication\nof the information by making such orders against the defendant as\nthe court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 3  Preserving and accessing stored communications",
