    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-171",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "171 Outline of Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-171"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.365",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Divisions 3, 4 and 4A set out some circumstances when\nsections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prohibit a disclosure of information or a document.\nNote 1:\nDivision 3 covers the Organisation. Division 4 covers disclosures for\nthe purposes of Australian enforcement agencies. Division 4A covers\ndisclosures for the purposes of foreign law enforcement.\nNote 2:\nThose Divisions do not permit the disclosure of the contents or\nsubstance of a communication: see Division 2.\n\n(2) Division 5 sets out some circumstances when sections 276, 277\nand 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prohibit a use\nof information or a document.\n\n(3) Division 6 creates offences for certain disclosures and uses of\ninformation and documents.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Divisions 3, 4 and 4A set out some circumstances when\nsections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prohibit a disclosure of information or a document.\nNote 1:\nDivision 3 covers the Organisation. Division 4 covers disclosures for\nthe purposes of Australian enforcement agencies. Division 4A covers\ndisclosures for the purposes of foreign law enforcement.\nNote 2:\nThose Divisions do not permit the disclosure of the contents or\nsubstance of a communication: see Division 2.\n\n(2) Division 5 sets out some circumstances when sections 276, 277\nand 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not prohibit a use\nof information or a document.\n\n(3) Division 6 creates offences for certain disclosures and uses of\ninformation and documents.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-171-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-171-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-171-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4201999979a760c0a985986d2c8b24c534b177027c55c607c08311972f3c1321"
    },
