      "cml:integrityHash": "3804d2971782b1af56f18833673e843df2f135bf92ed3843bd7663e044d97b35",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of information under certain circumstances is permitted."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-171-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "171(1) Outline of Part",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 365,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Divisions 3, 4 and 4A set out some circumstances when\nsections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prohibit a disclosure of information or a document.\nNote 1:\nDivision 3 covers the Organisation. Division 4 covers disclosures for\nthe purposes of Australian enforcement agencies. Division 4A covers\ndisclosures for the purposes of foreign law enforcement.\nNote 2:\nThose Divisions do not permit the disclosure of the contents or\nsubstance of a communication: see Division 2."
    },
    {
