      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-174",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "174 Voluntary disclosure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-174"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.367",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prohibit a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or\na document to the Organisation if the disclosure is in connection\nwith the performance by the Organisation of its functions.\nLimitation\n\n(2) This section does not apply if the Director-General of Security, the\nDeputy Director-General of Security or any other ASIO employee\nor ASIO affiliate requests the holder to disclose the information or\ndocument.\nNote:\nSections 175 and 176 deal with the disclosure of information or a\ndocument in response to authorisations by the Organisation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prohibit a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or\na document to the Organisation if the disclosure is in connection\nwith the performance by the Organisation of its functions.\nLimitation\n\n(2) This section does not apply if the Director-General of Security, the\nDeputy Director-General of Security or any other ASIO employee\nor ASIO affiliate requests the holder to disclose the information or\ndocument.\nNote:\nSections 175 and 176 deal with the disclosure of information or a\ndocument in response to authorisations by the Organisation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-174-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-174-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "89ea19e49689656bc791456d3728d732a47ccff812f2b6c51822969579d8ff90"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-174",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "174 Voluntary disclosure",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 367,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prohibit a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or\na document to the Organisation if the disclosure is in connection\nwith the performance by the Organisation of its functions.\nLimitation\n\n(2) This section does not apply if the Director-General of Security, the\nDeputy Director-General of Security or any other ASIO employee\nor ASIO affiliate requests the holder to disclose the information or\ndocument.\nNote:\nSections 175 and 176 deal with the disclosure of information or a\ndocument in response to authorisations by the Organisation."
    },
