    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "176(5) Authorisations for access to prospective information or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-176-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.368",
      "values:originalText": "(5) An authorisation under this section:\n\n(a) comes into force at the time the person from whom the\ndisclosure is sought receives notification of the authorisation;\nand\n\n(b) unless it is revoked earlier, ends at the time specified in the\nauthorisation, which must be a time that:\n\n(i) is no later than the end of the period of 90 days\nbeginning on the day the authorisation is made; and\n\n(ii) if the authorisation is made under a journalist\ninformation warrant—is no later than the end of the\nperiod specified under section 180N as the period for\nwhich the warrant is to remain in force.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\nRevoking the authorisation",
      "skos:definition": "(5) An authorisation under this section:\n\n(a) comes into force at the time the person from whom the\ndisclosure is sought receives notification of the authorisation;\nand\n\n(b) unless it is revoked earlier, ends at the time specified in the\nauthorisation, which must be a time that:\n\n(i) is no later than the end of the period of 90 days\nbeginning on the day the authorisation is made; and\n\n(ii) if the authorisation is made under a journalist\ninformation warrant—is no later than the end of the\nperiod specified under section 180N as the period for\nwhich the warrant is to remain in force.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\nRevoking the authorisation",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b6fb1e8670b499bdd8a79cb4da78bd69f49b3810162fd3d718b6167e5014e0cd",
      "skos:note": "Authorisation under this section comes into force upon notification and ends at the specified time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-176-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "176(5) Authorisations for access to prospective information or",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 368,
      "values:originalText": "(5) An authorisation under this section:\n\n(a) comes into force at the time the person from whom the\ndisclosure is sought receives notification of the authorisation;\nand\n\n(b) unless it is revoked earlier, ends at the time specified in the\nauthorisation, which must be a time that:\n\n(i) is no later than the end of the period of 90 days\nbeginning on the day the authorisation is made; and\n\n(ii) if the authorisation is made under a journalist\ninformation warrant—is no later than the end of the\nperiod specified under section 180N as the period for\nwhich the warrant is to remain in force.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\nRevoking the authorisation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "holds",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authorisation holds from the point of notification.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) comes into force at the time the person from whom the disclosure is sought receives notification of the authorisation;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorisation holds from the point of notification."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "ends",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authorisation ends at the specified time.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) unless it is revoked earlier, ends at the time specified in the authorisation;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorisation ends at the specified time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Time period for authorisation overlaps with the period specified under section 180N.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(ii) if the authorisation is made under a journalist information warrant—is no later than the end of the period specified under section 180N as the period for which the warrant is to remain in force.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The time period for authorisation overlaps with the period specified under section 180N."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "revokes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authorisation can be revoked earlier than the specified time.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Revoking the authorisation",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorisation can be revoked earlier than the specified time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-5-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "holds",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authorisation is held by the State.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "An authorisation under this section:",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorisation is held by the State."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "176(6) Authorisations for access to prospective information or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-176-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.368",
      "values:originalText": "(6) An eligible person must revoke the authorisation if:\n\n(a) he or she is satisfied that the disclosure is no longer required;\nor\n\n(b) in a case where the authorisation is made under a journalist\ninformation warrant:\n\n(i) the warrant is revoked under subsection 180N(1); or\n\n(ii) the Director-General of Security has informed the\nAttorney-General under section 180P that the\nDirector-General is satisfied that the grounds on which\nthe warrant was issued have ceased to exist.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "(6) An eligible person must revoke the authorisation if:\n\n(a) he or she is satisfied that the disclosure is no longer required;\nor\n\n(b) in a case where the authorisation is made under a journalist\ninformation warrant:\n\n(i) the warrant is revoked under subsection 180N(1); or\n\n(ii) the Director-General of Security has informed the\nAttorney-General under section 180P that the\nDirector-General is satisfied that the grounds on which\nthe warrant was issued have ceased to exist.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "73ef95c11e65891f4b463455724101da1e7d6a205c69b85f883adc13446faaf6",
      "skos:note": "Revoke authorisation if disclosure is no longer required or warrant has been revoked."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-176-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "176(6) Authorisations for access to prospective information or",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 368,
      "values:originalText": "(6) An eligible person must revoke the authorisation if:\n\n(a) he or she is satisfied that the disclosure is no longer required;\nor\n\n(b) in a case where the authorisation is made under a journalist\ninformation warrant:\n\n(i) the warrant is revoked under subsection 180N(1); or\n\n(ii) the Director-General of Security has informed the\nAttorney-General under section 180P that the\nDirector-General is satisfied that the grounds on which\nthe warrant was issued have ceased to exist.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"
    },
