    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "176A(4) Meaning of enforcement agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-176a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.370",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In considering whether to make the declaration, the Minister must\nhave regard to:\n\n(b) whether the making of authorisations under section 178 or\n179 would be reasonably likely to assist the authority or body\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nEnforcement agencies  Division 4\n\nSection 176A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nin performing the functions referred to in subsection (3B);\nand\n\n(c) whether the authority or body:\n\n(i) is required to comply with the Australian Privacy\nPrinciples; or\n\n(ii) is required to comply with a binding scheme that\nprovides protection of personal information that meets\nthe requirements of subsection (4A); or\n\n(iii) has agreed in writing to comply with a scheme\nproviding such protection of personal information, in\nrelation to personal information disclosed to it under\nChapter 4, if the declaration is made; and\n\n(d) whether the authority or body proposes to adopt processes\nand practices that would ensure its compliance with the\nobligations of an enforcement agency under Chapter 4; and\n\n(e) whether the Minister considers that the declaration would be\nin the public interest; and\n\n(f) any other matter that the Minister considers relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In considering whether to make the declaration, the Minister must\nhave regard to:\n\n(b) whether the making of authorisations under section 178 or\n179 would be reasonably likely to assist the authority or body\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nEnforcement agencies  Division 4\n\nSection 176A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nin performing the functions referred to in subsection (3B);\nand\n\n(c) whether the authority or body:\n\n(i) is required to comply with the Australian Privacy\nPrinciples; or\n\n(ii) is required to comply with a binding scheme that\nprovides protection of personal information that meets\nthe requirements of subsection (4A); or\n\n(iii) has agreed in writing to comply with a scheme\nproviding such protection of personal information, in\nrelation to personal information disclosed to it under\nChapter 4, if the declaration is made; and\n\n(d) whether the authority or body proposes to adopt processes\nand practices that would ensure its compliance with the\nobligations of an enforcement agency under Chapter 4; and\n\n(e) whether the Minister considers that the declaration would be\nin the public interest; and\n\n(f) any other matter that the Minister considers relevant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4-logic-diffusion-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8f8ba166528490c30822b7a3f25bf6fc7413aac2611d04d3800f68b85292f315",
      "skos:note": "The Minister must consider certain factors when deciding whether to make a declaration."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-176a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "176A(4) Meaning of enforcement agency",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 370,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In considering whether to make the declaration, the Minister must\nhave regard to:\n\n(b) whether the making of authorisations under section 178 or\n179 would be reasonably likely to assist the authority or body\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nEnforcement agencies  Division 4\n\nSection 176A\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nin performing the functions referred to in subsection (3B);\nand\n\n(c) whether the authority or body:\n\n(i) is required to comply with the Australian Privacy\nPrinciples; or\n\n(ii) is required to comply with a binding scheme that\nprovides protection of personal information that meets\nthe requirements of subsection (4A); or\n\n(iii) has agreed in writing to comply with a scheme\nproviding such protection of personal information, in\nrelation to personal information disclosed to it under\nChapter 4, if the declaration is made; and\n\n(d) whether the authority or body proposes to adopt processes\nand practices that would ensure its compliance with the\nobligations of an enforcement agency under Chapter 4; and\n\n(e) whether the Minister considers that the declaration would be\nin the public interest; and\n\n(f) any other matter that the Minister considers relevant."
    },
    {
