      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) whether the authority or body proposes to adopt processes and practices that would ensure its compliance..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4-logic-argumentation-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "IMPLIES",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The Minister's decision implies certain conditions about the authority or body's actions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(e) whether the Minister considers that the declaration would be in the public interest;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "AND",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The declaration must consider multiple factors simultaneously.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(f) any other matter that the Minister considers relevant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "176A(4A) Meaning of enforcement agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-176a-ss-4a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.370",
      "values:originalText": "(4A) For the purposes of subparagraphs (4)(c)(ii) and (iii), the protection\nof personal information provided by the scheme must:\n\n(a) be comparable to the protection provided by the Australian\nPrivacy Principles; and\n\n(b) include a mechanism for monitoring the authority’s or body’s\ncompliance with the scheme; and\n\n(c) include a mechanism that enables an individual to seek\nrecourse if his or her personal information is mishandled.",
      "skos:definition": "(4A) For the purposes of subparagraphs (4)(c)(ii) and (iii), the protection\nof personal information provided by the scheme must:\n\n(a) be comparable to the protection provided by the Australian\nPrivacy Principles; and\n\n(b) include a mechanism for monitoring the authority’s or body’s\ncompliance with the scheme; and\n\n(c) include a mechanism that enables an individual to seek\nrecourse if his or her personal information is mishandled.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-176a-ss-4a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c85c409c425ed78aae1c13426cae9fe53edcd1c8aac3af7fbba3824b8b50139d",
      "skos:note": "Protection of personal information must be comparable to the Australian Privacy Principles.",
      "dc:description": "comparable protection, mechanism for monitoring compliance, and recourse for mishandled information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-176a-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "176A(4A) Meaning of enforcement agency",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 370,
      "values:originalText": "(4A) For the purposes of subparagraphs (4)(c)(ii) and (iii), the protection\nof personal information provided by the scheme must:\n\n(a) be comparable to the protection provided by the Australian\nPrivacy Principles; and\n\n(b) include a mechanism for monitoring the authority’s or body’s\ncompliance with the scheme; and\n\n(c) include a mechanism that enables an individual to seek\nrecourse if his or her personal information is mishandled."
    },
