    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "177 Voluntary disclosure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-177"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.372",
      "values:originalText": "Enforcement of the criminal law\n\n(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or\na document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is\nreasonably necessary for the enforcement of the criminal law.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nEnforcement agencies  Division 4\n\nSection 178\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nEnforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or protection\nof the public revenue\n\n(2) Sections 276 and 277 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not\nprevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or a\ndocument to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is reasonably\nnecessary for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary\npenalty or for the protection of the public revenue.\nLimitation\n\n(3) This section does not apply if a relevant staff member of an\nenforcement agency requests the holder to disclose the information\nor document.\nNote:\nSections 178 to 180 deal with the disclosure of information or a\ndocument in response to authorisations by an authorised officer of an\nenforcement agency.",
      "skos:definition": "Enforcement of the criminal law\n\n(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or\na document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is\nreasonably necessary for the enforcement of the criminal law.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nEnforcement agencies  Division 4\n\nSection 178\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nEnforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or protection\nof the public revenue\n\n(2) Sections 276 and 277 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not\nprevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or a\ndocument to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is reasonably\nnecessary for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary\npenalty or for the protection of the public revenue.\nLimitation\n\n(3) This section does not apply if a relevant staff member of an\nenforcement agency requests the holder to disclose the information\nor document.\nNote:\nSections 178 to 180 deal with the disclosure of information or a\ndocument in response to authorisations by an authorised officer of an\nenforcement agency.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b7b7836deb029f31e8c3b1b967675bde4cbccc8d47a80432c241083b9febef93"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-177",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "177 Voluntary disclosure",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 372,
      "values:originalText": "Enforcement of the criminal law\n\n(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or\na document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is\nreasonably necessary for the enforcement of the criminal law.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nEnforcement agencies  Division 4\n\nSection 178\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nEnforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or protection\nof the public revenue\n\n(2) Sections 276 and 277 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do not\nprevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or a\ndocument to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is reasonably\nnecessary for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary\npenalty or for the protection of the public revenue.\nLimitation\n\n(3) This section does not apply if a relevant staff member of an\nenforcement agency requests the holder to disclose the information\nor document.\nNote:\nSections 178 to 180 deal with the disclosure of information or a\ndocument in response to authorisations by an authorised officer of an\nenforcement agency."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "177(1) Voluntary disclosure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-177-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.372",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or\na document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is\nreasonably necessary for the enforcement of the criminal law.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nEnforcement agencies  Division 4\n\nSection 178\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nEnforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or protection\nof the public revenue",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or\na document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is\nreasonably necessary for the enforcement of the criminal law.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nEnforcement agencies  Division 4\n\nSection 178\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nEnforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or protection\nof the public revenue",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-177-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "71fc5dbb063d326d72c7fcefc5f5b74a628d17c2494c490468fb87b34a65c6e6",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of information or document to enforcement agency is reasonably necessary for the enforcement of criminal law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-177-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "177(1) Voluntary disclosure",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 372,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prevent a disclosure by a person (the holder) of information or\na document to an enforcement agency if the disclosure is\nreasonably necessary for the enforcement of the criminal law.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nEnforcement agencies  Division 4\n\nSection 178\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nEnforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary penalty or protection\nof the public revenue"
    },
