      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the disclosure is reasonably necessary for..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-178a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "178A Authorisations for access to existing information or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-178a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.374",
      "values:originalText": "documents—locating missing persons\n\n(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prevent a disclosure of information or a document if the\ninformation or document is covered by an authorisation in force\nunder subsection (2).\n\n(2) An authorised officer of the Australian Federal Police, or a Police\nForce of a State, may authorise the disclosure of specified\ninformation or specified documents that came into existence before\nthe time the person from whom the disclosure is sought receives\nnotification of the authorisation.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\n\n(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that the disclosure is reasonably necessary for the\npurposes of finding a person who the Australian Federal Police, or\na Police Force of a State, has been notified is missing.",
      "skos:definition": "documents—locating missing persons\n\n(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prevent a disclosure of information or a document if the\ninformation or document is covered by an authorisation in force\nunder subsection (2).\n\n(2) An authorised officer of the Australian Federal Police, or a Police\nForce of a State, may authorise the disclosure of specified\ninformation or specified documents that came into existence before\nthe time the person from whom the disclosure is sought receives\nnotification of the authorisation.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\n\n(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that the disclosure is reasonably necessary for the\npurposes of finding a person who the Australian Federal Police, or\na Police Force of a State, has been notified is missing.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-178a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-178a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-178a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fe180152ec3c320bbbe3781f52a5dbb40fe7d65c1d6b00aafb20bd9d2d12a5ff"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-178a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "178A Authorisations for access to existing information or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 374,
      "values:originalText": "documents—locating missing persons\n\n(1) Sections 276, 277 and 278 of the Telecommunications Act 1997 do\nnot prevent a disclosure of information or a document if the\ninformation or document is covered by an authorisation in force\nunder subsection (2).\n\n(2) An authorised officer of the Australian Federal Police, or a Police\nForce of a State, may authorise the disclosure of specified\ninformation or specified documents that came into existence before\nthe time the person from whom the disclosure is sought receives\nnotification of the authorisation.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\n\n(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that the disclosure is reasonably necessary for the\npurposes of finding a person who the Australian Federal Police, or\na Police Force of a State, has been notified is missing."
    },
