      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.375",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that the disclosure is reasonably necessary for:\n\n(a) in any case—the investigation of a serious offence; or\n\n(b) in any case—the investigation of an offence against a law of\nthe Commonwealth, a State or a Territory that is punishable\nby imprisonment for at least 3 years; or\n\n(c) in the case of an authorised officer of the ACC—the\nperformance of the ACC’s function covered by\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
