    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180B(3) Authorisations for access to prospective information or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180b-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.378",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General has authorised the making of the\nauthorisation under a provision mentioned in an item of the\nfollowing table; and\n\n(b) the authorised officer is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the disclosure is reasonably necessary for an\ninvestigation or proceeding referred to in that table item;\nand\n\n(ii) the disclosure is appropriate in all the circumstances.\n\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nForeign law enforcement  Division 4A\n\nSection 180B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nAuthorising access to prospective information or documents\nItem\nFor Attorney-General\nauthorisations under:\nthe investigation or proceeding is:\nsection 15D of the Mutual\nAssistance in Criminal Matters\nAct 1987\nan investigation or proceeding relating\nto an offence against the law of a\nforeign country that:\n(a) is punishable by imprisonment for 3\nyears or more, imprisonment for\nlife or the death penalty; or\n(b) involves an act or omission that, if\nit had occurred in Australia, would\nbe a serious offence\nsection 78B of the International\nCriminal Court Act 2002\nan investigation or proceeding relating\nto a crime within the jurisdiction of the\nICC\nsection 34B of the International\nWar Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nan investigation or proceeding relating\nto a War Crimes Tribunal offence",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General has authorised the making of the\nauthorisation under a provision mentioned in an item of the\nfollowing table; and\n\n(b) the authorised officer is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the disclosure is reasonably necessary for an\ninvestigation or proceeding referred to in that table item;\nand\n\n(ii) the disclosure is appropriate in all the circumstances.\n\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nForeign law enforcement  Division 4A\n\nSection 180B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nAuthorising access to prospective information or documents\nItem\nFor Attorney-General\nauthorisations under:\nthe investigation or proceeding is:\nsection 15D of the Mutual\nAssistance in Criminal Matters\nAct 1987\nan investigation or proceeding relating\nto an offence against the law of a\nforeign country that:\n(a) is punishable by imprisonment for 3\nyears or more, imprisonment for\nlife or the death penalty; or\n(b) involves an act or omission that, if\nit had occurred in Australia, would\nbe a serious offence\nsection 78B of the International\nCriminal Court Act 2002\nan investigation or proceeding relating\nto a crime within the jurisdiction of the\nICC\nsection 34B of the International\nWar Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nan investigation or proceeding relating\nto a War Crimes Tribunal offence",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b1998e424f1ad8af245eea29015cd66774a833284a74a64d04e0c20e29dccb4",
      "skos:note": "Authorized officer must obtain Attorney-General authorization before making an authorization."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180B(3) Authorisations for access to prospective information or",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 378,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless:\n\n(a) the Attorney-General has authorised the making of the\nauthorisation under a provision mentioned in an item of the\nfollowing table; and\n\n(b) the authorised officer is satisfied that:\n\n(i) the disclosure is reasonably necessary for an\ninvestigation or proceeding referred to in that table item;\nand\n\n(ii) the disclosure is appropriate in all the circumstances.\n\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nForeign law enforcement  Division 4A\n\nSection 180B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nAuthorising access to prospective information or documents\nItem\nFor Attorney-General\nauthorisations under:\nthe investigation or proceeding is:\nsection 15D of the Mutual\nAssistance in Criminal Matters\nAct 1987\nan investigation or proceeding relating\nto an offence against the law of a\nforeign country that:\n(a) is punishable by imprisonment for 3\nyears or more, imprisonment for\nlife or the death penalty; or\n(b) involves an act or omission that, if\nit had occurred in Australia, would\nbe a serious offence\nsection 78B of the International\nCriminal Court Act 2002\nan investigation or proceeding relating\nto a crime within the jurisdiction of the\nICC\nsection 34B of the International\nWar Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nan investigation or proceeding relating\nto a War Crimes Tribunal offence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-3-norm",
