      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Disclosure is no longer required",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Authorised officer must revoke"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180B(5) Authorisations for access to prospective information or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180b-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.378",
      "values:originalText": "(5) An authorisation under subsection (2):\n\n(a) comes into force at the time the person from whom the\ndisclosure is sought receives notification of the authorisation;\nand\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the time specified in the authorisation,\nwhich must not be more than 21 days after the day the\nauthorisation is made, or that period as extended under\nsubsection (6), unless it is revoked earlier.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\nExtension of prospective authorisation",
      "skos:definition": "(5) An authorisation under subsection (2):\n\n(a) comes into force at the time the person from whom the\ndisclosure is sought receives notification of the authorisation;\nand\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the time specified in the authorisation,\nwhich must not be more than 21 days after the day the\nauthorisation is made, or that period as extended under\nsubsection (6), unless it is revoked earlier.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\nExtension of prospective authorisation",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-5-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-5-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-5-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2c47ccd799acb7a59663ae3b57e2c19b41d404beda288ac2ee467f8f52a4f19",
      "skos:note": "Authorisation under subsection (2) comes into force upon notification and ceases after a specified period or is revoked earlier.",
      "dc:references": [
        "sec-184"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180b-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180B(5) Authorisations for access to prospective information or",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 378,
      "values:originalText": "(5) An authorisation under subsection (2):\n\n(a) comes into force at the time the person from whom the\ndisclosure is sought receives notification of the authorisation;\nand\n\n(b) ceases to be in force at the time specified in the authorisation,\nwhich must not be more than 21 days after the day the\nauthorisation is made, or that period as extended under\nsubsection (6), unless it is revoked earlier.\nNote:\nSection 184 deals with notification of authorisations.\nExtension of prospective authorisation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180b-ss-5-norm",
