    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180D Authorisations to disclose information or documents—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.381",
      "values:originalText": "enforcement of the criminal law\n\n(1) If specified information or specified documents are disclosed\nbecause of an authorisation given under this Division, an\nauthorised officer of the Australian Federal Police may authorise\nthe following:\n\n(a) the disclosure of the information or documents to the\nOrganisation or an enforcement agency;\n\n(b) the use of the information or documents by the Australian\nFederal Police.\n\n(2) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure to the Organisation—the\ndisclosure is reasonably necessary for the performance by the\nOrganisation of its functions; and\n\n(b) in the case of a disclosure to an enforcement agency—the\ndisclosure is reasonably necessary:\n\n(i) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or\n\n(ia) for the purposes of Division 105A of the Criminal Code\n(post-sentence orders); or\n\n(ib) for the purposes of Division 395 of the Criminal Code\n(community safety orders); or\n\n(ii) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary\npenalty; or\n\n(iii) for the protection of the public revenue; and\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "enforcement of the criminal law\n\n(1) If specified information or specified documents are disclosed\nbecause of an authorisation given under this Division, an\nauthorised officer of the Australian Federal Police may authorise\nthe following:\n\n(a) the disclosure of the information or documents to the\nOrganisation or an enforcement agency;\n\n(b) the use of the information or documents by the Australian\nFederal Police.\n\n(2) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure to the Organisation—the\ndisclosure is reasonably necessary for the performance by the\nOrganisation of its functions; and\n\n(b) in the case of a disclosure to an enforcement agency—the\ndisclosure is reasonably necessary:\n\n(i) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or\n\n(ia) for the purposes of Division 105A of the Criminal Code\n(post-sentence orders); or\n\n(ib) for the purposes of Division 395 of the Criminal Code\n(community safety orders); or\n\n(ii) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary\npenalty; or\n\n(iii) for the protection of the public revenue; and\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180d-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9dfa33d4f18aaa984da9b23f8557853e89842dd693b67e3ebb64c82b9a21d1d8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180D Authorisations to disclose information or documents—",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 381,
      "values:originalText": "enforcement of the criminal law\n\n(1) If specified information or specified documents are disclosed\nbecause of an authorisation given under this Division, an\nauthorised officer of the Australian Federal Police may authorise\nthe following:\n\n(a) the disclosure of the information or documents to the\nOrganisation or an enforcement agency;\n\n(b) the use of the information or documents by the Australian\nFederal Police.\n\n(2) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless he or\nshe is satisfied that:\n\n(a) in the case of a disclosure to the Organisation—the\ndisclosure is reasonably necessary for the performance by the\nOrganisation of its functions; and\n\n(b) in the case of a disclosure to an enforcement agency—the\ndisclosure is reasonably necessary:\n\n(i) for the enforcement of the criminal law; or\n\n(ia) for the purposes of Division 105A of the Criminal Code\n(post-sentence orders); or\n\n(ib) for the purposes of Division 395 of the Criminal Code\n(community safety orders); or\n\n(ii) for the enforcement of a law imposing a pecuniary\npenalty; or\n\n(iii) for the protection of the public revenue; and\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180d-ss-1",
