    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180E Disclosing information etc. to foreign countries or foreign law",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.382",
      "values:originalText": "enforcement agencies\n\n(1) A person must not disclose information or a document in\naccordance with an authorisation under section 180A, 180B or\n180C to a foreign country or foreign law enforcement agency\nunless the disclosure is subject to the following conditions:\n\n(a) that the information will only be used for the purposes for\nwhich the foreign country or foreign law enforcement agency\nrequested the information;\n\n(b) that any document or other thing containing the information\nwill be destroyed when it is no longer required for those\npurposes;\n\n(c) in the case of information or a document disclosed under\nsection 180B—any other condition determined, in writing, by\nthe Attorney-General.\n\n(2) A determination made under paragraph (1)(c) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nPrivacy to be considered when making authorisations  Division 4B\n\nSection 180F\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "enforcement agencies\n\n(1) A person must not disclose information or a document in\naccordance with an authorisation under section 180A, 180B or\n180C to a foreign country or foreign law enforcement agency\nunless the disclosure is subject to the following conditions:\n\n(a) that the information will only be used for the purposes for\nwhich the foreign country or foreign law enforcement agency\nrequested the information;\n\n(b) that any document or other thing containing the information\nwill be destroyed when it is no longer required for those\npurposes;\n\n(c) in the case of information or a document disclosed under\nsection 180B—any other condition determined, in writing, by\nthe Attorney-General.\n\n(2) A determination made under paragraph (1)(c) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nPrivacy to be considered when making authorisations  Division 4B\n\nSection 180F\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180e-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0cced6ed77be747d3b1f163daa10d980c5120a5fe65e4b95fc70fd947456f90d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180E Disclosing information etc. to foreign countries or foreign law",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 382,
      "values:originalText": "enforcement agencies\n\n(1) A person must not disclose information or a document in\naccordance with an authorisation under section 180A, 180B or\n180C to a foreign country or foreign law enforcement agency\nunless the disclosure is subject to the following conditions:\n\n(a) that the information will only be used for the purposes for\nwhich the foreign country or foreign law enforcement agency\nrequested the information;\n\n(b) that any document or other thing containing the information\nwill be destroyed when it is no longer required for those\npurposes;\n\n(c) in the case of information or a document disclosed under\nsection 180B—any other condition determined, in writing, by\nthe Attorney-General.\n\n(2) A determination made under paragraph (1)(c) is not a legislative\ninstrument.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nPrivacy to be considered when making authorisations  Division 4B\n\nSection 180F\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
