      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180F Authorised officers to consider privacy",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.383",
      "values:originalText": "Before making an authorisation under Division 4 or 4A in relation\nto the disclosure or use of information or documents, the\nauthorised officer considering making the authorisation must be\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that any interference with the\nprivacy of any person or persons that may result from the\ndisclosure or use is justifiable and proportionate, having regard to\nthe following matters:\n\n(aa) the gravity of any conduct in relation to which the\nauthorisation is sought, including:\n\n(i) the seriousness of any offence in relation to which the\nauthorisation is sought; and\n\n(ii) the seriousness of any pecuniary penalty in relation to\nwhich the authorisation is sought; and\n\n(iii) the seriousness of any protection of the public revenue\nin relation to which the authorisation is sought; and\n\n(iv) whether the authorisation is sought for the purposes of\nfinding a missing person;\n\n(a) the likely relevance and usefulness of the information or\ndocuments;\n\n(b) the reason why the disclosure or use concerned is proposed to\nbe authorised.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "Before making an authorisation under Division 4 or 4A in relation\nto the disclosure or use of information or documents, the\nauthorised officer considering making the authorisation must be\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that any interference with the\nprivacy of any person or persons that may result from the\ndisclosure or use is justifiable and proportionate, having regard to\nthe following matters:\n\n(aa) the gravity of any conduct in relation to which the\nauthorisation is sought, including:\n\n(i) the seriousness of any offence in relation to which the\nauthorisation is sought; and\n\n(ii) the seriousness of any pecuniary penalty in relation to\nwhich the authorisation is sought; and\n\n(iii) the seriousness of any protection of the public revenue\nin relation to which the authorisation is sought; and\n\n(iv) whether the authorisation is sought for the purposes of\nfinding a missing person;\n\n(a) the likely relevance and usefulness of the information or\ndocuments;\n\n(b) the reason why the disclosure or use concerned is proposed to\nbe authorised.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180f-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180f-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1673e43d5b41915545c0bf7963ed3a5eff060b4df50222e28c2a35c4f7b382ad",
      "skos:note": "Authorised officers must consider privacy before making an authorisation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180F Authorised officers to consider privacy",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 383,
      "values:originalText": "Before making an authorisation under Division 4 or 4A in relation\nto the disclosure or use of information or documents, the\nauthorised officer considering making the authorisation must be\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that any interference with the\nprivacy of any person or persons that may result from the\ndisclosure or use is justifiable and proportionate, having regard to\nthe following matters:\n\n(aa) the gravity of any conduct in relation to which the\nauthorisation is sought, including:\n\n(i) the seriousness of any offence in relation to which the\nauthorisation is sought; and\n\n(ii) the seriousness of any pecuniary penalty in relation to\nwhich the authorisation is sought; and\n\n(iii) the seriousness of any protection of the public revenue\nin relation to which the authorisation is sought; and\n\n(iv) whether the authorisation is sought for the purposes of\nfinding a missing person;\n\n(a) the likely relevance and usefulness of the information or\ndocuments;\n\n(b) the reason why the disclosure or use concerned is proposed to\nbe authorised.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180f-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180f"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180f-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Duty to consider privacy",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Authorised officers must be satisfied on reasonable grounds",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Privacy must be considered"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180G The Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.384",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An eligible person (within the meaning of subsection 175(2) or\n176(2), as the case requires) must not make an authorisation under\nDivision 3 that would authorise the disclosure of information or\ndocuments relating to a particular person if:\n\n(a) the eligible person knows or reasonably believes that\nparticular person to be:\n\n(i) a person who is working in a professional capacity as a\njournalist; or\n\n(ii) an employer of such a person; and\n\n(b) a purpose of making the authorisation would be to identify\nanother person whom the eligible person knows or\nreasonably believes to be a source;\nunless a journalist information warrant is in force in relation to that\nparticular person.\n\n(2) Nothing in this section affects by implication the kind of person in\nrelation to whom a warrant (other than a journalist information\nwarrant) may be issued under this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An eligible person (within the meaning of subsection 175(2) or\n176(2), as the case requires) must not make an authorisation under\nDivision 3 that would authorise the disclosure of information or\ndocuments relating to a particular person if:\n\n(a) the eligible person knows or reasonably believes that\nparticular person to be:\n\n(i) a person who is working in a professional capacity as a\njournalist; or\n\n(ii) an employer of such a person; and\n\n(b) a purpose of making the authorisation would be to identify\nanother person whom the eligible person knows or\nreasonably believes to be a source;\nunless a journalist information warrant is in force in relation to that\nparticular person.\n\n(2) Nothing in this section affects by implication the kind of person in\nrelation to whom a warrant (other than a journalist information\nwarrant) may be issued under this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180g-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "98adb1db1db73b67559b606340825317052899b4729c3ece83855fed21de9f01"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180G The Organisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 384,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An eligible person (within the meaning of subsection 175(2) or\n176(2), as the case requires) must not make an authorisation under\nDivision 3 that would authorise the disclosure of information or\ndocuments relating to a particular person if:\n\n(a) the eligible person knows or reasonably believes that\nparticular person to be:\n\n(i) a person who is working in a professional capacity as a\njournalist; or\n\n(ii) an employer of such a person; and\n\n(b) a purpose of making the authorisation would be to identify\nanother person whom the eligible person knows or\nreasonably believes to be a source;\nunless a journalist information warrant is in force in relation to that\nparticular person.\n\n(2) Nothing in this section affects by implication the kind of person in\nrelation to whom a warrant (other than a journalist information\nwarrant) may be issued under this Act."
    },
