    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180M Issuing a journalist information warrant in an emergency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.387",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General of Security may issue a journalist\ninformation warrant in relation to a particular person if:\n\n(a) a request under section 180J has been made for the issue of a\njournalist information warrant in relation to the particular\nperson; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General has not, to the knowledge of the\nDirector-General, made a decision under section 180L in\nrelation to the request; and\n\n(c) within the preceding period of 3 months:\n\n(i) the Attorney-General has not refused to issue a\njournalist information warrant in relation to the\nparticular person; and\n\n(ii) the Director-General has not issued such a journalist\ninformation warrant; and\n\n(d) the Director-General is satisfied that, security will be, or is\nlikely to be, seriously prejudiced if the access to which the\nrequest relates does not begin before a journalist information\nwarrant can be issued and made available by the\nAttorney-General; and\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General of Security may issue a journalist\ninformation warrant in relation to a particular person if:\n\n(a) a request under section 180J has been made for the issue of a\njournalist information warrant in relation to the particular\nperson; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General has not, to the knowledge of the\nDirector-General, made a decision under section 180L in\nrelation to the request; and\n\n(c) within the preceding period of 3 months:\n\n(i) the Attorney-General has not refused to issue a\njournalist information warrant in relation to the\nparticular person; and\n\n(ii) the Director-General has not issued such a journalist\ninformation warrant; and\n\n(d) the Director-General is satisfied that, security will be, or is\nlikely to be, seriously prejudiced if the access to which the\nrequest relates does not begin before a journalist information\nwarrant can be issued and made available by the\nAttorney-General; and\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180m-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180m-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9106cb98ccf188f2817f373c91b1c3aa3c8010879d524dc50e4afab1af056e22",
      "skos:note": "The Director-General must issue a journalist information warrant in an emergency."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180M Issuing a journalist information warrant in an emergency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 387,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General of Security may issue a journalist\ninformation warrant in relation to a particular person if:\n\n(a) a request under section 180J has been made for the issue of a\njournalist information warrant in relation to the particular\nperson; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General has not, to the knowledge of the\nDirector-General, made a decision under section 180L in\nrelation to the request; and\n\n(c) within the preceding period of 3 months:\n\n(i) the Attorney-General has not refused to issue a\njournalist information warrant in relation to the\nparticular person; and\n\n(ii) the Director-General has not issued such a journalist\ninformation warrant; and\n\n(d) the Director-General is satisfied that, security will be, or is\nlikely to be, seriously prejudiced if the access to which the\nrequest relates does not begin before a journalist information\nwarrant can be issued and made available by the\nAttorney-General; and\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"
    },
    {
