      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180n",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180N Duration of a journalist information warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180n"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.389",
      "values:originalText": "A journalist information warrant issued under section 180L must\nspecify the period (not exceeding 6 months) for which it is to\nremain in force. The Attorney-General may revoke the warrant at\nany time before the end of the specified period.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "A journalist information warrant issued under section 180L must\nspecify the period (not exceeding 6 months) for which it is to\nremain in force. The Attorney-General may revoke the warrant at\nany time before the end of the specified period.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180n-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180n-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ef76b301a5224710f9639c44b9601c82f1308c2725e271cefa2b9d4394cdf946",
      "skos:note": "A journalist information warrant must specify a duration of up to 6 months.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180n",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180N Duration of a journalist information warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 389,
      "values:originalText": "A journalist information warrant issued under section 180L must\nspecify the period (not exceeding 6 months) for which it is to\nremain in force. The Attorney-General may revoke the warrant at\nany time before the end of the specified period.\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180n-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180n"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180n-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide a duration",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180P Discontinuance of authorisations before expiry of a journalist",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.390",
      "values:originalText": "information warrant\n\nIf, before a journalist information warrant issued under this\nSubdivision ceases to be in force, the Director-General of Security\nis satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have\nceased to exist, he or she must:\n\n(a) forthwith inform the Attorney-General accordingly; and\n\n(b) takes such steps as are necessary to ensure that the making of\nauthorisations under the authority of the warrant is\ndiscontinued.\nSubdivision C—Issuing journalist information warrants to\nenforcement agencies",
      "skos:definition": "information warrant\n\nIf, before a journalist information warrant issued under this\nSubdivision ceases to be in force, the Director-General of Security\nis satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have\nceased to exist, he or she must:\n\n(a) forthwith inform the Attorney-General accordingly; and\n\n(b) takes such steps as are necessary to ensure that the making of\nauthorisations under the authority of the warrant is\ndiscontinued.\nSubdivision C—Issuing journalist information warrants to\nenforcement agencies",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180p-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180p-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3d9e04ac433c8627e04b29822588847680302edcfe3a54bee196b790119751fe",
      "skos:note": "Ensure discontinuation of authorisations upon warrant expiry"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180P Discontinuance of authorisations before expiry of a journalist",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 390,
      "values:originalText": "information warrant\n\nIf, before a journalist information warrant issued under this\nSubdivision ceases to be in force, the Director-General of Security\nis satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have\nceased to exist, he or she must:\n\n(a) forthwith inform the Attorney-General accordingly; and\n\n(b) takes such steps as are necessary to ensure that the making of\nauthorisations under the authority of the warrant is\ndiscontinued.\nSubdivision C—Issuing journalist information warrants to\nenforcement agencies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180p-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180p"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180p-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to ensure discontinuation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180Q Enforcement agency may apply for a journalist information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.390",
      "values:originalText": "warrant\n\n(1) An enforcement agency may apply to a Part 4-1 issuing authority\nfor a journalist information warrant in relation to a particular\nperson.\n\n(2) The application must be made on the agency’s behalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subsection 39(2)—a person\nreferred to in that subsection in relation to that agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The chief officer of the agency may, in writing, nominate for the\npurposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) an office or position in the\nagency that is involved in the management of the agency.\n\n(4) A nomination under subsection (3) is not a legislative instrument.\n\n(5) The application may be made in writing or in any other form.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nJournalist information warrants  Division 4C\n\nSection 180R\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nThe Electronic Transactions Act 1999 deals with giving information\nin writing by means of an electronic communication.",
      "skos:definition": "warrant\n\n(1) An enforcement agency may apply to a Part 4-1 issuing authority\nfor a journalist information warrant in relation to a particular\nperson.\n\n(2) The application must be made on the agency’s behalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subsection 39(2)—a person\nreferred to in that subsection in relation to that agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The chief officer of the agency may, in writing, nominate for the\npurposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) an office or position in the\nagency that is involved in the management of the agency.\n\n(4) A nomination under subsection (3) is not a legislative instrument.\n\n(5) The application may be made in writing or in any other form.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nJournalist information warrants  Division 4C\n\nSection 180R\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nThe Electronic Transactions Act 1999 deals with giving information\nin writing by means of an electronic communication.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180q-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180q-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180q-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180q-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d9bceb39819ed7a46968c3f9b31b50cfcf09492d3472ea264640caad3d3609c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180Q Enforcement agency may apply for a journalist information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 390,
      "values:originalText": "warrant\n\n(1) An enforcement agency may apply to a Part 4-1 issuing authority\nfor a journalist information warrant in relation to a particular\nperson.\n\n(2) The application must be made on the agency’s behalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subsection 39(2)—a person\nreferred to in that subsection in relation to that agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The chief officer of the agency may, in writing, nominate for the\npurposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) an office or position in the\nagency that is involved in the management of the agency.\n\n(4) A nomination under subsection (3) is not a legislative instrument.\n\n(5) The application may be made in writing or in any other form.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nJournalist information warrants  Division 4C\n\nSection 180R\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nThe Electronic Transactions Act 1999 deals with giving information\nin writing by means of an electronic communication."
    },
