    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "180T Issuing a journalist information warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.391",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After considering an application under section 180Q, the Part 4-1\nissuing authority must:\n\n(a) issue a journalist information warrant that authorises the\nmaking of authorisations under one or more of sections 178,\n178A, 179 and 180 in relation to the particular person to\nwhich the application relates; or\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After considering an application under section 180Q, the Part 4-1\nissuing authority must:\n\n(a) issue a journalist information warrant that authorises the\nmaking of authorisations under one or more of sections 178,\n178A, 179 and 180 in relation to the particular person to\nwhich the application relates; or\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180t-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180t-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b07ca77328d24575419862d8237b8821d2bea5582864ac3a1e4940274e050006",
      "skos:note": "Authority must issue a journalist information warrant upon application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180T Issuing a journalist information warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 391,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After considering an application under section 180Q, the Part 4-1\nissuing authority must:\n\n(a) issue a journalist information warrant that authorises the\nmaking of authorisations under one or more of sections 178,\n178A, 179 and 180 in relation to the particular person to\nwhich the application relates; or\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data"
    },
    {
