          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180x-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180x-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-180x-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "baac27bbda47d5fa264c6f526401ba720c47f520d1d4266b376af4f0392e99e1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-180x",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "180X Public Interest Advocates",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 394,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Prime Minister shall declare, in writing, one or more persons\nto be Public Interest Advocates.\n\n(2) A Public Interest Advocate may make submissions:\n\n(a) to the Attorney-General about matters relevant to:\n\n(i) a decision to issue, or refuse to issue, a journalist\ninformation warrant under section 180L; or\n\n(ii) a decision about the conditions or restrictions (if any)\nthat are to be specified in such a warrant; or\n\n(b) to a Part 4-1 issuing authority about matters relevant to:\n\n(i) a decision to issue, or refuse to issue, the warrant under\nsection 180T; or\n\n(ii) a decision about the conditions or restrictions (if any)\nthat are to be specified in such a warrant.\n\n(3) The regulations may prescribe matters relating to the performance\nof the role of a Public Interest Advocate.\n\n(4) A declaration under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nUses of telecommunications data connected with provision of access  Division 5\n\nSection 181\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
