      "values:originalText": "(2) A Public Interest Advocate may make submissions:\n\n(a) to the Attorney-General about matters relevant to:\n\n(i) a decision to issue, or refuse to issue, a journalist\ninformation warrant under section 180L; or\n\n(ii) a decision about the conditions or restrictions (if any)\nthat are to be specified in such a warrant; or\n\n(b) to a Part 4-1 issuing authority about matters relevant to:\n\n(i) a decision to issue, or refuse to issue, the warrant under\nsection 180T; or\n\n(ii) a decision about the conditions or restrictions (if any)\nthat are to be specified in such a warrant."
