    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-182",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "182 Secondary disclosure/use offence: disclosures under Division 4",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-182"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.401",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) information or a document is disclosed to the person as\npermitted by Division 4 or 4A; and\n\n(b) the person discloses or uses the information or document.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\nExempt disclosures\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a disclosure of non-missing\nperson information if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is reasonably necessary:\n\n(i) for a person to comply with his or her obligations under\nsection 185D or 185E; or\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) information or a document is disclosed to the person as\npermitted by Division 4 or 4A; and\n\n(b) the person discloses or uses the information or document.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\nExempt disclosures\n\n(2) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a disclosure of non-missing\nperson information if:\n\n(a) the disclosure is reasonably necessary:\n\n(i) for a person to comply with his or her obligations under\nsection 185D or 185E; or\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
