    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-182a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "182A Disclosure/use offences: journalist information warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-182a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.404",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses or uses information; and\n\n(b) the information is about any of the following:\n\n(i) whether a journalist information warrant (other than\nsuch a warrant that relates only to section 178A) has\nbeen, or is being, requested or applied for;\n\n(ii) the making of such a warrant;\n\n(iii) the existence or non-existence of such a warrant;\n\n(iv) the revocation of such a warrant.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses or uses a document; and\n\n(b) the document consists (wholly or partly) of any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(i) a journalist information warrant (other than such a\nwarrant that relates only to section 178A);\n\n(ii) the revocation of such a warrant.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nDisclosure/use offences  Division 6\n\nSection 182B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses or uses information; and\n\n(b) the information is about any of the following:\n\n(i) whether a journalist information warrant (other than\nsuch a warrant that relates only to section 178A) has\nbeen, or is being, requested or applied for;\n\n(ii) the making of such a warrant;\n\n(iii) the existence or non-existence of such a warrant;\n\n(iv) the revocation of such a warrant.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses or uses a document; and\n\n(b) the document consists (wholly or partly) of any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(i) a journalist information warrant (other than such a\nwarrant that relates only to section 178A);\n\n(ii) the revocation of such a warrant.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nDisclosure/use offences  Division 6\n\nSection 182B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-182a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-182a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bca844c6c50ceafffb193c9ad28180f16dcee84ff0a1edd8e50302e17e4edc08"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-182a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "182A Disclosure/use offences: journalist information warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 404,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses or uses information; and\n\n(b) the information is about any of the following:\n\n(i) whether a journalist information warrant (other than\nsuch a warrant that relates only to section 178A) has\nbeen, or is being, requested or applied for;\n\n(ii) the making of such a warrant;\n\n(iii) the existence or non-existence of such a warrant;\n\n(iv) the revocation of such a warrant.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person discloses or uses a document; and\n\n(b) the document consists (wholly or partly) of any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(i) a journalist information warrant (other than such a\nwarrant that relates only to section 178A);\n\n(ii) the revocation of such a warrant.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\nAccess to telecommunications data  Chapter 4\nPermitted access to telecommunications data  Part 4-1\nDisclosure/use offences  Division 6\n\nSection 182B\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
