      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-183",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "183 Form of authorisations and notifications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-183"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.406",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) an authorisation under Division 3, 4 or 4A of Part 4-1;\n\n(b) the notification of such an authorisation;\n\n(c) the revocation of such an authorisation;\n\n(d) the notification of such a revocation;\nmust:\n\n(e) be in written form or in electronic form (for example, email);\nand\n\n(f) comply with such requirements as are determined under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator may, by legislative\ninstrument, determine requirements for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(f).\n\n(3) A Communications Access Coordinator must consult the ACMA\nand the Information Commissioner in relation to matters that relate\nto the privacy functions (within the meaning of the Australian\nInformation Commissioner Act 2010) before a determination is\nmade under subsection (2).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) an authorisation under Division 3, 4 or 4A of Part 4-1;\n\n(b) the notification of such an authorisation;\n\n(c) the revocation of such an authorisation;\n\n(d) the notification of such a revocation;\nmust:\n\n(e) be in written form or in electronic form (for example, email);\nand\n\n(f) comply with such requirements as are determined under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator may, by legislative\ninstrument, determine requirements for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(f).\n\n(3) A Communications Access Coordinator must consult the ACMA\nand the Information Commissioner in relation to matters that relate\nto the privacy functions (within the meaning of the Australian\nInformation Commissioner Act 2010) before a determination is\nmade under subsection (2).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-183-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-183-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-183-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d6f11036b20d384bd4087a319e7e4a102872b63aeea4cc6fc1235de2805705a2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-183",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "183 Form of authorisations and notifications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 406,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) an authorisation under Division 3, 4 or 4A of Part 4-1;\n\n(b) the notification of such an authorisation;\n\n(c) the revocation of such an authorisation;\n\n(d) the notification of such a revocation;\nmust:\n\n(e) be in written form or in electronic form (for example, email);\nand\n\n(f) comply with such requirements as are determined under\nsubsection (2).\n\n(2) A Communications Access Coordinator may, by legislative\ninstrument, determine requirements for the purposes of\nparagraph (1)(f).\n\n(3) A Communications Access Coordinator must consult the ACMA\nand the Information Commissioner in relation to matters that relate\nto the privacy functions (within the meaning of the Australian\nInformation Commissioner Act 2010) before a determination is\nmade under subsection (2)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-183-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "183(1) Form of authorisations and notifications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-183-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.406",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) an authorisation under Division 3, 4 or 4A of Part 4-1;\n\n(b) the notification of such an authorisation;\n\n(c) the revocation of such an authorisation;\n\n(d) the notification of such a revocation;\nmust:\n\n(e) be in written form or in electronic form (for example, email);\nand\n\n(f) comply with such requirements as are determined under\nsubsection (2).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) an authorisation under Division 3, 4 or 4A of Part 4-1;\n\n(b) the notification of such an authorisation;\n\n(c) the revocation of such an authorisation;\n\n(d) the notification of such a revocation;\nmust:\n\n(e) be in written form or in electronic form (for example, email);\nand\n\n(f) comply with such requirements as are determined under\nsubsection (2).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-183"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-183-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-183-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "90bc720f5fd07d8a840a0a2ae62fb3a6f3691f227280554e9a3a104560b1bc8a",
      "skos:note": "Written form or electronic form of authorisation and revocation notifications must comply with requirements.",
      "dc:description": "written form or electronic form"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-183-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "183(1) Form of authorisations and notifications",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 406,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) an authorisation under Division 3, 4 or 4A of Part 4-1;\n\n(b) the notification of such an authorisation;\n\n(c) the revocation of such an authorisation;\n\n(d) the notification of such a revocation;\nmust:\n\n(e) be in written form or in electronic form (for example, email);\nand\n\n(f) comply with such requirements as are determined under\nsubsection (2)."
    },
