    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "185A Evidentiary certificates relating to acts by carriers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-185a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.408",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier or a body corporate of\nwhich the carrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(b) the secretary of a carrier or a body corporate of which the\ncarrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(c) an employee of a carrier authorised in writing for the\npurposes of this paragraph by a person referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b);\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\ndone by, or in relation to, employees of the carrier in order to\nenable the disclosure of information or a document covered by an\nauthorisation in force under a provision of Division 3 or 4 of",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier or a body corporate of\nwhich the carrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(b) the secretary of a carrier or a body corporate of which the\ncarrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(c) an employee of a carrier authorised in writing for the\npurposes of this paragraph by a person referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b);\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\ndone by, or in relation to, employees of the carrier in order to\nenable the disclosure of information or a document covered by an\nauthorisation in force under a provision of Division 3 or 4 of",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "64048c17d210fae68d9a785259762fd25409d73cfc819507029567ebff58df29",
      "skos:note": "Authorized personnel may issue written certificates"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-185a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "185A Evidentiary certificates relating to acts by carriers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 408,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The following:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier or a body corporate of\nwhich the carrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(b) the secretary of a carrier or a body corporate of which the\ncarrier is a subsidiary;\n\n(c) an employee of a carrier authorised in writing for the\npurposes of this paragraph by a person referred to in\nparagraph (a) or (b);\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\ndone by, or in relation to, employees of the carrier in order to\nenable the disclosure of information or a document covered by an\nauthorisation in force under a provision of Division 3 or 4 of"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to issue certificates",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "185B Evidentiary certificates relating to acts by the Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-185b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.409",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General of Security or the Deputy Director-General\nof Security may issue a written certificate signed by him or her\nsetting out such facts as he or she considers relevant with respect\nto:\n\n(a) anything done by an ASIO employee or ASIO affiliate in\nconnection with the disclosure of information or a document\ncovered by an authorisation in force under a provision of\nDivision 3 or 4 of Part 4-1; or\n\n(b) anything done by an ASIO employee or ASIO affiliate in\nconnection with:\n\n(i) the communication by a person to another person of\ninformation, or information contained in a document,\ncovered by such an authorisation; or\n\n(ii) the making use of such information; or\n\n(iii) the making of a record of such information; or\n\n(iv) the custody of a record of such information; or\n\n(v) the giving in evidence of such information.\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubsection (1) by the Director-General of Security or the Deputy\nDirector-General of Security and to be signed by him or her:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) is, in an exempt proceeding, prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General of Security or the Deputy Director-General\nof Security may issue a written certificate signed by him or her\nsetting out such facts as he or she considers relevant with respect\nto:\n\n(a) anything done by an ASIO employee or ASIO affiliate in\nconnection with the disclosure of information or a document\ncovered by an authorisation in force under a provision of\nDivision 3 or 4 of Part 4-1; or\n\n(b) anything done by an ASIO employee or ASIO affiliate in\nconnection with:\n\n(i) the communication by a person to another person of\ninformation, or information contained in a document,\ncovered by such an authorisation; or\n\n(ii) the making use of such information; or\n\n(iii) the making of a record of such information; or\n\n(iv) the custody of a record of such information; or\n\n(v) the giving in evidence of such information.\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubsection (1) by the Director-General of Security or the Deputy\nDirector-General of Security and to be signed by him or her:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) is, in an exempt proceeding, prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b72d54cc337469949d138438f73afc071fac3dcd9aecfaa6aa91afd0defdcbb5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-185b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "185B Evidentiary certificates relating to acts by the Organisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 409,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General of Security or the Deputy Director-General\nof Security may issue a written certificate signed by him or her\nsetting out such facts as he or she considers relevant with respect\nto:\n\n(a) anything done by an ASIO employee or ASIO affiliate in\nconnection with the disclosure of information or a document\ncovered by an authorisation in force under a provision of\nDivision 3 or 4 of Part 4-1; or\n\n(b) anything done by an ASIO employee or ASIO affiliate in\nconnection with:\n\n(i) the communication by a person to another person of\ninformation, or information contained in a document,\ncovered by such an authorisation; or\n\n(ii) the making use of such information; or\n\n(iii) the making of a record of such information; or\n\n(iv) the custody of a record of such information; or\n\n(v) the giving in evidence of such information.\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubsection (1) by the Director-General of Security or the Deputy\nDirector-General of Security and to be signed by him or her:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) is, in an exempt proceeding, prima facie evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document."
    },
