    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-185d-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "185D(1) Notification etc. of authorisations intended to identify media",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 410,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a journalist information warrant is issued under Subdivision B of\nDivision 4C of Part 4-1:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security must, as soon as practicable,\ngive a copy of the warrant to the Inspector-General of\nIntelligence and Security; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General must, as soon as practicable, cause the\nParliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security\nto be notified of the issuing of the warrant."
