    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185d-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "185D(5) Notification etc. of authorisations intended to identify media",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-185d-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.410",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a journalist information warrant is issued to an enforcement\nagency:\n\n(aa) if the agency was the ACC:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the ACC must, as soon as\npracticable, give copies of the warrant to the Minister\nand the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security;\nand\n\n(ii) the Minister must, as soon as practicable after receiving\na copy, cause the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nIntelligence and Security to be notified of the issuing of\nthe warrant; and\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If a journalist information warrant is issued to an enforcement\nagency:\n\n(aa) if the agency was the ACC:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the ACC must, as soon as\npracticable, give copies of the warrant to the Minister\nand the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security;\nand\n\n(ii) the Minister must, as soon as practicable after receiving\na copy, cause the Parliamentary Joint Committee on\nIntelligence and Security to be notified of the issuing of\nthe warrant; and\n\nChapter 4  Access to telecommunications data",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-185d"
