    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "186B(2) Inspection of records",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-186b-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.421",
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this section, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) after notifying the chief officer of the agency, may enter at\nany reasonable time premises occupied by the agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the agency that are relevant to the inspection;\nand\n\n(c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to\ntake extracts from, records of the agency; and\n\n(d) may require a member of staff of the agency to give the\nOmbudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers\nnecessary, being information:\n\n(i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the\nmember has access; and\n\n(ii) that is relevant to the inspection.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this section, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) after notifying the chief officer of the agency, may enter at\nany reasonable time premises occupied by the agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the agency that are relevant to the inspection;\nand\n\n(c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to\ntake extracts from, records of the agency; and\n\n(d) may require a member of staff of the agency to give the\nOmbudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers\nnecessary, being information:\n\n(i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the\nmember has access; and\n\n(ii) that is relevant to the inspection.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186b-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a7f4c13f9abc28e3a2675eb1eb1d2094985fe011c0675f9afa95a58b104e3880",
      "skos:note": "Ombudsman may enter premises, access records, and require staff information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-186b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "186B(2) Inspection of records",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 421,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this section, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) after notifying the chief officer of the agency, may enter at\nany reasonable time premises occupied by the agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the agency that are relevant to the inspection;\nand\n\n(c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to\ntake extracts from, records of the agency; and\n\n(d) may require a member of staff of the agency to give the\nOmbudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers\nnecessary, being information:\n\n(i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the\nmember has access; and\n\n(ii) that is relevant to the inspection."
    },
