      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "186C Power to obtain relevant information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-186c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.423",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Ombudsman has reasonable grounds to believe that an\nofficer of a particular enforcement agency is able to give\ninformation relevant to an inspection under this Chapter of the\nagency’s records, the Ombudsman may:\n\n(a) if the Ombudsman knows the officer’s identity—by writing\ngiven to the officer, require the officer to do one or both of\nthe following:\n\n(i) give the information to the Ombudsman, by writing\nsigned by the officer, at a specified place and within a\nspecified period;\n\n(ii) attend before a specified inspecting officer to answer\nquestions relevant to the inspection; or\n\n(b) if the Ombudsman does not know the officer’s identity—\nrequire the chief officer of the agency, or a person nominated\nby the chief officer, to attend before a specified inspecting\nofficer to answer questions relevant to the inspection.\n\n(2) A requirement under subsection (1) to attend before an inspecting\nofficer must specify:\n\n(a) a place for the attendance; and\n\n(b) a period within which, or a time and day when, the\nattendance is to occur.\nThe place, and the period or the time and day, must be reasonable\nhaving regard to the circumstances in which the requirement is\nmade.\n\n(3) A person must not refuse:\n\n(a) to attend before a person; or\n\n(b) to give information; or\n\n(c) to answer questions;\nwhen required to do so under this section.\n\nChapter 4A  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman\n\nSection 186D\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPenalty for an offence against this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Ombudsman has reasonable grounds to believe that an\nofficer of a particular enforcement agency is able to give\ninformation relevant to an inspection under this Chapter of the\nagency’s records, the Ombudsman may:\n\n(a) if the Ombudsman knows the officer’s identity—by writing\ngiven to the officer, require the officer to do one or both of\nthe following:\n\n(i) give the information to the Ombudsman, by writing\nsigned by the officer, at a specified place and within a\nspecified period;\n\n(ii) attend before a specified inspecting officer to answer\nquestions relevant to the inspection; or\n\n(b) if the Ombudsman does not know the officer’s identity—\nrequire the chief officer of the agency, or a person nominated\nby the chief officer, to attend before a specified inspecting\nofficer to answer questions relevant to the inspection.\n\n(2) A requirement under subsection (1) to attend before an inspecting\nofficer must specify:\n\n(a) a place for the attendance; and\n\n(b) a period within which, or a time and day when, the\nattendance is to occur.\nThe place, and the period or the time and day, must be reasonable\nhaving regard to the circumstances in which the requirement is\nmade.\n\n(3) A person must not refuse:\n\n(a) to attend before a person; or\n\n(b) to give information; or\n\n(c) to answer questions;\nwhen required to do so under this section.\n\nChapter 4A  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman\n\nSection 186D\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPenalty for an offence against this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "49a8e371b15df678b7bd74c75da90b30bd8d3b5ffb9d5e6c0b8a1621391e1025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-186c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "186C Power to obtain relevant information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 423,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Ombudsman has reasonable grounds to believe that an\nofficer of a particular enforcement agency is able to give\ninformation relevant to an inspection under this Chapter of the\nagency’s records, the Ombudsman may:\n\n(a) if the Ombudsman knows the officer’s identity—by writing\ngiven to the officer, require the officer to do one or both of\nthe following:\n\n(i) give the information to the Ombudsman, by writing\nsigned by the officer, at a specified place and within a\nspecified period;\n\n(ii) attend before a specified inspecting officer to answer\nquestions relevant to the inspection; or\n\n(b) if the Ombudsman does not know the officer’s identity—\nrequire the chief officer of the agency, or a person nominated\nby the chief officer, to attend before a specified inspecting\nofficer to answer questions relevant to the inspection.\n\n(2) A requirement under subsection (1) to attend before an inspecting\nofficer must specify:\n\n(a) a place for the attendance; and\n\n(b) a period within which, or a time and day when, the\nattendance is to occur.\nThe place, and the period or the time and day, must be reasonable\nhaving regard to the circumstances in which the requirement is\nmade.\n\n(3) A person must not refuse:\n\n(a) to attend before a person; or\n\n(b) to give information; or\n\n(c) to answer questions;\nwhen required to do so under this section.\n\nChapter 4A  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman\n\nSection 186D\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPenalty for an offence against this subsection:\nImprisonment\nfor 6 months."
    },
