      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.424",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law,\nprevents an officer of an enforcement agency from:\n\n(a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or\nin writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or\n\n(b) giving access to a record of the agency to an inspecting\nofficer;\nfor the purposes of an inspection under this Chapter of the\nagency’s records.\n\nOversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Chapter 4A\n\nSection 186E\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law,\nprevents an officer of an enforcement agency from:\n\n(a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or\nin writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or\n\n(b) giving access to a record of the agency to an inspecting\nofficer;\nfor the purposes of an inspection under this Chapter of the\nagency’s records.\n\nOversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Chapter 4A\n\nSection 186E\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
