    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186d-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "186D(4) Ombudsman to be given information and access despite other",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-186d-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.424",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law,\nprevents an officer of an enforcement agency from making a record\nof information, or causing a record of information to be made, for\nthe purposes of giving the information to a person as permitted by\nsubsection (3).",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law,\nprevents an officer of an enforcement agency from making a record\nof information, or causing a record of information to be made, for\nthe purposes of giving the information to a person as permitted by\nsubsection (3).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186d-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186d-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "43dc319e0b4016a5f25ff8aa3cdfa79c9541ac30c52c3f945101103d4402bcd4",
      "skos:note": "Enforcement agency must provide information to a person upon request.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-186d-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "186D(4) Ombudsman to be given information and access despite other",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 424,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Nothing in section 133, 181A, 181B or 182, or in any other law,\nprevents an officer of an enforcement agency from making a record\nof information, or causing a record of information to be made, for\nthe purposes of giving the information to a person as permitted by\nsubsection (3)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186d-ss-4-norm",
