      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "186E Application of Ombudsman Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-186e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.425",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 11A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 does not apply in\nrelation to the exercise or proposed exercise of a power, or the\nperformance or the proposed performance of a function, of the\nOmbudsman under this Chapter.\n\n(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the\nOmbudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything\nthat an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this\nChapter.\n\n(3) Subject to section 186D of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and\n(8) of the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this\nChapter and so apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer; and\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully accessed information or\nlawfully intercepted information; and\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Chapter; and\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted.\n\nChapter 4A  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman\n\nSection 186F\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 11A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 does not apply in\nrelation to the exercise or proposed exercise of a power, or the\nperformance or the proposed performance of a function, of the\nOmbudsman under this Chapter.\n\n(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the\nOmbudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything\nthat an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this\nChapter.\n\n(3) Subject to section 186D of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and\n(8) of the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this\nChapter and so apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer; and\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully accessed information or\nlawfully intercepted information; and\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Chapter; and\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted.\n\nChapter 4A  Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman\n\nSection 186F\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186e-ss-2"
        },
