      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186h-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If an act is done in good faith, then no liability.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Act done in good faith",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No liability"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186h-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Entails",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If an act is done in good faith, then it entails no liability.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Act done in good faith",
      "cml:conclusionText": "No liability"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "186J Reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979#sec-186j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.428",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman must report to the Minister, in writing, about the\nresults of inspections under section 186B of the records of agencies\nduring a financial year.\n\n(2) The report under subsection (1) must be given to the Minister as\nsoon as practicable after the end of the financial year.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause a copy of the report to be laid before each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe Minister receives it.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may report to the Minister in writing at any time\nabout the results of an inspection under this Chapter and must do\nso if so requested by the Minister.\n\n(5) If, as a result of an inspection under this Chapter of the records of\nan enforcement agency, the Ombudsman is of the opinion that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened a provision of this Act, the\nOmbudsman may include in his or her report on the inspection a\nreport on the contravention.\n\nOversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Chapter 4A\n\nSection 186J\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nIn complying with this section, the Ombudsman remains bound by the\nobligations imposed by sections 133, 181B and 182.\n\n(6) The Ombudsman must give a copy of a report under subsection (1)\nor (4) to the chief officer of any enforcement agency to which the\nreport relates.\n\n(7) A report under this section must not include information which, if\nmade public, could reasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\n\n(c) compromise any enforcement agency’s operational activities\nor methodologies.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Ombudsman must report to the Minister, in writing, about the\nresults of inspections under section 186B of the records of agencies\nduring a financial year.\n\n(2) The report under subsection (1) must be given to the Minister as\nsoon as practicable after the end of the financial year.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause a copy of the report to be laid before each\nHouse of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House after\nthe Minister receives it.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may report to the Minister in writing at any time\nabout the results of an inspection under this Chapter and must do\nso if so requested by the Minister.\n\n(5) If, as a result of an inspection under this Chapter of the records of\nan enforcement agency, the Ombudsman is of the opinion that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened a provision of this Act, the\nOmbudsman may include in his or her report on the inspection a\nreport on the contravention.\n\nOversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Chapter 4A\n\nSection 186J\n\nTelecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nIn complying with this section, the Ombudsman remains bound by the\nobligations imposed by sections 133, 181B and 182.\n\n(6) The Ombudsman must give a copy of a report under subsection (1)\nor (4) to the chief officer of any enforcement agency to which the\nreport relates.\n\n(7) A report under this section must not include information which, if\nmade public, could reasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\n\n(c) compromise any enforcement agency’s operational activities\nor methodologies.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sec-186j-ss-1"
        },
